    "chunk_text": "That means spending the capital budget on time and in full. It means fixing the payment controls that let millions walk out of the Treasury, giving the families rebuilding after Ditwah an account of where the money went, and putting jobs for the young at the centre of the 2027 Budget.\n\n(The author is a former COO of the Public-Private Partnership unit of the Finance Minister, an ex-banker and educationist)\n\nThe 2027 Budget, due in November, is the moment to set the targets. Each one below can be measured, and each should be reported in public every month.\n\nTreasury: spend at least 90% of the capital budget, half of it by the end of June. Publish spending by ministry every month.\n\nHealth: complete at least 10 of the 25 stalled hospital projects, and cut the shortfall of 1,100 specialists by a quarter.\n\nAgriculture: return rice output to its 2025 level with no emergency imports of the staple, and deliver fertiliser to farmers before each season begins.\n\nEnergy: legislate a strategic fuel reserve, starting with 30 days of stock by the end of 2027 on the way to the 90-day international norm.\n\nJobs and investment: realise $ 1.5 billion of FDI and bring unemployment among 25- to 29-year-olds back below 10%.\n\nDitwah recovery: publish quarterly progress on every one of the 1,028 recovery projects, with money spent against money approved.\n\nScenario planning: publish, with the Budget, what happens to fuel, the rupee and the deficit if oil reaches $ 100 or $ 130, and the contingency plan for each."
