    "chunk_text": "Halal Council wins Gold again, secures double honours at CNCI Achiever Awards 2026\n\nHAC Managing Director Rizvi Zaheed receives the Gold Award from Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Deputy Minister Chathuranga Abeysinghe. Others from left: HAC CEO Aakif, Director, CNCI Past Chairman Kevin Edwards, CNCI Chairman Pradeep Kahwalage, HAC Head of Quality Nafas\n\nHAC Chairman Dr. Admani Haroon receives the Top Achievers Award from CNCI Past Chairman Tissa Seneviratne. Others from left: CNCI Past Chairman Ruwan Edirisinghe, CNCI Member of the Internal Panel of Judges Ravi Rupasinghe, and Sri Lanka Institute of Nanotechnology CEO Ilmi Hewajulige\n\nFrom Silver in 2024 to Gold and Top Achievers Awards in both 2025 and 2026, HAC celebrates three consecutive years of national recognition for excellence\n\nThe Halal Assessment Council (Guarantee) Ltd., (HAC) has once again secured the prestigious Gold Award and Top Achievers Award at the 25th CNCI Achiever Awards 2026 for Industrial Excellence, organised by the Ceylon National Chamber of Industries (CNCI) in collaboration with the Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Ministry.\n\nThis latest achievement marks HAC\u2019s second consecutive year of winning both honours, building on its Silver Award in 2024 and demonstrating a consistent track record of excellence in Sri Lanka\u2019s services sector.\n\nCelebrating its 25th anniversary, the CNCI Achiever Awards recognise outstanding Sri Lankan enterprises for excellence in business performance, innovation, quality, productivity and sustainable growth.\n\nCommenting on the achievement, HAC Director and CEO Aakif A. Wahab stated: \u201cThese awards are more than recognition of our achievements. They reflect the dedication of our team and the trust placed in us by Sri Lankan businesses and consumers. Our commitment is to ensure that credible Halal certification not only builds consumer confidence but also helps Sri Lankan products compete and succeed in domestic and international markets.\u201d"
