    "chunk_text": "Panelists at Connect 2026 Jakarta examined why Sri Lanka is an ideal destination for foreign direct investment, including government incentives and policy support, ease of doing business, opportunities within landmark national development projects, and Public-Private Partnership opportunities. Priority sectors showcased included: Real Estate Development; Logistics and Supply Chain; Maritime and Port-related Industries; Textile and Apparel and Pharmaceuticals and Healthcare Manufacturing.\n\nThe second panel turned to Indonesia as one of Asia\u2019s fastest-growing investment destinations, supported by strong economic fundamentals, a large consumer market, progressive investment reforms and significant downstream industrial development. Discussion covered the current status of Sri Lankan investment in Indonesia, the country\u2019s evolving investment landscape, priority sectors for foreign investors, and institutional cooperation to further strengthen bilateral investment relations.\n\nPanellists included Danantara Chief Economist/Managing Director Reza Siregar, Hayleys Aventura Managing Director Dr Wasaba Jayasekara, MAS Holdings\u2019 Silueta Ltd., CEO Ruwan Keragala, and KADIN (Indonesian Chamber of Commerce and Industry). The session was moderated by CIMA Global Learning Partner Akalangka De Zoysa.\n\nThe forum drew representatives of Indonesian conglomerates, chambers and business associations, Indonesian Government officials, Honorary Consuls of Sri Lanka and their delegations, representatives of Sri Lankan companies operating in Indonesia, media and social media influencers, and a Sri Lankan delegation including members of the Ceylon Chamber of Commerce.\u00a0 \u00a0The BOI will continue to engage with Indonesian investors who expressed interest during the forum, in collaboration with the Embassy of Sri Lanka in Jakarta."
