    "chunk_text": "The Sri Lankan delegation was led by Trade, Commerce, Food Security and Cooperative Development Minister Wasantha Samarasinghe. Other members included Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Ministry Secretary Thilaka Jayasundara, EDB Chairman and Chief Executive Officer Mangala Wijesinghe, and the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka (BOI) Executive Director.\n\nAddressing the forum, Minister Samarasinghe highlighted Sri Lanka\u2019s economic recovery, noting that the economy recorded growth of 5% in both 2024 and 2025.\n\nIndustry and Entrepreneurship Development Ministry Secretary Jayasundara, outlined the progress made in restoring economic stability and strengthening investor confidence. She noted that Sri Lanka recorded economic growth of 5%, while the industrial sector expanded by 7.8% in 2025. She also highlighted improvements in the country\u2019s fiscal position, including a Budget deficit equivalent to 2.3% of gross domestic product (GDP) and a declining debt ratio.\n\nJayasundara further stated that foreign direct investment (FDI) exceeded $ 1 billion in 2025, representing an increase of 72%. These developments, she noted, demonstrated the opportunities available to investors seeking to establish or expand their presence in Sri Lanka.\n\nDelivering the welcome address, High Commissioner of Sri Lanka to the UK Senadheera, highlighted the longstanding trade relationship between the two countries. He also drew attention to the opportunities available to Sri Lankan exporters under the UK\u2019s Developing Countries Trading Scheme (DCTS), which provides preferential market access for eligible exports.\n\nEDB Chairman Wijesinghe, outlined Sri Lanka\u2019s export potential in the UK market, highlighting the strengths of the country\u2019s products and services across key sectors. He emphasised Sri Lanka\u2019s competitiveness as a sourcing destination, supported by sustainable manufacturing practices, authentic products and compliance with international quality standards."
