    "md5": "a4fa649623ba3e3324b23630a1fa64ca",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 700,
    "chunk_text": "Govt aims to return State-held lands in North by year-end: Minister\n\nEnvironment Minister Dhammika Patabendi told Parliament today that the Government is aiming to release as much State-held land in the Northern Province as possible before the end of this year.\n\nHe said a Cabinet-appointed committee had identified lands currently held by the State and that steps would be taken to release those that could be handed over before the year-end.\n\nThe Minister said the process had been delayed due to a lack of cooperation from certain State institutions in some districts.\n\nHe also stressed that unauthorised construction or land clearing would not be permitted on lands currently under State control."
