    "chunk_size_bytes": 2013,
    "chunk_text": "Speaking to Mirror Business, Hayleys Fentons Managing Director Hasith Prematillake said the entry into the two-wheeler market of Sri Lanka marks an important step in broadening the company\u2019s portfolio and reaching new customer segments. \u201cCFMOTO is not for the mass market. It\u2019s a bike for the niche market consisting Gen-Z and tech-savvy urban riders, focusing on connected, sustainable, and high-performance city commuting. It\u2019s not a market that existed in Sri Lanka. What was available here was a market for used, reconditioned Japanese bikes in the 300cc - 450cc range. With our entry, we have created a market for brand new CFMOTO bikes, and we don\u2019t see any competition.\u201d\n\nPrematillake also noted that they got a dominant international partner to enter the two-wheel segment. \u201cHeadquartered in Hangzhou, China, CFMOTO has built a robust market share in over 100 countries and regions, and has branches in Europe, United States and Thailand. It currently holds a 25 percent market share in the highly competitive 200cc-plus manual/street motorcycle segment in China. The brand has redefined modern riding by blending advanced performance with accessible luxury. Its engineering capabilities are proven at the highest level in international motorsport.\u201d\n\nThe two-wheeler market in Sri Lanka has experienced a massive post-crisis recovery in 2026, driven by normalising supply chains, strong demand for commuter models, and growing interest in electric alternatives.\u00a0 As per Department of Motor Traffic (DMT) statistics, the total number of registered motorcycles (two wheelers) in the country by the end of 2025 has surpassed 5.2 million.\n\nAlongside the opening of CFMOTO flagship showroom in Colombo 10, Hayleys Mobility has officially onboarded 44 authorised dealer partners across Sri Lanka. The network includes dealerships in Mahawewa, Moratuwa, Piliyandala, Dematagoda, Kalutara, Thalawathugoda, Maharagama, Kaduwela, Gampaha and Maradana, supporting the brand\u2019s reach beyond Colombo."
