    "chunk_text": "Nadika Ranasinghe new CFA Society Sri Lanka President\n\nCFA Society Sri Lanka, part of the global network of CFA Institute member societies dedicated to advancing the investment profession, announced the appointment of Nadika Ranasinghe, CFA, as its new President, following the society\u2019s Annual General Meeting held on October 30, 2026, in Colombo.\n\nA seasoned financial services professional with over two decades of experience spanning capital markets, investment research, credit ratings, corporate strategy and investment banking, Nadika brings extensive industry expertise and a strong record of leadership and service to the society.\n\nNadika obtained her CFA Charter in 2008 and has been actively involved with CFA Society Sri Lanka for the past 18 years, serving in several key leadership capacities, including as a board member, Treasurer and Vice President.\n\nShe has also chaired key society initiatives, including the Scholarship Committee and Capital Market Awards in 2022 and 2023, the society\u2019s flagship event recognising excellence in Sri Lanka\u2019s capital markets.\n\nThrough her long-standing involvement, Nadika has contributed significantly towards strengthening member engagement, promoting professional excellence and supporting the development of Sri Lanka\u2019s investment profession.\n\nNadika said, \u201cI am honoured to assume the leadership of CFA Society Sri Lanka, an institution that has played a pivotal role in shaping my professional journey. As the financial services industry continues to evolve, the society\u2019s mission of promoting ethical conduct, professional excellence and lifelong learning remains more important than ever. I look forward to working closely with our members, volunteers and stakeholders to further strengthen the investment profession and contribute to the continued development of Sri Lanka\u2019s capital markets.\u201d"
  },
