    "md5": "cdb25254ec22f548224390ece7985f32",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1767,
    "chunk_text": "The healthcare revenue increased 13.3 percent to Rs.19.6 billion over the six months, although its operating margin declined to 11.2 percent, from 13.1 percent as the pricing restrictions and higher import costs weighed on the earnings.\n\nLina Manufacturing\u2019s revenue rose 35.1 percent, supported by the deliveries against the government orders. The medical devices revenue increased 19.9 percent, while Healthguard Distribution grew 4.1 percent. the Healthguard Pharmacy revenue remained broadly stable.\n\nThe consumer revenue rose 53.5 percent to Rs.15 billion, with the consolidation of spice exporter JAPC accounting for a substantial part of the increase. Excluding JAPC, the sector revenue grew 13 percent.\n\nThe consumer operating margin edged up to 8 percent, from 7.8 percent. The tea export revenue increased 25.4 percent over the six months, while the branded tea and confectionery revenue grew 5.6 percent and 2.2 percent, respectively. JAPC\u2019s spice export revenue rose 28.6 percent.\n\nThe agribusiness revenue increased 7.2 percent to Rs.5.6 billion, driven by the oil palm operations. The oil palm revenue rose 9.1 percent to Rs.5 billion on higher own-crop production, although the second-quarter growth moderated as the bought-crop availability and oil extraction rates declined.\n\nThe dairy revenue fell 2.9 percent to Rs.561.1 million as the higher selling prices only partly offset the lower milk sales volumes. The agribusiness operating margin narrowed to 47.8 percent, from 49.1 percent, reflecting the higher oil palm operating costs. During the first half, Sunshine finalised a joint venture agreement with India\u2019s Zydus Lifesciences, to develop an oral solid dosage pharmaceutical manufacturing facility at the Horana Export Processing Zone."
