    "chunk_size_bytes": 1961,
    "chunk_text": "Seylan\u2019s quarterly profit tops Rs.3bn\n\nSeylan Bank\u2019s group profit rose 6 percent to Rs.3.08 billion in the September quarter, with an impairment reversal supporting the earnings as the higher funding costs squeezed the interest income growth and the expenses outpaced the revenue.\n\nThe profit attributable to the equity holders increased 6.2 percent to Rs.3.07 billion, from Rs.2.89 billion a year earlier, while the earnings per share improved to Rs.4.82, from Rs.4.54.\n\nThe group recorded an impairment reversal of Rs.965.3 million, against a charge of Rs.226.7 million in the corresponding quarter, delivering a favourable year-on-year swing of nearly Rs.1.2 billion.\n\nThis helped offset the pressure on the operating performance. The group operating income was virtually unchanged at Rs.11.82 billion, while the operating expenses rose 12.2 percent to Rs.6.32 billion. The operating profit before impairment and taxes consequently fell about 11 percent to Rs.5.50 billion.\n\nAt bank level, the quarterly profit after tax increased 6.95 percent to Rs.3.04 billion, while the profit before income tax grew 8.74 percent to Rs.4.75 billion. The interest income rose 21.7 percent to Rs.25.12 billion but the interest expenses increased at a faster 39.5 percent to Rs.15.83 billion. Consequently, the quarterly net interest income edged down to Rs.9.29 billion, from Rs.9.30 billion. The fee income provided support, with the net fee and commission income increasing 13.5 percent to Rs.2.46 billion.\n\nThe bank reported a net trading loss of Rs.2.31 billion for the quarter, compared with a loss of Rs.97.6 million a year earlier. The net other operating income increased to Rs.2.26 billion, from Rs.295.5 million, substantially offsetting the trading loss.\n\nTotal bank operating income grew just 0.26 percent to Rs.11.71 billion, while the operating expenses rose 12.2 percent to Rs.6.27 billion. The personnel expenses increased 13 percent to Rs.3.33 billion."
