    "md5": "e91d5f7af84b2e04e4dd9e904e9f4998",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1984,
    "chunk_text": "CAL to acquire 51% of Hong Kong fund manager AFC\n\nCapital Alliance Holdings PLC (CAL) has signed an agreement to acquire a controlling 51 percent stake in Hong Kong-based Asia Frontier Capital Ltd (AFC), extending its fund management business into additional frontier markets.\n\nThe proposed acquisition, through wholly- owned Singapore subsidiary CAL Global Pte. Ltd, remains subject to regulatory approvals, including clearance from Hong Kong\u2019s Securities and Futures Commission. The announcement did not disclose the purchase price or an expected\u00a0completion date.\n\nAFC manages more than US $ 125 million for investors across Europe, Asia and North America. Its funds include the multi-country AFC Asia Frontier Fund and dedicated strategies investing in Vietnam, Iraq and Uzbekistan.\n\nThe transaction would connect CAL\u2019s operations in Sri Lanka, Bangladesh and Singapore, with AFC\u2019s Hong Kong investment platform and teams in Vietnam, Uzbekistan and Iraq. It would also broaden CAL\u2019s access to international investors and expand its investment offering beyond its\u00a0existing markets.\n\n\u201cFrontier markets offer some of the most compelling growth stories in the world; yet, they remain hard for international investors to reach,\u201d CAL Group CEO Kanishke Mannakkara said.\n\n\u201cIt also takes us into three more frontier markets, giving us a platform to build a deeper presence there over time and into Hong Kong, one of the world\u2019s most important financial hubs.\u201d\n\nFounded in 2013 by Thomas Hugger, AFC has also been a long-standing investor in Sri Lankan and Bangladeshi equities.\n\nAFC founder and CEO Hugger said the partnership would preserve the firm\u2019s investment approach and decision-making independence while strengthening its research, technology, compliance and operating capabilities.\n\n\u201cOur investors will continue to benefit from the same approach to managing their money, with the same team, investment process and independence in our decisions,\u201d he said."
