    "chunk_size_bytes": 968,
    "chunk_text": "Experience has shown that a change of faces alone cannot deliver good governance while the structures of power remain poorly restrained. The task is to build a constitutional order that protects democratic freedoms, strengthens institutional accountability and leaves future generations a country governed by principles rather than by the unchecked authority of individuals.\n\nThe National People\u2019s Power must honour its manifesto pledge to introduce such a Constitution. This is a responsibility owed to the people, not merely an election promise.\n\nMore than a decade after Sobitha Thero\u2019s call, the question he raised remains unanswered. The Executive Presidency was built on the promise that a strong hand would take the decisions a legislature could not. Nearly half a century on, the country has had ample time to weigh that promise against its cost. The materials are at hand and the warnings are on record. What remains is the will to finish what 2015 began."
