    "md5": "cbc42c22dc89f65b1a338bc09afa9d4f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1718,
    "chunk_text": "Israel and its little empire in turmoil: Deadlocked elections  leave Israel facing  possible civil strife\n\nno Israeli party has received sufficient numbers to form a government (photo courtesy AFP)\n\nLet me explain --\u00a0 else,\u00a0 we may have the non-resident Israeli Ambassador based in New Delhi together with his boss, the US Ambassador in Colombo, rushing into our news office taking umbrage at our headline and accusing us of \u2018fake news\u2019. But that in fact, is the reality facing Israeli society today.\n\nIsrael\u2019s empire consists of the Palestinian territories, which they control with great brutality, having imposed a system of apartheid on its occupants. In addition,\u00a0 basics such as drinking water are controlled. Building of houses is also under the control of the occupiers. Travel is restricted, and particular roads blocked with no rhyme or reason.\n\nSince Israel commenced its war on unarmed Palestinian civilians in October 2023,\u00a0 over 75,000 Palestinians have been killed \u2013this excludes the thousands still buried under the rubble, or missing. In\u00a0 June 2026,\u00a0 a UN Independent International Commission of Inquiry reported Israeli forces had killed approximately 20,000 children and injured 44,000 more.\n\nThe Palestinian city of Gaza has been reduced to rubble. According to the World Health Organisation (WHO) and the UN Office for the Co-ordination of Humanitarian Affairs (OCHA), 34 out of 36 hospitals (94%) in the Gaza Strip have been damaged. Roughly half\u00a0 the health facilities are either partially functioning or completely out of service.\n\nUNICEF reported that nearly 97% to 98% of school buildings and all universities in the Gaza Strip have been damaged or destroyed since October 2023."
