    "chunk_size_bytes": 1774,
    "chunk_text": "Benjamin Netanyahu, the outgoing Prime Minister,\u00a0 and his extreme right-wing colleagues in the out-going regime have won 53 seats in the Knesset. The opposition faction, also a coalition of parties led by Gadi Eisenkot\u2019s \u2018Yashar Party\u2019, won a total of 48 seats. The Palestinian-Israeli Parties (two Arab-majority lists, the Joint List and Ra\u2019am) who form around 20% or more of Israel\u2019s population won 19 seats.\n\nYet, to form a government, one or the other Israeli parties need at the least 61 seats in the Knesset to form a government\u2026 and therein lies the problem for both Netanyahu and Eisenkot.\n\nAs it is, Netanyahu will remain caretaker-prime minister until the stalemate ends. His Likud party and its partners in coalition won the largest number of seats in the Knesset, but lost their majority. On their own,\u00a0 they cannot form a government. Netanyahu\u2019s main rival \u2013\u00a0 Eisenkot - does not have sufficient seats to replace him.\n\nEisenkot has ruled out joining with Natanyahu\u2019s coalition as long as he is linked with either Ben Gavir\u2019s \u2018Jewish Power\u2019 party or Bezalel Smotrich\u2019s \u2018Religious Zionism\u2019 party. His other option is to join hands with the Palestinian-Arab parties.\u00a0 There is speculation that Eisenkot may come to an understanding with the Israeli-Palestinian group.\u00a0 However, Eisenkot, has set three conditions for any party joining his coalition \u2013\u00a0 accepting Israel as a Jewish and democratic state, the values of the Declaration of Independence, and\u00a0 a duty of service, military or civilian.\n\nHe has since added a fourth condition -the next government\u2019s basic guidelines, he said, will state that whoever does not accept that Hamas is a terrorist organisation that must be dismantled, cannot be a partner in government."
