    "chunk_text": "He has since added a fourth condition -the next government\u2019s basic guidelines, he said, will state that whoever does not accept that Hamas is a terrorist organisation that must be dismantled, cannot be a partner in government.\n\nAlthough Eisenkot is the self-proclaimed \u2018Voice of Change\u2019, he is little different from Netanyahu on continuing the latter\u2019s policy on Gaza, the invasion of Lebanon, Syria or the war in Iran.\u00a0 Again, Eisenkot\u2019s support for continuing attacks on Gaza, his support for the war on Iran and continuing attacks on alleged Iranian/Hamas/Hizbolla camps in Syria, Lebanon, makes such a plan a nonstarter.\n\nOn the other hand,\u00a0 Netanyahu who is facing corruption charges and fighting to remain in power may feel it is to his benefit to end his partnership with Ben Gavir and Smotrich (who together have 13 seats) and join hands with Eisenkot\u2019s group which has won 48 seats in the Knesset.\n\nThe fly in the ointment,\u00a0 however,\u00a0 is whether Gavir will be willing to simply walk away and give up his power and position. Reports from human rights organisations and watchdogs (such as the Association for Civil Rights in Israel or DAWN) note that thousands of private Israeli citizens and settlers have been provided arms and co-opted into a newly formed National Guard which is directly under Gavir\u2019s control.\n\nNumbering around 250,000, these armed civilians are under Gavir\u2019s command. Reports from human rights organisations and watchdogs such as the Association for Civil Rights and DAWN confirm that thousands of private citizens and settlers have received firearms through these programmes,\u00a0 and it is these groups more than the regular army which are carrying out porgroms in the West Bank."
