    "chunk_size_bytes": 1985,
    "chunk_text": "The motion stresses that the need has arisen to develop a strong legal, social and reconciliation mechanism in order to prevent the recurrence of such racist and crisis-ridden incidents in the future and that it has become essential to take necessary steps to prevent activities that undermine the trust and goodwill existing between different ethnic groups in Sri Lanka\n\nThe motion has come up despite a remark made by Minister of Justice Harshana Nanayakkara during a recent debate in Parliament that it is more appropriate to appoint a select committee to look into national reconciliation rather than focusing on the July 1983 riots alone.\n\nDaily Mirror learnt that a motion can be taken up for debate even if a motion is signed by five members and the Speaker appoints a select committee if its approved by a majority of MPs in Parliament as per the standing orders.\n\nMPs who have signed the motion are Ministers Ramalingam Chandrasekhar, Ananda Wijepala, Deputy Ministers Sunil Watagala, Eranga Gunasekara, Gamagedara Dissanayake, Sugath Thilakaratne, MPs S. Sri Bavanandarajah, Nishantha Perera, K. Ilankumaran, Kanthasamy Prabu, Ravindra Bandara, Fasmin Sharif, Sellaththamby Thilaganathan, Bhagya Sri Herath, R.M. Samantha Ranasinghe, Sanjeewa Ranasingha, Riyas Farook, Sudath Balagalla, E.M. Basnayaka, Thanura Dissanayake, M.A.C.S. Chathuri Gangani, Gayan Janaka, Shantha Pathma Kumara Subasingha, Janitha Ruwan Kodithuwakku, Chaminda Lalith Kumara, Anushka Thilakarathne, Eranga Weeraratne, Muneer Mulaffer, Lasith Bhashana Gamage, Kitnan Selvaraj, Chandana Sooriyaarachchi, Sandaruwan Madarasinghe, Jagath Manuwarna, Deepthi Wasalage, Kanchana Welipitiya, R.G. Wijerathna, Nilanthi Kottahachchi, Muhammad Faizal, Sunil Biyanwila, Chandima Hettiaratchi, Manjula Sugath Rathnayaka, Aruna Panagoda, Susantha Dodawatta, Roshan Akmeemana, U.P. Abeywickrama, Nanda Bandara, Wasantha Pushpa Kumara, Asoka Sapumal Ranwala, Nihal Abeysinghe, Sena Nanayakkara, and Nishantha Perera."
