    "chunk_index": 2,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "5c101634252b2ccfe32823a1b1e64860",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1893,
    "chunk_text": "QYou and most Tamil-speaking writers publish your work in India, yet almost all literary awards in Colombo for the best Tamil literary works only consider books published in Sri Lanka. How do you interpret this issue?\n\nQIn one of your previous media interviews, you mentioned an unstoppable compulsion to write through any hardship. Looking back, has writing been a form of healing for you? And what is the impact of war and state oppression on your creative work?\n\nJust as I could never live in another country outside this land, I cannot live without writing. As Tamils, we have endured severe systemic oppression on our ancestral land. Writing is the medicine that soothes our pain; writing serves justice for our pain. Even today, we suffer from painful memories. Our future generations must live a life of self-respect and equality. We only pick up pens. We hold onto writing. Through writing fiction and non-fiction, we can tell our stories to the Sinhala people and to the world.\n\nQYou have always spoken about the importance of bringing your work to Sinhala readers in the south. Given that you and other Tamil writers constantly face discrimination, do you still have hope that the Sinhala community will empathize with the grievances you address in your poetry and novels?\n\nSurely, we must tell our stories to the Sinhala society. I believe that through our stories, they will certainly understand us. Literature possesses that magnificent power.\n\nSinhala readers who read my novel \u2018Nadugal\u2019 understood with great pain and emotional resonance the feelings of a Tamil mother and a Tamil brother yearning for the memory of a freedom fighter who died in the war. At the same time, ethnic discrimination, oppression, and threats still prevail. I still have strong hope that one day, the Sinhala people will fully understand and acknowledge the political struggle of the Tamil people."
  },
