    "md5": "7bf0e5b2ec536402d00a35c744c7b477",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 835,
    "chunk_text": "Government clarifies TIN requirement\n\nColombo, Nov. 3 (Daily Mirror) - Deputy Minister of Economic Development Nishantha Jayaweera said people could continue their economic activities without a Taxpayer Identification Number (TIN).\n\nAddressing Parliament, he said individuals could visit the relevant institutions and carry out their transactions by providing a copy of their National Identity Card, telephone number and email address, if available.\n\nHe stressed that people need not rush to the Department of Inland Revenue to obtain a TIN.\n\nThe Deputy Minister added that the Commissioner General of Inland Revenue would issue a statement clarifying the matter soon.\n\nA large number of people visited the Inland Revenue Department\u2019s (IRD) head office to obtain Taxpayer Identification Numbers (TIN), resulting in severe congestion."
