    "chunk_text": "Oil prices rose more than $1 early on Tuesday amid concerns of risks to energy supplies.\n\nUS West Texas Intermediate crude was up $1.60, at $98.06 \u2060a barrel while Brent crude futures rose $1.84 to $106.61 a barrel by 07:44 GMT.\n\nThe reported US attacks come on the eve of crucial midterm elections in the US, with US President Donald Trump\u2019s Republican Party fighting to keep control of the House of Representatives and the Senate.\n\nThey also come amid intensifying diplomatic efforts to prevent renewed US and Israeli attacks on Iran.\n\nTrump, writing on his Truth Social platform on Monday, suggested that a deal with Iran could happen soon.\n\n\u201cOil Prices are dropping like a rock, down almost $10 a Barrel, a record, because people feel that there will not be a War with Iran,\u201d he wrote. \u201cIran wants a settlement, as soon as possible. It could happen!\u201d\n\nEarlier, when asked by reporters if he was considering striking Iran after Tuesday\u2019s midterm elections, Trump replied \u201cno\u201d.\n\nUS Vice President JD Vance, meanwhile, expressed optimism about the negotiations before reports of the strikes emerged, telling reporters on Monday that he had discussed the talks with Trump earlier in the day.\n\n\u201cWe\u2019ve had a number of good conversations with the Iranians,\u201d he said when asked about a letter he sent last week to Iran\u2019s security chief, Mohsen Rezaei. \u201cThe president and I both feel pretty good about the prospects for potentially coming to a negotiated settlement. We\u2019re going to keep on working at it.\u201d\n\nIranian Foreign Ministry spokesperson Esmaeil Baghaei said Tehran\u2019s demands for peace had been clearly communicated to Washington and \u201cthe ball is in the US court\u201d.\n\nHe said Iran\u2019s proposed plan to reopen the Strait of Hormuz had been condensed and could be implemented within two days if Washington met Tehran\u2019s conditions. These included the US lifting its naval blockade of Iranian ports and securing an end to hostilities, paving the way for the reopening of the strait and renewed negotiations."
