    "chunk_size_bytes": 1774,
    "chunk_text": "Govt. defends SLTPB-funded Rs. 104 m sponsorship for ABU assembly\n\nCabinet Spokesman Dr. Nalinda Jayatissa clarifies sponsorship was channelled via SLTPB, as part of its mandate to promote the country internationally\n\nSLTPB expects to generate Rs. 250 m in media value; says funding came from tourism-related levies, not a direct Treasury allocation\n\nNotes international exposure to position Sri Lanka for leisure, conferences and major events\n\nThe Government yesterday defended its decision to provide over Rs. 104 million in sponsorship for the 63rd Asian Broadcasting Union (ABU) General Assembly in Colombo, citing its potential to generate international publicity and strengthen Sri Lanka\u2019s positioning as a tourism and MICE destination.\n\nCabinet Spokesman and Minister Dr. Nalinda Jayatissa clarified that the sponsorship was channelled through the Sri Lanka Tourism Promotion Bureau (SLTPB), as part of its mandate to promote the country internationally, and did not constitute a direct allocation from the Treasury.\n\nResponding to questions at the weekly post-Cabinet media briefing, he said the Bureau financed the sponsorship through funds generated from tourism-related levies, stressing that supporting international events with potential tourism promotional benefits fell within its remit.\n\nHe explained that the SLTPB regularly evaluates opportunities to support events and programs capable of strengthening the tourism industry, with sponsorship proposals assessed by its board, which includes representatives from the tourism and hospitality sectors.\n\nOn 2 November, in a media release issued by Sri Lanka Tourism noted that the ABU General Assembly was expected to generate promotional media value exceeding Rs. 250 million through international exposure."
  },
