    "chunk_size_bytes": 1257,
    "chunk_text": "On 2 November, in a media release issued by Sri Lanka Tourism noted that the ABU General Assembly was expected to generate promotional media value exceeding Rs. 250 million through international exposure.\n\nThe Spokesperson, who is also the Mass Media Minister clarified that the selection of MTV Channel Ltd., as the host broadcaster was made by the ABU and not by the Government.\n\nThe Colombo gathering brought together around 350 international delegates representing leading media organisations, providing Sri Lanka with an opportunity to showcase its tourism attractions and enhance its international visibility.\n\nAccording to Dr. Jayatissa, the ABU has around 225 member organisations across 66 countries, making the assembly a significant international platform for exposure.\n\nIn addition, queries were also raised over the approval process, including whether the sponsorship proposal had initially been declined by the SLTPB and the rationale for seeking Cabinet approval.\n\nDr. Jayatissa said Cabinet approval was required given the value of the sponsorship, while reiterating that the SLTPB had the authority to assess and support tourism promotion opportunities.\n\nThe 63rd ABU General Assembly was held in Colombo from 30 October to 3 November 2026."
