    "md5": "5114a976ffedb923375416596d9abdde",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1086,
    "chunk_text": "EU to provide \u20ac 10 m grant for sustainable trade project\n\nThe Cabinet of Ministers has approved signing a Financial Grant Agreement between the Government and the European Union (EU) to secure \u20ac 10 million funding to implement a four-year project, aimed at strengthening sustainable trade relations between Sri Lanka and the EU.\n\nAddressing the weekly post-Cabinet media briefing, Cabinet Spokesman and Minister Dr. Nalinda Jayatissa said the EU had agreed to support the initiative, which seeks to promote green transition initiatives and climate-resilient trade practices.\n\nThe project will also focus on strengthening trade-related institutional capacities and supporting Sri Lanka\u2019s efforts to comply with international standards required to access the EU market.\n\n\u201cThe Trade, Commerce, Food Security and Cooperative Development Ministry is expected to implement the project over a period of four years,\u201d he added.\n\nThe proposal to this effect was submitted by President Anura Kumara Dissanayake, in his capacity as the Finance, Planning and Economic Development Minister."
