    "md5": "8a0011c84a6ac0cc4bf5e1f1218ea48b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1903,
    "chunk_text": "LAUGFS Gas outlines Nov., shipment plans and measures to restore LPG supplies\n\nLAUGFS Gas PLC yesterday said it has arranged three LPG shipments expected to arrive in Sri Lanka this month and is working with the relevant authorities to secure approvals for domestic supplies through its Hambantota terminal.\n\nThe company said it sincerely regrets the hardship caused to households and businesses by the current supply disruptions. \u201cAs a Sri Lankan company serving the domestic LPG market for more than 25 years, LAUGFS remains committed to restoring availability and strengthening long-term supply reliability,\u201d it said.\n\nThese dates remain subject to shipping arrangements, port operations and applicable regulatory approvals. Domestic releases from the Hambantota shipments require the necessary authorisations. Distribution is expected to resume progressively following receipt and clearance of the cargoes.\n\nConflict in the Middle East and disruptions to maritime transport through the Strait of Hormuz have affected international LPG supply chains, creating procurement and shipping difficulties for Sri Lanka and other importing countries.\n\nTo strengthen Sri Lanka\u2019s LPG supply security and support regional trade, LAUGFS Terminals Limited (LTL), a wholly owned subsidiary of LAUGFS Gas PLC, invested $ 65 million in its Hambantota import and export terminal, which commenced operations in 2019. With 30,000 metric tonnes of storage capacity, it is Sri Lanka\u2019s largest LPG receiving, storage and entrep\u00f4t terminal.\n\nThe project received capital goods import-duty concessions under the Board of Investment\u2019s Commercial Hub framework, subject to the applicable conditions. Under the relevant Hub Regulations, domestic releases are linked to 40% of annual re-export turnover by value. This is an export-linked operating condition, not a restriction on LAUGFS Gas\u2019s domestic market share."
  },
