    "chunk_text": "The project received capital goods import-duty concessions under the Board of Investment\u2019s Commercial Hub framework, subject to the applicable conditions. Under the relevant Hub Regulations, domestic releases are linked to 40% of annual re-export turnover by value. This is an export-linked operating condition, not a restriction on LAUGFS Gas\u2019s domestic market share.\n\nTemporary permission previously granted by the Finance Ministry under Emergency Regulations ceased when those regulations ended.\n\nLTL has requested three months of temporary permission to use the Hambantota terminal for domestic LPG supply. In parallel, the company is working with the BOI, Finance Ministry, Sri Lanka Customs and the Department of Imports and Exports Control to complete its transition out of hub status and establish the necessary operating arrangements, with applicable duties and taxes payable.\n\nThe BOI Chairman confirmed to the company yesterday that, following instructions from the President, he had written to the Treasury Secretary requesting that the necessary approvals be facilitated within one week. These approvals remain pending. LAUGFS appreciates the Government\u2019s intervention and the cooperation of the relevant authorities.\n\nAs an additional supply safeguard, LAUGFS Gas has also called a new tender for direct LPG deliveries to Colombo commencing in January 2027.\n\nLAUGFS Gas PLC and LAUGFS Terminals Ltd., are not itself entities designated by the US Department of the Treasury\u2019s Office of Foreign Asset Control (OFAC). The company remains committed to applicable regulatory and compliance requirements and to maintaining transparency with its stakeholders.\n\nLAUGFS Gas PLC appreciates its customers and business partners for their patience and will provide further updates as shipment arrivals and regulatory approvals are confirmed, the company said."
