    "md5": "f05a8a3d7eb8914040ee3b74dffaa686",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1561,
    "chunk_text": "New Asia Forum 2026 targets $ 30 b in  investment mobilisation\n\nThe New Asia Forum (NAF) 2026 aims to mobilise $ 30 billion in investment across the New Asia region by strengthening strategic partnerships and accelerating investment execution.\n\nHeld under the patronage of President Prabowo Subianto, with Danantara Indonesia as a founding partner, the forum will take place on 3\u20134 December 2026 in Bali, Indonesia.\n\nNAF 2026 is designed as an action-oriented platform connecting global investors, industry leaders, and policymakers to advance investment opportunities across strategic sectors. Moving beyond conventional economic dialogue, the forum seeks to translate investment interest into concrete commitments, financing structures, and measurable outcomes.\n\nDanantara Indonesia, Global Relations and Communications Managing Director Pahala Nugraha Mansury emphasised Asia\u2019s growing potential to attract long-term global capital amid shifting economic and geopolitical dynamics.\n\n\u201cOur focus is on encouraging long-term capital to recognise the many investment opportunities across Asian countries, because this is precisely where the centre of gravity for growth lies. This will enable growth at scale, anchored by ASEAN and driven by Indonesia as the largest country in ASEAN,\u201d said Pahala.\n\nThe Asia-Pacific region currently accounts for nearly 60% of global economic growth. However, long-term international capital allocation to the region remains below its potential, presenting significant opportunities for greater investment collaboration."
  },
