    "chunk_text": "The Asia-Pacific region currently accounts for nearly 60% of global economic growth. However, long-term international capital allocation to the region remains below its potential, presenting significant opportunities for greater investment collaboration.\n\nThe forum will follow a two-day structure: Discovery and Diligence on 3 December, focusing on investment opportunities, feasibility, and transaction structures; and Action and Execution on 4 December, advancing capital commitments, strategic partnerships, and implementation milestones.\n\nEight priority sectors will anchor the discussions: strategic resources and downstreaming; energy and power; advanced mobility and manufacturing; digital infrastructure and AI; food and agribusiness; trade and connectivity; tourism and creative economy; and education and human capital.\n\nAs a founding partner, Danantara Indonesia will participate as a co-investor alongside global partners, supporting investment in strategic sectors and reinforcing Indonesia\u2019s role in regional economic transformation.\n\nThrough its transaction-focused approach, NAF 2026 aims to deliver preliminary investment agreements, bankable financing structures, and clearly defined implementation milestones. Investment commitments and progress will be tracked across subsequent editions to promote accountability, continuity, and tangible economic impact for Indonesia and the wider region."
