    "chunk_index": 5,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "3ee2996c1e80cca1773b89654a48a8c3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1664,
    "chunk_text": "Another concern was the relaxation of height restrictions that had traditionally limited construction in coastal areas to the height of a coconut tree. Sri Lanka subsequently saw the growth of apartment developments on beachfront properties, marketed for short-term tourist accommodation.\n\nThe Government\u2019s responsibility is not simply to permit any construction. It is to ensure that development decisions collectively strengthen the destination through proper zoning laws.\n\nSuch poor policy choices help explain why I believe Sri Lanka has not moved up the tourism value chain. More than 20 years ago, the Maldives attracted international luxury resort investments, at times costing USD 1 million per key, capable of commanding very high rates. Properties associated with brands such as One&Only, Cheval Blanc and Four Seasons helped establish the Maldives\u2019 reputation in the luxury market.\n\nLocal brands such as Per Aquum evolved by piggy-backing on high-end international brands. While Sri Lanka has well-established local hospitality brands, we should ask why the country has not attracted a larger portfolio of internationally branded resorts, particularly at the upper end of the market.\n\nOnly around 6% of Sri Lanka\u2019s graded resort hotel rooms are internationally branded compared to at least 33% in tourism focused countries in Asia such as Maldives, Vietnam and Mauritius.\n\nInternational brands can bring distribution networks, loyalty programmes, global marketing, operating systems and access to customers who might otherwise not consider a destination. They can also help local investors benchmark their products against international standards."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-04-dailyftlk-3902def9",
    "num": "dailyftlk-3902def9",
    "date_str": "2026-11-04",
    "description": "Why Sri Lanka needs serious reset of its tourism strategy",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/opinion/Why-Sri-Lanka-needs-serious-reset-of-its-tourism-strategy/14-799605",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
