    "chunk_size_bytes": 1708,
    "chunk_text": "First, gazette maximum determination periods for every category of investment approval, and attach a rule of deemed approval: if an agency fails to respond within the period, the application is approved unless refused in writing with reasons. A published timeline without consequence is an aspiration. Deemed approval turns it into a commitment. This can be done by regulation under existing investment law within six months.\n\nThird, consolidate expatriate work authorisation into a single permit issued through the BOI Visa Management System and accepted by the Department of Immigration and Emigration, extend the conversion window to six months, and permit conversion after travel. If the citizen\u2019s window is to be generous, let it at least be as generous as the State\u2019s.\n\nFourth, assign every approved project a named senior officer with authority to convene the agencies involved and a duty to report delays each month. Accountability needs a name, not merely an institution.\n\nFifth, publish a live project tracker showing every approved project above a defined threshold, its approval date, its current stage, the responsible agency and the reason for any delay. It will be uncomfortable for a quarter. After that it will be self-correcting, because no agency wishes to be named as the cause of delay.\n\nSixth, complete the Single Window for Investment, for which the Finance Ministry has already called proposals, and make it genuine: one interface and one status tracker covering BOI registration, incorporation, tax registration, environmental clearance, local authority approval and utility connections. A portal that merely forwards applications into the same silences would be worse than none."
