    "chunk_text": "Sixth, complete the Single Window for Investment, for which the Finance Ministry has already called proposals, and make it genuine: one interface and one status tracker covering BOI registration, incorporation, tax registration, environmental clearance, local authority approval and utility connections. A portal that merely forwards applications into the same silences would be worse than none.\n\nTimelines alone will not suffice if the rules themselves can change mid-stream. The scaling back of Port City tax concessions after investors had committed did more damage than any single failed project, because it showed that even our flagship stability zone could alter its own terms. A Cabinet policy statement grandfathering agreed terms, written into the standard BOI agreement, would cost nothing. Neither would a cross-party investment compact committing the principal parties to leave the core framework intact for at least ten years. FDI decisions run on twenty- to thirty-year horizons; ours have rarely survived a change of government.\n\nThis is not a partisan argument. On this question, there should be no sides. Much of the work has already been done: the labour law consolidation has been drafted and agreed at committee, the mediation law is in force, and the single window is in procurement. The scarce resource is not analysis. It is the will to bind the State to the same discipline it has always required of its citizens.\n\nA country that respects its people\u2019s time will find that investors respect it too. Let us put the State on the clock.\n\n(The author is a President\u2019s Counsel and a former Cabinet Minister)"
