    "chunk_text": "C-O-L is the ultimate economic thermometer which measures peoples\u2019 happiness or discontent in any economy or society. Prices of consumables rise and fall depending on the stock of supply available in the market. There is no denying that the current pandemic is the consequence of supply constraints driven by two main forces: wars and climate change. The first is recent and the second is much older. But both are beyond the control of monetary authorities and their pet remedy to bring down C-O-L by monitoring the rate of inflation to counter it by raising interest rate and urging Governments to cut public spending is a futile exercise, which will eventually reduce investment, increase unemployment and worsen poverty level.\n\nThe post-Cold War economic order, hailed by Fukuyama as\u00a0 \u2018The End of History and The\n\nWeaponisation of natural resources and financialisation of the real economy has sacrificed long term economic growth through production of goods and services that promote people\u2019s economic well being but instead is concentrating on short term profits through financial engineering. The market is operating not to satisfy the consumers but to increase the financial returns of corporate shareholders.\u00a0 It is the share market and not the product market that always captures the news headline.\n\nConsumers are not to question how and why but to go and buy, and buy what? Whatever the market dishes out through its aggressive marketing techniques. Hedonistic adaptation of consumer tastes and availability of credit facilities has made consumers and especially the young ones to buy what they do not need with money they do not have, perhaps to keep up with the Joneses or to impress someone whom they do not like. In short, the market creates hedonistic wants and sells them as needs."
