    "chunk_text": "The Rajapaksas always used ethno-religious racism to gain/hold power. Ranil Wickremesinghe and Sajith Premadasa, instead of providing a rational oppositional alternative to the toxic Rajapaksa politics, are making their own efforts to appease extremists. Ranil Wickremesinghe was the prime minister and Sajith Premadasa was a key minister when Galagoda-Atte Gnanasara was sentenced to imprisonment in 2018. They, who had no problem with that sentencing then, are now demanding that Anura Kumara Dissanayake pardon the erring monk immediately. In November 2022, President Wickremesinghe said, \u201cNo one is entitled to special protection just because they are wearing a robe\u201d (Speech in Parliament - 29 November 2022 https://dbsjeyaraj.com/dbsj/?p=80449). Today former President Wickremesinghe is demanding that all robe-wearers be accorded special protection.\n\nBut to succeed in their combined and separate power projects, lay and robe-wearing politicians need a minority enemy. The JHU rode to parliament on an anti-Christian wave targeting non-Buddhist Sinhalese. The JHU also played an enabling role in the Galagoda-Atte Gnanasara led campaign to create the Muslim enemy in 2012/13. If neither enemy can be resurrected, an effort can be made to revive the Tiger and the Tamil enemy. Udaya Gammanpila has already accused the Government of allowing a Siva Kovil to be built in the Anuradhapura sacred city. A Siva Kovil was indeed built in Anuradhapura, not in 21CE but in 10CE - over 2 millennia ago (https://amazinglanka.com/wp/anuradhapura-siva-kovil/#google_vignette). But to rile up Sinhala-Buddhist fear and anger, any lie, however outrageous would do.\n\nIf the SJB and the UNP fail to oppose the Government on rational, economic, lines, they will soon be overtaken by the Rajapaksas and the robe-wearers who dream of becoming organ-grinders even as they continue to play the customary role of incendiary monkeys."
