    "md5": "38f587ebdd2f65b41c7385838702eacc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1086,
    "chunk_text": "The Government should consider targeted incentives for genuine export manufacturers. These could include tax relief linked to retaining and creating jobs, investing in machinery, training workers and increasing exports. Support must have clear conditions and measurable results.\n\nTransport operators, food suppliers, maintenance services, small businesses and entire communities depend on the industry. Sri Lanka cannot take this industry for granted when foreign exchange and employment remain essential to economic recovery. Its success was built through years of hard work and trust. That trust must be protected.\n\nThe Government must stop treating apparel as a success that will look after itself. It must listen to manufacturers, workers and exporters, identify why production is moving and act. The objective is not to enrich companies at workers\u2019 expense. It is to keep businesses profitable, workers earning a decent living and export earnings in the country.\n\nSri Lanka cannot keep talking about creating jobs while allowing the factories that provide them to look elsewhere."
