    "chunk_text": "The absurdities in the POC are largely due to it having apparently been implanted from\u00a0 El Salvador and Singapore. El Salvador has, until recently, been beset with organised transnational criminal gangs such as MS-13, which originated among Salvadoran migrant youth in Los Angeles in the 1980s, and Barrio 18 and many other small gangs. Those gangs possessed quasi-military capabilities and entrapped the state. It took Nayib Bukele, the president, to lock up 2 per cent of the adult population to rid the country of gangs.\n\nSri Lanka needs both bills, but they should come with adequate safeguards and common sense.\n\nCorrection: In my last week\u2019s column, \u201c China SEO exit from Colombo logistics Hub:\u00a0 why are investors fleeing,\u201d I inadvertently mentioned the recent exit of China Merchants Holdings from a\u00a0 $392 million logistics hub as from the Colombo Port City. It should be corrected as Colombo Port. The South Asia Commercial and Logistics Hub (SACHL) is a joint venture between China Merchants, Sri Lanka Port Authority and\u00a0 Access Engineering PLC in the Port of Colombo and was not a Port City Project.\u00a0 My apologies.\n\nMatter of factly, the\u00a0 Port City projects that had recently been abandoned include, Asiri Hospital, Universal Entertainment Colombo, Clothespin Management and Development and Gateway Education facility. Active projects include: Colombo International Financial Centre, The Marina Hotel & Yacht Marina, Prime Melwa Marina-Front Development, Downtown Duty-Free Mall and ICC Port City Residential Towers."
