    "chunk_size_bytes": 1602,
    "chunk_text": "Democrats win the U.S. House and take unified control of Congress\n\nMPRnews - Democrats have won control of the U.S. House in addition to the U.S. Senate, delivering a shockingly decisive rebuke of Republican governance in Washington and ushering in a new era of congressional resistance to President Donald Trump.\n\nThe midterm elections that came to a close Tuesday channeled voters' deep frustrations over high prices, the Iran war and concerns over government corruption. Democrats routed their rivals across the map, from Texas to Iowa to New Hampshire, including states Trump won by double digits just two years ago.\n\nEven Republican Sen. Susan Collins of Maine, a battle-tested survivor of difficult elections, lost to Democrat Troy Jackson.\n\nThe results from across the country were a major blow to Trump, who spent nearly every day of the last month holding rallies to energize his supporters but was unable to stop a wipeout.\n\nDemocratic control will profoundly reshape Trump\u2019s final two years in office and likely hamstring his agenda.\n\nParty leaders have signaled they'll use a foothold in Congress to ensure Trump's final two years in office feature a series of investigations against top members of his administration and deeper scrutiny of how he's enriched his family. Impeachment of Trump and his Cabinet officials is not off the table.\n\nIn celebratory events Tuesday night, Democratic Senate Leader Chuck Schumer called it a \u201cgenerational remake of the Senate map.\u201d Democratic House Leader Hakeem Jeffries said \u201cthe American people are crying out for transformational change.\u201d"
