    "chunk_text": "In celebratory events Tuesday night, Democratic Senate Leader Chuck Schumer called it a \u201cgenerational remake of the Senate map.\u201d Democratic House Leader Hakeem Jeffries said \u201cthe American people are crying out for transformational change.\u201d\n\nIn a late-night phone interview with Fox News, Trump said he didn't consider the elections to be a personal defeat. Voters, he said, \u201cdidn't like the candidates.\u201d\n\nDemocrats had braced for Trump to again try to undermine the results if they won after he warned that noncitizens would cast ballots en masse and filed lawsuits in Alaska and California. Instead, he said on Fox that he would accept them.\n\nStill, the Republican-controlled Congress had acted as a rubber stamp to much of Trump's agenda. While the president has proven adept at steamrolling efforts to rein him in, Democrats will seek to reshape the remainder of his term. Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth and tech titan Elon Musk, a former top Trump adviser, are among possible targets for investigations.\n\nDespite the results, Senate Majority Leader John Thune wrote on X that \u201cSenate Republicans will not stand idly by as the far-left, socialist wing of the Democrat Party attempts to unwind everything we\u2019ve done.\u201d He said they will work with Trump \u201cto stop the worst impulses of Democrat extremism.\u201d"
