    "chunk_text": "I\u2019m extremely grateful and heartfelt. Why I started it was a comment I saw on a post. I was holding an alligator at Everglades and there was a comment in Sinhala which said; \u201cI grew up watching Animal Planet or Discovery,\u00a0 and I always see a white man going round the world catching animals. But I never thought our people can do this.\u201d It was very impactful. So I wanted to prove that we too, could do this. You don\u2019t need a million followers to have some impact.\n\nQ : Could you share some unforgettable experiences while in the field?\n\nThe more the number of times I\u2019ve been bitten by animals the more it shows the amount of experience! But there are good scientists who haven\u2019t been bitten by animals. One unforgettable experience was getting bitten by a crocodile in Bangladesh. I had the experience of going to a village hospital, staying overnight, having to go on a push cycle for almost half a day to reach the next town and it was an experience unto itself. It gives you so much insight to life in another country. I\u2019ve had my fair share of animal encounters. Recently we dove in Australia with some tiger sharks. But to be that close to a gigantic animal face to face is very rare. But it also shows that a lot of these things don\u2019t harm you.\n\nQ : With all these experiences, what have the wilds taught you?"
