    "md5": "ae2d915c6044180601c7f8014d7cb7e9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1930,
    "chunk_text": "TikTok removes over 430,000 videos in Sri Lanka in 2Q\n\nTikTok removed more than 430,000 videos in Sri Lanka for violating its community guidelines in the second quarter of 2026, while reporting that nearly 13,000 videos were subsequently restored.\n\nThe platform\u2019s latest Community Guidelines Enforcement Report, covering April to June, recorded 430,357 video removals in Sri Lanka. TikTok said it proactively identified 99.4 percent of those videos before the users reported them.\n\nOf the proactively removed videos, 93.9 percent were taken down within 24 hours of posting, according to the company.\n\nHowever, TikTok also reported that 12,960 videos were restored in Sri Lanka.\n\nThe company supplied no comparison with Sri Lankan removals in the preceding quarter, limiting an assessment of whether enforcement activity increased or declined. It also did not provide a country-level breakdown of violations.\n\nGlobally, TikTok removed 188.3 million videos during the quarter, equivalent to approximately 0.5 percent of all content uploaded to the platform, according to the report.\n\nAutomated detection technologies accounted for 183.3 million of those removals or about 97.4 percent of the total, underscoring the scale of the platform\u2019s reliance on automated moderation. About 6.3 million videos were reinstated globally following further review.\n\nEnforcement also extended to comments and accounts. TikTok removed 278.4 million comments worldwide, up approximately 17.2 percent, from 237.5 million in the first quarter. The increase reflects a higher number of comment removals, although the figures alone do not establish whether the prevalence of rule-breaking content increased.\n\nTikTok also removed 146.8 million fake accounts globally during the quarter, alongside a further 26.8 million accounts suspected of belonging to users under the age of 13. The release did not disclose the corresponding figures for Sri Lanka."
