    "chunk_size_bytes": 1603,
    "chunk_text": "Janashakthi Life among Top 20 Great Workplaces for Young Talent\n\nJanashakthi Life has been recognised among Sri Lanka\u2019s Top 20 Great Workplaces for Young Talent 2026 by Great Place To Work Sri Lanka, reflecting its commitment to creating a workplace where young professionals can learn, contribute and build meaningful careers.\n\nThe endorsement is based on the globally recognised Great Place To Work For All model, which evaluates organisations through its Trust Index Employee Experience Survey and Culture Audit.\n\nThe Trust Index assesses employees\u2019 experiences across areas such as trust, pride and camaraderie, while the Culture Audit evaluates the people practices that support a positive employee experience.\n\nAt Janashakthi Life, the company\u2019s people strategy recognises the diverse needs, expectations and aspirations of different employee segments, with young talent development being one of its key priorities.\n\nThe company focuses on creating a values-driven environment where young professionals are encouraged to share ideas, take ownership and make meaningful contributions.\n\nJanashakthi Life Director and CEO Ravi Liyanage said, \u201cYoung professionals bring fresh perspectives, new ideas and the potential to shape the future of our business. Creating an environment where they can develop their capabilities and take accountability of the organisation\u2019s strategic priorities remains a key pillar of our internal culture. This recognition reflects our commitment to building a workplace where young talent can progress while making impactful contributions to the organisation.\u201d"
