    "md5": "cc027862475a9a41262a3cefb29255ba",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1799,
    "chunk_text": "An inspirational leadership journey at Sri Lanka\u2019s largest bank\n\nBank of Ceylon Chief Executive Officer and General Manager Y.A. Jayathilaka\n\nJourney of Y.A. Jayathilaka - shaped by education, perseverance and a belief in purposeful transformation\n\nThere are journeys that are measured by positions held and milestones achieved. Then there are journeys that carry a deeper meaning, journeys that demonstrate what education, opportunity and perseverance can make possible. The journey of Bank of Ceylon Chief Executive Officer and General Manager Y.A. Jayathilaka belongs to the latter.\n\nFrom a modest classroom in Embilipitiya to the leadership of Sri Lanka\u2019s largest bank, his story is not simply one of professional advancement. It is a reflection of the possibilities created by Sri Lanka\u2019s free education system, the value of determined effort and the importance of remembering the communities and people who shape us along the way.\n\nHis recent return to the two schools that played a defining role in his early life \u2013 Moraketiya Maha Vidyalaya, where he completed his formative schooling and Embilipitiya Central\u2019s College, where he pursued his Advanced Level studies, brought that journey into particularly sharp focus.\n\nThe Upahara ceremonies held in his honour were more than occasions of recognition. They were moments of reconnection with former teachers, classmates, friends and communities, and with the beginnings of a journey that eventually led him to the helm of one of the country\u2019s most important institutions.\n\nReturning to those classrooms as CEO of Bank of Ceylon, however, was not simply a return as a senior corporate leader. It was a return as a former student, one who had once shared the same aspirations, uncertainties and hopes as countless young Sri Lankans."
  },
  {
