    "md5": "3bea7904df39a4ae0d9d5835042c1487",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1966,
    "chunk_text": "Returning to those classrooms as CEO of Bank of Ceylon, however, was not simply a return as a senior corporate leader. It was a return as a former student, one who had once shared the same aspirations, uncertainties and hopes as countless young Sri Lankans.\n\nThat moment captured something fundamental about his journey: success is rarely achieved alone.\n\nHe began his education at Moraketiya Maha Vidyalaya before continuing at Embilipitiya Central College. His academic performance, including achieving second highest in the district, opened the way to university education at the University of Sri Jayewardenepura.\n\nHe subsequently obtained a Bachelor of Science (Special) in Business Administration from the University of Sri Jayewardenepura and a Master of Business (Finance) from the University of Kelaniya.\n\nHis professional education was further strengthened through a Diploma in Banking and Finance, Associate Membership of the Institute of Bankers of Sri Lanka and executive and professional programmes at the Postgraduate Institute of Management-University of Sri Jayewardenepura and Advance Management Programme at INSEAD, France.\n\nFor him, education was never merely a pathway to a qualification. It was an opportunity to broaden horizons.\n\nThat perspective has remained visible throughout his career, particularly in his emphasis on developing people, sharing knowledge and ensuring that technology and innovation create opportunities rather than barriers.\n\nBefore entering banking, Jayathilaka gained corporate experience at John Keells Holdings and Sri Lanka Insurance Corporation. In 1997, he joined Bank of Ceylon as a Management Trainee.\n\nHis early banking experience included service at a rural branch in Bibile, providing first-hand exposure to the realities of grassroots banking and the financial needs of communities outside the major commercial centres.\n\nHis career subsequently expanded across a remarkably broad range of banking functions."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
