    "md5": "79dfd439d26bed5e7dbccb9b808adfe4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1783,
    "chunk_text": "His early banking experience included service at a rural branch in Bibile, providing first-hand exposure to the realities of grassroots banking and the financial needs of communities outside the major commercial centres.\n\nHis career subsequently expanded across a remarkably broad range of banking functions.\n\nHis progression through the bank\u2019s leadership structure was equally gradual. He entered the Executive Management in 2015 through key Assistant General Manager responsibilities and moved into Corporate Management in February 2020, taking on a broader strategic role in the institution.\n\nIn August 2025, he assumed duties as Acting General Manager and Chief Executive Officer of Bank of Ceylon. His appointment was formally confirmed on February 27, 2026 as the bank\u2019s 24th General Manager and Chief Executive Officer.\n\nModern banking is increasingly defined by technology but technology alone does not constitute transformation.\n\nThroughout his career, Jayathilaka has maintained a practical view of innovation: technology must ultimately make banking simpler, more accessible and more useful to people.\n\nHis experience in major technology and transformation initiatives has included core banking systems, trade finance platforms, workflow automation and digital banking solutions. His project management experience at BOC UK Limited also provided exposure to large-scale system implementations and international banking practices.\n\nAt Bank of Ceylon, this philosophy was reflected in initiatives such as BOC Digi Branches, Branch on Wheels, Smart Passbooks and Cardless Withdrawals efforts aimed at taking banking beyond the conventional boundaries and making services more convenient for the customers.\n\nHis focus on innovation also extended to the bank\u2019s employees."
  },
  {
