    "language": "en",
    "md5": "6da8005be6c61cdc3384fba019cecdd0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1982,
    "chunk_text": "At Bank of Ceylon, this philosophy was reflected in initiatives such as BOC Digi Branches, Branch on Wheels, Smart Passbooks and Cardless Withdrawals efforts aimed at taking banking beyond the conventional boundaries and making services more convenient for the customers.\n\nHis focus on innovation also extended to the bank\u2019s employees.\n\nBOC Connect, the agent banking service launched in 2021, sought to take the banking services closer to the communities that traditionally had limited access to conventional banking facilities. Its expansion through the postal network represented another step towards bringing financial services closer to the people.\n\nFurthermore, the expansion of the agent banking services in partnership with the Sri Lanka Post Department was another important step towards bringing the financial services closer to the people. Today, BOC Connect has expanded across all 25 districts, covering 331 Divisional Secretariat Divisions. Through such innovative initiatives, he has been able to respond to the real needs of the people and make banking services more accessible, convenient and inclusive. These initiatives reflect a broader philosophy: innovation is most valuable when it addresses a real need.\n\nJayathilaka\u2019s leadership philosophy has also been shaped by the belief that a bank\u2019s responsibilities extend beyond financial performance.\n\nHis interest in developing communities was equally evident through initiatives such as \u2018Ran Kekulu Chaarika\u2019, which provided the children from rural areas with opportunities to visit Colombo and experience educational and cultural landmarks, including the BOC Currency Museum fully sponsored by the bank.\n\nThe creation of Sri Lanka\u2019s first dedicated agricultural banking arm was another expression of this approach. By developing financial solutions specifically for the farmers and agri-businesses, the initiative sought to connect banking with one of the fundamental sectors of the national economy."
  },
  {
