    "md5": "3b406b7fdf0e8e5836f879a74f6033f6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1158,
    "chunk_text": "That philosophy is increasingly shaping BOC\u2019s future direction, with the bank seeking to combine its traditional strength of trust and accessibility with technology, innovation and a more seamless digital customer experience.\n\nHis association with BOC UK Limited has provided additional international exposure, while his involvement with LankaPay and the CRIB has connected his experience with two important components of Sri Lanka\u2019s financial infrastructure digital payments and credit information.\n\nHe has also contributed to the development of the banking profession through his role on the Governing Board of the Institute of Bankers of Sri Lanka, supporting professional development and the strengthening of banking capabilities.\n\nThese responsibilities illustrate the breadth of his professional journey from rural branch banking to international finance, from customer service to technology and from operational management to institutional governance.\n\nLooking back on Jayathilaka\u2019s journey, perhaps the most enduring lesson is that the greatest measure of success is not simply how far one travels but how much one can contribute along the way."
