    "md5": "db2c1a52004ae0d75900f5446b7b4b9c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1792,
    "chunk_text": "Nestl\u00e9 Golden Chef\u2019s Hat Competition 2026 Recognizes the Best of Sri Lanka\u2019s Culinary Talent\n\nTop three grand winners of the Professional Nestl\u00e9 Golden Chefs\u2019 Hat Competition 2026 receiving awards from the Hon. Vijitha Herath, Minister of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism.\n\nTop three grand winners of the Junior Nestl\u00e9 Golden Chefs\u2019 Hat Competition 2026 receiving awards from the Hon. Vijitha Herath, Minister of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism.\n\nNestl\u00e9 Professional Sri Lanka, in partnership with the Chefs Guild of Lanka and the Sri Lanka Hospitality Graduates Association, concluded the Nestl\u00e9 Golden Chefs\u2019 Hat Competition 2026 with a grand awards ceremony at Cinnamon Life at City of Dreams on 1 November. The Hon. Vijitha Herath, Minister of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism, graced the occasion as Chief Guest.\n\nThe competition was held across two main categories; with the Professional category attracting participants from over 70 leading hotels island-wide, while the Junior category, held in partnership with the Sri Lanka Hospitality Graduates Association, brought together 1,500 hotel school students from 13 culinary schools.\n\nThis year also introduced the Nestl\u00e9 Professional Green Spatula Award, developed with the World Association of Chefs\u2019 Societies to promote sustainable culinary practices such as reducing food waste and sourcing responsibly.\n\nWinning teams; Professional Category - Santani Wellness Kandy (Winner), Shangri - La Hambanthota (1st Runner-up), Covanro Sigiriya (2nd Runner-up), Shangri-La Hambanthota (Grand Spatula Award); Junior Category - SLITHM Bandarawela (Winner), SLITHM Rathnapura (1st Runner-up), SLITHM Rathnapura and Academy of Hospitality Management (2nd Runner-up joint winners)."
  },
