    "chunk_size_bytes": 1802,
    "chunk_text": "INSEE Ecocycle launches electric waste collection trucks\n\nFrom left: INSEE Ecocycle Director Eng. Sujith Gunawardhana, Senior Manager Commercial and Logistics Janaka Ranga and Assistant Manager Logistics Chamal Rathnayake\n\nINSEE Ecocycle Lanka, a leading environmental solutions provider specialising in waste management and circular economy solutions, has marked a significant milestone with the launch of its first fully electric (EV) waste collection truck under the theme \u2018\u0dc4\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dad\u0dc0\u0dad\u0dca \u0d9c\u0db8\u0db1\u0d9a\u0dca\u2019 (A Greener Journey), marking the first step in a phased transition of its waste-collection fleet to electric vehicles.\n\nThe first vehicle was officially unveiled at the INSEE Ecocycle facility in Katunayake, in the presence of INSEE Ecocycle Director Eng. Sujith Gunawardhana.\n\nINSEE Ecocycle\u2019s move towards electric waste-collection trucks marks a significant step in decarbonising its logistics operations. By embracing cleaner transport technology, the company aims to reduce operational emissions and the overall lifecycle carbon footprint of the waste it manages.\n\nThe initiative also strengthens the sustainability commitments made to the customers through INSEE Ecocycle\u2019s ISO-certified Integrated Management System, demonstrating how environmental responsibility is being translated into practical, measurable action across the value chain for a greener future.\n\nINSEE Lanka CEO Eng. Thusith Gunawarnasuriya said, \u201cThis milestone reflects our commitment to embedding sustainability across every aspect of our operations. The transition to electric waste-collection trucks is more than a fleet upgrade; it is a tangible demonstration of our vision to lead the shift towards a lower-carbon future while creating lasting value for our stakeholders and the environment.\u201d"
  },
