    "chunk_size_bytes": 1488,
    "chunk_text": "SLTPB to get acting chairman this week amid conflicting reasons of Hewawasam\u2019s exit\n\nThe government is expected to appoint an Acting Chairman to the Sri Lanka Tourism Promotion Bureau (SLTPB) this week, as the agency faces a narrow window to finalise its budget for next year following the resignation of Chairman Buddhika Hewawasam, Mirror Business learns.\n\nHewawasam, who had headed the bureau since October 2024, stepped down upon completing his two-year term, with his last day in office understood to have been October 30. No successor or acting head had been formally named at the time of writing.\n\nIndustry sources indicated that the urgency stems from the bureau\u2019s annual budget for 2027, which must be finalised within the next few weeks. This leaves little room for a prolonged leadership vacuum at an agency that receives 70 percent of the Tourism Development Fund (TDF), the statutory levy paid by tourism businesses.\n\nHowever, accounts of why Hewawasam left differ sharply. While some within the industry maintain that he stepped down on personal grounds, one source familiar with the matter pointed to friction with the ministry. \u201cFrom what I hear, there is a disagreement between him and the foreign minister\u2014a clash,\u201d the source told Mirror Business. Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism Minister Vijitha Herath oversees both the SLTPB and the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority (SLTDA). Attempts to reach Hewawasam for comment were unsuccessful."
  },
