    "chunk_size_bytes": 1699,
    "chunk_text": "CAL eyes multi-fold growth as AFC opens global capital pipeline to frontier markets\n\nFrom left: Sachin Unamboowe, AVP and Head of Sales, CAL and Moderator; Thomas Hugger, Founder and CEO, Asia Frontier Capital Ltd.; Ruchir Desai (CFA), Fund Manager, Asia Frontier Capital Ltd.; Deshan Pushparajah (CFA), Managing Director \u2013 Global Markets, CAL; and Kanishke Mannakkara, Group CEO, CAL, during the panel discussion\n\nPoints to 15-17x AUM growth in eight years as a guide to ambitions\n\nCombined AUM at US$ 1.2bn, with a footprint spanning frontier economies worth about US$ 1.5tn\n\nCapital Alliance Holdings PLC (CAL) is betting that taking control of Hong Kong-based Asia Frontier Capital (AFC) can create a business many multiples the size of either firm, with the frontier fund manager\u2019s offshore platform set to channel global capital into frontier economies, according to CAL Group Chief Executive Officer Kanishke Mannakkara.\n\n\u201cWe are not investing in AFC because we think AFC will grow at 10 or 15 percent a year for the next five years. We see the potential to use the brilliance that AFC has to create something that is many multiples of what AFC is, and frankly what CAL is,\u201d Mannakkara told reporters in Colombo yesterday.\n\nPressed on the scale of those multiples, he steered clear of forward guidance, citing the regulatory limits on projections by a listed company, and pointed instead to the group\u2019s track record.\n\n\u201cI\u2019ll talk about the past, and I\u2019ll let you infer from that to the future,\u201d he remarked, noting that CAL\u2019s assets under management (AUM) had grown roughly 15 to 17 times over the past eight years, a compound annual growth rate of around 40 to 42 percent."
  },
