    "chunk_text": "For the first half, Group revenue increased 10 percent to Rs.283.74 billion and EBITDA grew 11 percent to Rs.34.65 billion. Pretax profit rose 10 percent to Rs.12.03 billion, while total profit after tax increased 34 percent to Rs.6.60 billion.\n\nOperating cash flow also strengthened, with a net inflow of Rs.18.83 billion against Rs.2.85 billion in the corresponding six months, helped by lower inventories and a release of funds from receivables.\n\nFinancing costs remain significant. First-half finance expenses increased 11 percent to Rs.13.25 billion, while bank overdrafts stood at Rs.61.12 billion at September-end.\n\nThe board declared a first interim dividend of 10 cents per share, payable on or before 2 December."
