    "md5": "12697e7b388ddfb11c50c4e4ec8543a7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1408,
    "chunk_text": "Victorian Premier meets Sri Lankan community leaders ahead of state election\n\nColombo, Nov. 4 (Daily Mirror) - Victorian Premier Ben Carroll has met with members of Melbourne\u2019s Sri Lankan community at a dinner hosted by community leader Sinantha Jayathilake, just weeks ahead of the November 28 state election.\n\nMr Carroll, who assumed office in July, was joined by Lily D\u2019Ambrosio, the retiring Member for Mill Park, who served as Victoria\u2019s Minister for Energy and Resources, Climate Action and the State Electricity Commission until July this year. She is regarded as Australia\u2019s longest-serving energy minister.\n\nAlso present were Lauren Kathage, MP for Yan Yean, and Elizabeth Nealy, Labor\u2019s candidate for Mill Park and a former Mayor of Banyule.\n\nCommunity leaders, business owners and families used the occasion to raise issues affecting Sri Lankan Victorians, including small business development, skilled migration, education and the rising cost of living.\n\n\u201cThe Sri Lankan community has helped build Victoria, from our small businesses to our hospitals and classrooms. Tonight was about making sure our voice is heard at the highest level, and I am grateful the Premier took the time to sit down and listen to us directly,\u201d Mr Jayathilake said.\n\nThe dinner was held during Ms D\u2019Ambrosio\u2019s final weeks in Parliament, following her 24 years of representing the Mill Park electorate."
