    "chunk_text": "He said the Government had spent two Budgets without delivering on its promises and questioned whether the third Budget would simply contain more unfulfilled assurances.\n\nRajapaksa also challenged the Government to identify new employment opportunities created through foreign investments attracted during its tenure.\n\nHe warned that unfavourable tax policies and legislation could further discourage foreign investment, arguing that both existing and potential investors could reconsider doing business in Sri Lanka.\n\nOn national security legislation, Rajapaksa said the Prevention of Terrorism Act (PTA) required amendments to reflect modern realities, particularly given the changing nature of terrorism and extremism in South Asia.\n\nHowever, he stressed that new legislation should not be used to target individuals based on their appearance, hairstyles, tattoos or clothing.\n\n\u201cModern anti-terrorism laws should address extremism and genuine security threats. They should not be used to imprison someone because of a tattoo, long hair or the clothes they wear,\u201d he said.\n\nHe also expressed concern over what he described as the increasing politicisation of the police and the misuse of law enforcement powers against Opposition members and ordinary citizens.\n\nCiting several alleged incidents, including deaths in police custody, shootings involving three-wheelers, alleged fabrication of drug-related charges and complaints of police misconduct, Rajapaksa questioned whether the Government was ensuring accountability within the police service.\n\nHe referred to the alleged death of a young man at the Homagama Police Station and questioned the Government\u2019s response to the incident.\n\nHe also raised concerns over an incident in which a 16-year-old was allegedly shot during a police pursuit, questioning the justification for the use of lethal force.\n\nReferring to incidents in Kurunegala, he alleged that police officers had been involved in misconduct, including an alleged robbery during a house search."
