    "chunk_text": "The JVP\u2019s catapulting to the Presidency and huge preponderance in Parliament in 2024 was mightily assisted by the laundering through a Presidential Commission appointed by President Chandrika Bandaranaike Kumaratunga of the stain of the delegitimising sin of Vijaya Kumaratunga\u2019s cruel murder. She had viciously and irrationally accused President Premadasa (at the time, Prime Minister) and not Wijeweera\u2019s JVP of murdering her husband and father of her two children. This despite the arrest and long, detailed confession by the gunman tasked and trained by the JVP for this and a series of other assassinations.\n\nThe worst damage to the SLFP came at the tail-end of her term when she went against the counsel of her brilliant Foreign Minister Lakshman Kadirgamar, and persisted in the project of a post-tsunami power-sharing mechanism (PTOMS) with the Tigers. That \u2018Munich\u2019-type betrayal was thwarted on two fronts:\n\nThe US Government, which emphasised that it was prevented by Congress from contributing funds to any structure involving a designated terrorist organisation. I was at the US Ambassador Jeff Lunstead\u2019s when Asst Secretary of State Christina Roca told that upfront to Ambassador Jayantha Dhanapala, CBK\u2019s chief negotiator with the LTTE over the PTOMS.\n\nThe Supreme Court of Sri Lanka which froze the vital middle tier of the mechanism located in the Wanni since it was inaccessible to the Sri Lankan State.\n\nFortunately for the SLFP, its founding father (CBK\u2019s father) SWRD Bandaranaike had a firm partner from the South when he began his independent political journey: DA Rajapaksa, whose son was the popular Prime Minister Mahinda Rajapaksa, a populist rebel known to dissent from the \u2018CBK line\u2019.\n\nOut of options, CBK grudgingly nominated Mahinda who won the 2005 Presidential election\u2014but not before she had gouged a wound that has never healed in the SLFP."
  },
