    "chunk_size_bytes": 2011,
    "chunk_text": "Fortunately for the SLFP, its founding father (CBK\u2019s father) SWRD Bandaranaike had a firm partner from the South when he began his independent political journey: DA Rajapaksa, whose son was the popular Prime Minister Mahinda Rajapaksa, a populist rebel known to dissent from the \u2018CBK line\u2019.\n\nOut of options, CBK grudgingly nominated Mahinda who won the 2005 Presidential election\u2014but not before she had gouged a wound that has never healed in the SLFP.\n\nPrabhakaran would boycott the Presidential Election because he discouraged \u2018Eelam Tamil\u2019 participation in a Sri Lankan election.\n\nThe US and India should support the Sri Lankan State against the Tigers, and endeavour to shape the postwar outcome in the direction of implementing existing devolution.\n\nFollowing my presentation, Steve Ghitelman who headed the South Asia desk of the US State Department\u2019s prestigious research wing, the INR, came up and invited me to speak on the upcoming election and the peace process to an inter-agency audience convened by/at the State Dept, which I did.\n\nProf. Walter Anderson told me that President Kumaratunga had informed them at dinner that she would support Opposition candidate Ranil Wickremesinghe at the election, he would win, Mahinda would lose, and she and Ranil together would offer Prabhakaran a federal solution, ushering in peace.\n\nKnowing\u00a0 CBK to be a lady of her word, I promptly pressed the ejector-button on my Washington gig, returned to Colombo and leaped into the election campaign, appearing on TV in support of Mahinda.\n\nMahinda Rajapaksa had to contest with a divided SLFP, his old friend Anura Bandaranaike (and even Sarath Amunugama) against him. After Mahinda won, Mangala Samaraweera tried to stall his assumption of SLFP leadership. MR plugged the gap with the support of his family \u2018clan\u2019, the ultranationalist Hela Urumaya, and the JVP. Mahinda had been until then, an opponent of an SLFP-JVP alliance which he prophesied would siphon-off SLFP votes to the JVP someday."
