    "md5": "628b0c9ca82380b1d9856585ca6953b2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1892,
    "chunk_text": "The shift in the balance of the SLFP and its partners, strengthening the ultranationalist element when Chandrika divided it in 2005 in her attempt to sabotage Mahinda.\n\nThe catastrophic Gotabaya Presidency was overthrown by the Sri Lankan citizens led by the university students and youth.\n\nThe SLFP created by SWRD Bandaranaike breaking away from the UNP, was realigned by Chandrika with the UNP under its most neoliberal leader, ending the two-party system as we knew it from 1951, making inevitable the rise of new forces to fill the space, play the role.\n\nInstead of voting for their own Dullas Alahapperuma at the Parliamentary selection of the President in 2022 (which Mahinda Rajapaksa disclosed he did), the SLPP, conceived through opposing the 2015 coalition with Ranil\u2019s UNP, supported Ranil Wickremesinghe instead, making him President. Thus, Ranil who was never elected President by the citizenry, was appointed to that post by Gotabaya Rajapaksa and endorsed by the SLPP\u2014reloading Chandrika\u2019s 2015 \u2018hybrid\u2019.\n\nRanil\u2019s economic stabilisation/adjustment \u2018shock therapy\u2019 (2022-2024) further crunched the SLPP\u2019s base after Gotabaya\u2019s \u2018fertiliser shock\u2019 had shrunk it (2019-2022). SLPP voters shifted to the JVP-NPP.\n\nWhen Namal Rajapaksa boldly broke away from the Ranil-led project and ran as SLPP candidate in 2024, elements of the SLPP and SLFP who had opposed the Yahapalanaya coalition, ironically stayed to support Ranil\u2014mimicking Chandrika\u2019s 2015 model.\n\nHaving co-founded the SLMP with Vijaya and outflanked her sibling Anura Bandaranaike from the left, critiquing his tilt towards JR\u2019s UNP, CBK turned architect of an SLFP-UNP coalition, reversing, negating and betraying her great father\u2019s 1951 and 1956 breakthroughs.\n\nThe UNP was wrecked by Ranil, the SLFP by Chandrika, the SLPP by Gotabaya. That\u2019s how and why AKD and the JVP prevailed."
  },
