    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "17f70e22629090078a85f992773d79a1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1853,
    "chunk_text": "I am no lawyer. I am no constitutional pundit either. But I do have a memory. I belong to the generation that witnessed our collective slide into the abyss of unreason following the passage of the original Prevention of Terrorism Act (PTA).\n\nAs we watch President Anura Kumara Dissanayake navigate his ship of state, one is forced to ask the very same question: Is AKD running faster than the winds that buffet him?\n\nIn his frantic hurry to manage a fragile economy still in recovery mode, appease international lenders, and anchor his party's grip on the state, is he sprinting so fast into the arms of the old national security apparatus that he has outrun his own shadow?\n\nThe parallel between J.R. (Dickie) Jayewardene\u2019s executive velocity and AKD\u2019s contemporary style appears obvious, instructive, and in this instance, quite chilling.\n\nWhen JRJ assumed absolute power in 1977, he moved with a terrifying, calculated speed. He claimed that his radical restructuring of the state, the creation of the omnipotent Executive Presidency and the enactment of the draconian 1979 PTA\u2014was a historical necessity to pave the way for economic liberalisation and to protect the nation from chaotic, destabilising forces.\n\nJRJ ran faster than the gales of labor unrest and ethnic tension, outrunning democratic norms to build an institutional fortress for the ruling class.\n\nToday, AKD operates with a similarly breathless executive urgency. Faced with the howling winds of IMF restructuring, external debt traps, and the volatile undercurrents of public expectations, the National People\u2019s Power (NPP) Government has seemingly abandoned the slow, cumbersome luxury of democratic consultation.\n\nLike JRJ, AKD\u2019s style is one of top-down efficiency; he behaves not as a subverter of the system, but as its ultimate authority\u2014a kind of Supreme Arbiter!"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-05-dailyftlk-fbec5331",
    "num": "dailyftlk-fbec5331",
    "date_str": "2026-11-05",
    "description": "Proletarian, virtuous Bonapartism",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/columns/Proletarian-virtuous-Bonapartism/4-799647",
