    "chunk_index": 2,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "22e909415ec2cc3ebd6410c969ec6e86",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1969,
    "chunk_text": "Today, AKD operates with a similarly breathless executive urgency. Faced with the howling winds of IMF restructuring, external debt traps, and the volatile undercurrents of public expectations, the National People\u2019s Power (NPP) Government has seemingly abandoned the slow, cumbersome luxury of democratic consultation.\n\nLike JRJ, AKD\u2019s style is one of top-down efficiency; he behaves not as a subverter of the system, but as its ultimate authority\u2014a kind of Supreme Arbiter!\n\nWhat happens when the subordinate class finally scales the ramparts of the state and occupies the throne room? History offers two scripts.\n\nIn the first, the victorious revolutionaries smash the old instruments of tyranny, declaring an unvarnished dawn of liberty. In the second\u2014the more common, painfully predictable script\u2014they look around the palace, realise how remarkably comfortable the executive chairs are, and decide that the old instruments of state control weren't actually not bad. They were just being operated on by the wrong people!\n\nWith these two bills, the promised political renaissance is rapidly transforming from a progressive social-democratic daydream into a wonderfully Orwellian reality.\n\nDuring the 2024 election cycle, the NPP alliance, spearheaded by the modern Janatha Vimukthi Peramuna (JVP), marched to power on a platform of immaculate moral renewal.\n\nTheir manifesto explicitly promised the total abolition of all \"oppressive\" laws, a blanket guarantee of civil rights, and the definitive burial of the infamous PTA.\n\nNow, the Ministry of Justice has presented a parallel universe of legal wizardry. To the uninitiated, this looks like a flagrant betrayal. But that is because you do not understand the subtle, Orwellian dialectic of modern governance.\n\nIn this new dispensation, \"Good Governance\" is no longer measured by human rights charters or international legal certainty. \"Good\" is whatever the JVP Politburo decides is good on any given day!"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-05-dailyftlk-fbec5331",
    "num": "dailyftlk-fbec5331",
    "date_str": "2026-11-05",
    "description": "Proletarian, virtuous Bonapartism",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/columns/Proletarian-virtuous-Bonapartism/4-799647",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
