    "chunk_text": "The common principle is simple: intervene early, facilitate payment by viable taxpayers, and act decisively against deliberate defaulters.\n\nCleaning up historical arrears addresses only part of the problem. Sri Lanka must simultaneously prevent another stock of uncollectible debt from accumulating.\n\nThe strategy for addressing the Rs. 2.1 trillion should therefore be straightforward: collect, resolve, or remove.\n\nCollect what is legally enforceable and economically recoverable. Resolve disputed liabilities quickly, including through carefully designed settlements where appropriate. And remove from the headline figure amounts that, following proper legal scrutiny, cannot realistically be recovered.\n\nSri Lanka has already asked compliant taxpayers to make a substantial contribution towards fiscal consolidation. Further gains should come from making the existing tax system work more effectively.\n\n(The author is Partner, Head of Tax, Deloitte Sri Lanka and Maldives)"
