    "md5": "e2883b7ef58f5dae4cfb848f8ed38266",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1931,
    "chunk_text": "The all-inclusive freight regime began with Gazette Extraordinary No. 1842/16 of 27 December 2013, effective 6 January 2014, and was developed through Gazette No. 2041/10 of 17 October 2017. The 2022 amendments under Gazette No. 2302/24 proved controversial, and Gazette No. 2321/62 rescinded the 2017 regulations and the 2022 amendment in March 2023. The Minister then issued Gazette Extraordinary No. 2334/26 on 31 May 2023, under section 10 of the Licensing of Shipping Agents, Freight Forwarders, Non-Vessel Operating Common Carriers and Container Operators Act, No. 10 of 1972. Its key provisions are these:\n\nRegulation 3: charges covering carriage \u201cfrom the origin to destination\u201d are included in the all-inclusive freight and recovered \u201conly from the party who is contractually bound to pay\u201d it.\n\nRegulations 5 and 7: no charge other than the all-inclusive freight may be made to importers or exporters, save a delivery order fee for importers, payable in Sri Lankan rupees.\n\nThe Gazette does not abolish THC as an economic cost. It regulates how that cost is recovered and identifies the party contractually liable for it. A service provider remains free to negotiate the total freight price. The primary question is therefore whether a charge forms part of the agreed carriage contract, not whether its cost arose at sea or on land.\n\nTwo layers of rules decide who pays. The first is the sale contract. Incoterms 2020, published by the International Chamber of Commerce, decide which of buyer or seller must arrange and pay for carriage: under FOB the buyer, under CIF the seller. They are contractual terms and do not govern the contract of carriage itself (Maersk summary of Incoterms 2020). The second layer is the contract of carriage. The party that contracts with the line or NVOCC pays the freight, and in Sri Lanka the Gazette requires that freight to be all-inclusive and recoverable only from that party."
