    "md5": "dbf986ecba1279340b74fbd6ef152e93",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1865,
    "chunk_text": "Northern Exporters Forum 2027: Connecting local production with global markets\n\nThe Northern Exporters Forum 2027 has been officially launched as an important initiative to connect the Northern Province\u2019s productive capacity and natural resources with international markets.\n\nThe forum will be held on 20 and 21 January 2027 at the Thiruvalluvar Cultural Centre in Jaffna. Its official launch and programme briefing took place on 29 October 2026 at the Northern Province Governor\u2019s Secretariat, under the leadership of Governor N. Vethanayahan.\n\nThe Governor said the forum would support the goal of increasing the Northern Province\u2019s contribution to Sri Lanka\u2019s gross domestic product from 4.5 per cent to 10 per cent. He emphasised the importance of expanding production, adding value, reaching new markets and attracting investment. The province has considerable potential in agriculture, fisheries, palmyrah-based products, handicrafts, information technology, tourism and cultural industries.\n\nFollowing the investment summit organised in the Northern Province this year, the Management Club of Sri Lanka\u2019s decision to hold an exporters\u2019 forum represents a useful next step in supporting the region\u2019s economic development. Attracting investment is important, but so is helping local products reach wider markets and creating opportunities to sell them.\n\nThe forum aims to introduce goods produced and services offered in the Northern Province to overseas markets, while strengthening the capabilities of small and medium-sized enterprises preparing to export.\n\nThe sectors expected to feature include agriculture and processed foods, palmyrah-based products, seafood, handloom and handicrafts, information technology, renewable energy, small industries, wellness products, traditional medicine, medical equipment, tourism and cultural industries."
  },
