    "chunk_text": "The agreement was signed by Northern Province Governor N. Vethanayahan, Vavuniya University Vice-Chancellor Arputharajah and Management Club of Sri Lanka Project Chairman Kaushal Rajapaksa. The initiative is intended to coordinate investors\u2019 engagement with relevant departments and institutions, and make it easier to obtain the information they need.\n\nThe Management Club of Sri Lanka is organising the forum, with the Ministry of Industry and Entrepreneurship Development providing leadership and support. The Consulate General of India in Jaffna is a key cooperation partner. The Export Development Board, National Chamber of Exporters, National Enterprise Development Authority and Industrial Development Board are also involved as partners. Vavuniya University will serve as the regional project management unit.\n\nConsul General of India Sai Murali, who attended the meeting, noted that useful lessons could be shared from similar initiatives previously undertaken in India. Such exchanges could help strengthen the export readiness of local producers.\n\nThe Northern Exporters Forum 2027 has the potential to provide an important platform for showcasing the province\u2019s productive capacity. For that opportunity to translate into lasting economic benefits, producers will need continued practical support before and after the forum\u2014including market information, access to finance and technical assistance, quality improvements and transport facilities. With sustained cooperation, products from the Northern Province can secure a lasting place in domestic and international markets."
