    "chunk_size_bytes": 1998,
    "chunk_text": "Delivering the keynote on \u2018The Future of FinTech,\u2019 Weerasinghe said Sri Lanka\u2019s post-crisis recovery has created the foundation for growth, but the next phase must focus on productivity, investment, employment and innovation.\n\n\u201cStability is not the destination; it is the foundation upon which sustainable growth must be built,\u201d he said.\n\nSri Lanka already has digital banking, mobile and internet banking, payment cards, digital payment applications and interoperable national payment infrastructure through LankaPay, he noted.\n\nLooking ahead, the Governor identified open and interoperable financial services, digital identity, data-driven lending, cross-border payment connectivity and digital investment services as key growth areas.\n\nHe also warned that fintech brings risks, including cyberattacks, operational disruptions, fraud, data breaches, inadequate consumer disclosures, excessive leverage and concentration of critical services among technology providers.\n\n\u201cWe must strike the right balance: encouraging competition and innovation while ensuring effective supervision, sound risk management and strong consumer protection,\u201d Weerasinghe said.\n\nHe reiterated that the Central Bank remains open to innovation and pointed to its FinTech Regulatory Sandbox as a controlled environment for testing eligible financial solutions.\n\nFinTech Forum Sri Lanka Chairman Channa de Silva said the theme of this year\u2019s festival was much more than a tagline.\n\n\u201cIt highlights the opportunity in front of us, at an organisation and a national level. Bringing together innovators, financial institutions, policymakers and global partners, we showcased Sri Lanka\u2019s fintech capabilities, opened doors to attract investment and talent, and created pathways for local solutions to scale internationally,\u201d he said.\n\n\u201cOur ultimate ambition is to turn collaboration into lasting economic value for the country and position Sri Lanka as a fintech hub in the regional fintech landscape.\u201d"
