    "chunk_text": "\u201cIt highlights the opportunity in front of us, at an organisation and a national level. Bringing together innovators, financial institutions, policymakers and global partners, we showcased Sri Lanka\u2019s fintech capabilities, opened doors to attract investment and talent, and created pathways for local solutions to scale internationally,\u201d he said.\n\n\u201cOur ultimate ambition is to turn collaboration into lasting economic value for the country and position Sri Lanka as a fintech hub in the regional fintech landscape.\u201d\n\nThe Sri Lanka FinTech Festival 2026, organised by FinTech Forum Sri Lanka in collaboration with the Digital Economy Ministry and powered by Visa, was held from 2 to 3 November at Shangri-La Colombo under the theme \u2018Building Capacity, Creating Opportunities and Scaling Sri Lanka\u2019s Digital Future.\u2019\n\nThe festival brought together policymakers, regulators, banks, non-bank financial institutions, technology firms, investors, entrepreneurs, SMEs and tourism-sector stakeholders to discuss the future of digital finance and showcase Sri Lanka\u2019s digital financial services capabilities.\n\nThe two-day event included the FinTech Expo conference, featuring exhibition floors, keynotes and panel discussions, and concluded with FinTech Night and the FinTech Awards 2026, which recognised contributors to Sri Lanka\u2019s fintech ecosystem."
