    "chunk_size_bytes": 1733,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka export excellence initiative supports SMEs to scale globally\n\nThe Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB), in collaboration with the International Finance Corporation (IFC) and the European Union (EU), successfully conducted the final pitching event of batch III of ExpoScaleUp, designed to help Sri Lankan SMEs become more competitive and expand into global markets. Supported through the EU\u2019s regional Accelerating Climate Smart and Inclusive Infrastructure in South Asia (ACSIIS) initiative under the EU Global Gateway Strategy, ExpoScaleUp is part of the Sri Lanka Export Excellence Initiative (SLEEI), a flagship program aimed at strengthening SME export readiness, market access and long-term competitiveness.\n\nThrough ExpoScaleUp III, 25 Sri Lankan SMEs developed export market plans to sharpen their strategies and position their businesses for international growth. The program concluded with a pitching event, where participants presented their business potential and pathways to new markets before a panel of experts.\n\nIn his opening address, EDB Chairman Mangala Wijesinghe, highlighted the importance of SMEs in strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s export sector and expanding the country\u2019s presence in international markets. He also acknowledged the collaborative efforts of IFC and the European Union in supporting Sri Lankan enterprises through initiatives aimed at enhancing their capabilities and export competitiveness.\n\nSpeaking at the event, IFC South Asia Manager-Country Advisory and Economics Gregory Smith, emphasised that helping SMEs are central to Sri Lanka\u2019s economy, and helping them compete globally is key to unlocking Sri Lanka\u2019s growth, creating jobs and strengthening economic resilience."
  },
