    "chunk_size_bytes": 1752,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2013Italy Business Council elects Dushy Jayaweera as President\n\nThe Sri Lanka\u2013Italy Business Council (SLITBC) of The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce held its 27th Annual General Meeting recently, electing a new leadership team for the year ahead and reflecting on the Council\u2019s longstanding role in strengthening business ties between Sri Lanka and Italy.\n\nDushy Jayaweera of the Acorn Group was elected President, while Shamil Mendis of Spear International was appointed Senior Vice President and Anika Williamson of JAT Holdings was elected Vice President, while Daminda Mulgama, outgoing President of the Council, will continue to serve as the Immediate Past President.\n\nThe AGM saw the participation of five of the Council\u2019s 13 Past Presidents, a notable presence that reflected its 27-year history and the contributions of successive leaders in promoting trade, investment and commercial cooperation between Sri Lanka and Italy.\n\nThe Council\u2019s Patron, Ambassador of Italy Damiano Francovigh and Deputy Head of Mission Dr. Alberto Arcidiacono also attended the AGM. Their presence reflected the continued support of the Italian Embassy for the Council\u2019s work and the importance of maintaining close engagement between the two countries\u2019 business communities.\n\nThe keynote address was delivered by Taprobane Seafoods Managing Director Timothy O\u2019Reilly who shared his company\u2019s journey and experiences in business development in Sri Lanka and Italy, while drawing on lessons in entrepreneurship and the opportunities available to Sri Lankan businesses in Italy.\n\nMembers also reviewed the Council\u2019s activities over the past year and discussed future priorities for expanding bilateral trade, investment and business partnerships."
  },
