    "chunk_text": "He is currently engaged with Startup operations, Conservation initiatives, and in providing Consulting support to limited businesses who are hungry for growth and transformation. His skill in growing people and delivering demonstrated breakthrough results repeatedly through existing teams, stem from the ability to combine best practices from different disciplines and industries with a bias for practical action, and by challenging norms which inhibit growth potential.\n\nFor many years, he was on the International Board of Youth Business International, which was one of King Charles\u2019 Charities based out of UK, and he has served on several local Boards. He was President of the Wildlife and Nature Protection Society (WNPS) and played a key catalytical role in its renaissance. Currently Chairman of their PLANT initiative (www.plantsl.org), he conceptualised and gave leadership to the initiative to drive it to become the largest private sector driven ecosystem restoration effort in Sri Lanka. A former Editor of the Loris Magazine, he currently spends most of his time working on addressing broad Conservation issues within Sri Lanka through practical responses on ground. He is a published photographer and passionate about travelling, music, and Community work."
