    "language": "en",
    "md5": "1815ebb384e5aa5c10060409f757d86a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1693,
    "chunk_text": "Meta and Roar AdX launch growth academy for Sri Lankan SMEs\n\nFrom left: Roar AdX Regional Vice President of Client Success Udara Dharmasena, Industries and Entrepreneurship Development Deputy Minister Chathuranga Abeysinghe, Meta Asia Pacific Director of Government and Social Impact Kaiya Waddell, Public Policy Manager Tehara Punchihewa, and Roar Global CMO Umair Wolid\n\nMeta recently launched its Small Business Growth Academy in Sri Lanka in partnership with Roar AdX, bringing practical digital marketing knowledge to entrepreneurs looking to reach more customers and grow their businesses.\n\nPresided over by Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Deputy Minister\u00a0 Chathuranga Abeysinghe, the launch brought together government and Meta representatives alongside local entrepreneurs who are clients of Roar AdX to discuss how small businesses can participate more effectively in the digital economy. Meta\u2019s platform insights were complemented by business owners\u2019 experiences of building brands on Facebook, Instagram and WhatsApp, grounding the discussion in the opportunities and challenges facing Sri Lankan enterprises. Through Roar AdX, these entrepreneurs had the opportunity to engage directly with Meta representatives, share their perspectives and learn about the latest tools and developments to support their growth.\n\nThe Academy forms part of Meta\u2019s rollout across 12 Asia-Pacific markets, with the program already introduced in countries including Pakistan, Malaysia and Indonesia. It aims to help entrepreneurs put digital and AI-enabled tools to practical use, with training covering advertising, Reels, WhatsApp for Business and reaching customers across borders."
  },
