    "md5": "021b21fc1fe139ede8432a466a8b838e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1916,
    "chunk_text": "CHOGM 2026 opens with drive to unlock prosperity for Commonwealth\u2019s 2.7 billion people\n\nThe 2026 Commonwealth Heads of Government Meeting (CHOGM) opened in Antigua and Barbuda on Tuesday with a drive for bold partnerships between governments and businesses to unlock prosperity for the Commonwealth\u2019s 2.7 billion people.\n\nCharles III, Head of the Commonwealth, joined leaders from across the Commonwealth at the official Opening Ceremony on 3 November 2026 in St. John\u2019s, where they were welcomed with a vibrant performance and dance, celebrating Antiguan and Barbudan culture and history.\n\nThe ceremony marked the start of leaders\u2019 deliberations under the theme \u2018Accelerating Partnerships and Investment for a Prosperous Commonwealth\u2019.\n\nThis is the first CHOGM under the leadership of Commonwealth Secretary-General Hon Shirley Botchwey. It will also be the first time Heads of Government engage directly at CHOGM with business leaders, investors, heads of international financial institutions and philanthropists. Their focus will be on mobilising partnerships and investment in scalable projects that will tangibly respond to member country needs, including in areas of skills-building, climate finance and green energy.\n\nIn his remarks, the King said: \u201cAll around us, trust between nations is under critical strain, as international norms and systems are tested to their limits. Brutal conflict stalks our world, destroying lives and casting long shadows across the globe. Technology is transforming our societies and our economies at dizzying speed, with little certainty about where it might lead us.\n\n\u201cAs I have consistently tried to emphasise, climate change is no longer just a terrifying prospect, but a catastrophic reality which threatens our very way of life\u2026 And in each of our countries, for too many people, the opportunity to fulfil their own potential lies far beyond their reach."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
