    "chunk_text": "The company's AI business is centered around Colossus and Colossus II, \u200btwo of the world's largest AI data centers near Memphis. Renting their computing power to customers including Anthropic has sent \u200brevenue soaring and helped SpaceX \u2060post its first profit as a public company.\n\nAny delays in bringing the capacity online may hamper Musk's ambitious revenue targets and intensify scrutiny from investors growing wary about AI infrastructure's mounting costs.\n\nChip research firm \u2060SemiAnalysis has identified \u200bmore than 9 gigawatts of planned or developing capacity, including new facilities at SpaceX's Starbase complex in \u200bBoca Chica, Texas.\n\nThat Boca Chica expansion could face resistance as Hinojosa has opposed the potential sale, opens new tab of a beachfront state park to SpaceX after Texas Monthly reported officials had discussed the deal.\n\n\"Let me be clear: Texas \u200bis not for sale,\" Hinojosa said last month. Musk, meanwhile, has deleted his election-day appeal to his followers to vote Republican."
