    "md5": "d645afb2deb867dff6520a94f8629a13",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1697,
    "chunk_text": "FASL launches university engagement under National AI Awareness Programme\n\nThe Fintech Association of Sri Lanka (FASL) commenced its university engagement under the National Artificial Intelligence Awareness Programme with a guest lecture at the University of Kelaniya on 26 October.\n\nThe two-hour lecture, delivered to undergraduate Financial Technology students by Rajkumar Kanagasingam, Founding President of FASL and Industry Fellow at the Global FinTech Institute, Singapore, introduced students to the evolution of FinTech, Generative AI, Agentic AI and emerging developments in global financial services.\n\nThe lecture was coordinated by Dr. Hirindu Kawshala, Senior Lecturer and Coordinator of the Master of Commerce (MCom) Programme at the University of Kelaniya.\n\nThe initiative follows a discussion Kanagasingam held with Prime Minister Dr. Harini Amarasuriya at Temple Trees in January 2026 on AI awareness and capacity building, followed by a proposal submitted to the Prime Minister\u2019s Office concerning FASL\u2019s National Artificial Intelligence Awareness Programme.\n\nThe FASL-led programme is supported by the Global Tech Advocates (GTA) Sri Lanka Working Group, part of an international network of over 40,000 technology professionals that includes Tech London Advocates, a Founding Partner of London Tech Week.\n\nThe lecture featured selected video-based educational presentations from the University of Hong Kong\u2019s \u2018Introduction to FinTech\u2019 course, led by Professor Douglas W. Arner, Kerry Holdings Professor in Law at the University of Hong Kong, Associate Director of the Cambridge Centre for Alternative Finance at the University of Cambridge, and Senior Adviser to FASL."
  },
  {
