    "md5": "a1201f63b21ec3137e60eb31c0ec5ac9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1975,
    "chunk_text": "The lecture featured selected video-based educational presentations from the University of Hong Kong\u2019s \u2018Introduction to FinTech\u2019 course, led by Professor Douglas W. Arner, Kerry Holdings Professor in Law at the University of Hong Kong, Associate Director of the Cambridge Centre for Alternative Finance at the University of Cambridge, and Senior Adviser to FASL.\n\nThe lecture highlighted Singapore\u2019s emergence as a leading international financial and FinTech hub, with particular attention to DBS Bank\u2019s pioneering role in integrating artificial intelligence across banking operations, customer services and digital banking.\n\nThe lecture drew an analogy between Agentic AI and aircraft autopilot systems to illustrate the importance of human oversight. While Generative AI primarily produces content, analysis and recommendations, Agentic AI can plan and execute tasks with varying degrees of autonomy. Just as aircraft autopilot systems operate under pilot supervision, Agentic AI requires appropriate safeguards and human oversight to prevent unintended outcomes.\n\nThe lecture also introduced students to the Cambridge Centre for Alternative Finance\u2019s 2026 Global AI in Financial Services Report, highlighting the growing importance of understanding AI developments in the global financial sector.\n\nDrawing on the Global Finance & Technology Network\u2019s (GFTN) Insights resources, students viewed selected video excerpts featuring Michael S. Barr, Governor of the US Federal Reserve and former Special Adviser to US President Bill Clinton, from the Singapore FinTech Festival 2025 panel discussion, \u201cThe Global Policy Dialogue: Towards the Next Decade of Transformation and New Financial Corridors.\u201d\n\nFASL plans to continue the National Artificial Intelligence Awareness Programme through university engagements and other initiatives, strengthening AI literacy, industry\u2013academia collaboration, responsible innovation and financial inclusion in Sri Lanka."
  },
