    "chunk_size_bytes": 1992,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka shines at Asia-Pacific Retailers Convention & Exhibition in Tokyo\n\nChathura Jayawardena, Chief Marketing Officer | Abans PLC receiving the Sri Lankan Retail Country Award from Murali Prakash, Chairman (FAPRA)\n\nAnuradha Ekanayake, CEO of Suwanda Industries (Pvt) Ltd, receiving the FAPRA Asia-Pacific Award 2026 for Best Efforts in Social Responsibility from Murali Prakash\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s retail industry marked an important milestone at the 22nd Asia-Pacific Retailers Convention & Exhibition (APRCE) in Tokyo, with regional award recognition, a key leadership appointment and new opportunities for cross-border collaboration.\n\nA 16-member delegation representing leading Sri Lankan businesses participated in APRCE Tokyo 2026, facilitated by the Sri Lanka Retailers\u2019 Association (SLRA). Held under the theme \u201cThe Future of Retail: Innovation Meets Tradition,\u201d the event brought together retail leaders from across the Asia-Pacific region for industry insights, networking and exploration of emerging retail trends.\n\nThe highlight of the mission was the important FAPRA Asia-Pacific Award 2026 for Best Efforts in Social Responsibility, won by Suwanda Industries (Cycle Pure Incense) for its initiative, \u201cSuwandaka Saviya \u2013 The Hands That Build Hope.\u201d Recognised at the APRCE Gala Awards, the achievement stood out among submissions from more than 15 Asia-Pacific countries and regions, placing a powerful Sri Lankan story of social responsibility on the regional stage.\n\nAdding to the celebrations, Abans PLC secured the SLRA Retail Awards 2026 Country Award for \u201cHaritha Wiruwa \u2013 Green Hero,\u201d recognised as the best overall initiative across five award categories.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s presence extended beyond recognition. Murali Prakash, Outgoing Chairman of FAPRA and a Past President and Executive Committee Member of SLRA, was elected Deputy Chairman of FAPRA for the next term, strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s representation within the Asia-Pacific retail community."
  },
