    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s presence extended beyond recognition. Murali Prakash, Outgoing Chairman of FAPRA and a Past President and Executive Committee Member of SLRA, was elected Deputy Chairman of FAPRA for the next term, strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s representation within the Asia-Pacific retail community.\n\nThe delegation also benefited from conference sessions, networking with regional industry leaders and retail exposure in Tokyo, including a facilitated visit to the renowned Ginza retail district.\n\nRepresentatives from Abans, Healthguard, Hameedia, Singer, NoLimit, Lakarcade, One Galle Face Mall of Shangri-La Hotels Lanka (Pvt) Ltd, and Suwanda Industries took part in the mission, bringing together diverse perspectives from Sri Lanka\u2019s retail and consumer sectors.\n\nThe mission reflects SLRA\u2019s continuing commitment to connecting Sri Lankan retailers with international knowledge, regional networks and opportunities for collaboration\u2014supporting a more competitive, innovative and globally connected retail industry.\n\nFrom a prestigious regional award to stronger representation in Asia-Pacific retail leadership, APRCE Tokyo 2026 was a significant moment for Sri Lanka\u2019s retail sector\u2014and a platform on which to build future partnerships."
