    "md5": "a8f93ae32eb2c2334f528e5aa1e46d0e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1622,
    "chunk_text": "Uber-Hayleys Mobility accelerate NEV adoption\n\nExclusive pricing and financing options on electric cars to help Uber drivers switch to cleaner, more affordable mobility\n\nUber and Hayleys Mobility announced an exclusive partnership to make electric vehicles (EVs) more accessible and affordable for the Uber drivers.\n\nThe collaboration brings together Uber\u2019s ride-hailing technology and driver network with Hayleys Mobility\u2019s new energy vehicle (NEV) portfolio and EV charging ecosystem, helping the drivers transition to electric mobility while reducing their everyday operating costs.\n\nAs part of the partnership, the eligible Uber drivers will have access to the Kaiyi eVibe e04electric car, at an exclusive discounted price, making the transition easier.\n\nHayleys Mobility will also facilitate leasing options through its network of over 20 financing partners, helping the drivers overcome one of the biggest barriers to EV ownership - the upfront cost of purchasing a vehicle.\n\nThe offer will be available through Uber\u2019s driver app, allowing the eligible drivers to discover the vehicle and explore purchase and financing options directly through the Uber app.\n\nUber Sri Lanka Country Manager Mobility Kaushalya Gunaratne said, \u201cFor the drivers, the switch to EVs needs to make economic sense, not just environmental sense. By making EVs more affordable and accessible, our partnership with Hayleys Mobility can help the drivers lower their operating costs, retain more of their earnings and contribute to cleaner mobility in Sri Lanka. We are confident that this encourages more drivers to make the switch.\u201d"
  },
