    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "6d8891e0fbbfb3d3f67762b50deda4f0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1703,
    "chunk_text": "CanCham Sri Lanka leads business delegation to Canada\n\nThe Business Promotion Mission of the Canadian Chamber of Commerce in Sri Lanka (CanCham Sri Lanka) created opportunities for its member companies to connect with the Canadian investors, explore commercial partnerships and expand their reach to international markets.\n\nRun from October 18 to November 01, 2026, the mission travelled across Vancouver, Toronto, Ottawa and Montr\u00e9al, with a focus on sectors such as tourism, real estate and infrastructure, agritech, green housing, healthcare and wellness, education, IT and fintech, with women in development and empowerment identified as a special area of interest.\n\nAt a business conclave and networking session in Vancouver, hosted by former Surrey Board of Trade President and CEO Anita Huberman, CanCham Sri Lanka Co-Founder and Board Director Mohamed Hameez outlined the chamber\u2019s proposed Canada-Sri Lanka-Indo-Pacific Corridor Initiative.\n\n\u201cOur proposed initiative seeks to connect the Canadian expertise, capital and innovation with Sri Lanka\u2019s capabilities and commercial opportunities. At a time of changing global trade dynamics, market diversification is increasingly important. Sri Lanka\u2019s strategic location at the crossroads of South Asia, Southeast Asia and the Middle East, together with its position along major maritime routes, presents opportunities for the Canadian businesses seeking to expand their reach into regional markets,\u201d he said.\n\nThe initiative is intended to link the Canadian investment and expertise with Sri Lankan businesses and resources, providing a framework for exploring commercial cooperation across the two countries and the wider Indo-Pacific."
  },
