    "chunk_size_bytes": 1694,
    "chunk_text": "The initiative is intended to link the Canadian investment and expertise with Sri Lankan businesses and resources, providing a framework for exploring commercial cooperation across the two countries and the wider Indo-Pacific.\n\nThe Vancouver programme included meetings with colleges and universities as well as Sri Lankan university student groups from British Columbia and Alberta, opening discussions on educational links and potential areas of collaboration.\n\nAt the Port City Colombo Investment Forum \u2013 Metro Vancouver, Hameez highlighted Port City Colombo\u2019s potential to attract regional business operations and investment. The forum connected the Canadian investors with Sri Lankan business leaders to explore the prospects in the country\u2019s flagship Special Economic Zone.\n\nFormer Surrey Councillor Linda Annis was also appointed as CanCham Sri Lanka\u2019s Honorary Brand Ambassador, which strengthens a further link between the chamber and Canadian community as it develops its international business network.\n\nFollowing the Vancouver programme, the delegation continued its mission in Toronto, Ottawa and Montr\u00e9al, with further business, investment, institutional and tourism-related engagements planned across the three cities.\n\nCanCham Sri Lanka is also connected to investment-promotion initiatives in Sri Lanka, including Northern Investment Summit and Sri Lanka Expo 2027. These platforms promote the chamber\u2019s international outreach by strengthening links between the local enterprises and overseas investors.\n\nThrough its involvement, CanCham Sri Lanka aims to build on its international business network and expand opportunities for international commercial cooperation."
