    "language": "en",
    "md5": "43b0cb442b2cacf251dfa5a4ad4fed9f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1841,
    "chunk_text": "MiHCM launches skills-based LMS, evolving Ziksa into personalised learning platform\n\nMiHCM has launched a new skills-based Learning Management System (LMS) that personalises learning for each employee while giving organisations stronger governance and clearer insight into learning effectiveness. The platform is now available to customers across all MiHCM regions.\n\nThe launch marks the evolution of its former Ziksa learning platform into a more connected learning and development experience.\n\nA new onboarding journey captures each learner\u2019s goals, preferences, strengths, interests, and preferred pace. Learning archetypesthen shape the experience, while a personalised dashboard recommends learning based on the learner\u2019s strengths and future growth directions.\n\n\u201cWith the new MiHCM LMS, we are connecting learning to each employee\u2019s goals, strengths, and career direction, while giving organisations the governance and insight to manage it at scale. The result is a learning experience that is simpler for employees, more manageable for organisations, and designed to become increasingly intelligent over time,\u201d said MiHCM Group CEO Harsha Purasinghe.\n\nFrom their personalised dashboard, learners can browse the course catalogue, track their progress, and resume learning already underway. Video, audio, and text content are brought together in a unified course player. Learners can view transcripts and jump to the corresponding moment in video or audio.\n\nAssessments are built into the learning journey rather than sitting outside it. Supported question types are evaluated automatically, and configurable feedback and explanations help learners understand their results. Learners can access every certificate they have earned, and certificate verification details can be shared so that their achievements can be confirmed."
  },
