    "description": "Democrats win control of the House of Representatives with a vow to combat Trump",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/international/Democrats-win-control-of-the-House-of-Representatives-with-a-vow-to-combat-Trump/107-354193",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1793857227.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-05-dailymirrorlk-b6f2c32b-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "311b4700222d98ac5bb232feecbe6673",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1925,
    "chunk_text": "Democrats win control of the House of Representatives with a vow to combat Trump\n\nNBC NEWS - Democrats won control of the House of Representatives with what could be their largest majority in nearly two decades, NBC News projects, as voters delivered a stunning rebuke to President Donald Trump and Republicans.\n\nThe House projection is based on an analysis that Democrats will win about 255 House seats \u2014 an estimate that could still tick up or down by a few seats but will be well beyond the 218 needed to secure a majority.\n\nNBC News has projected the Democrats will also flip control of the Senate, putting them in charge of both chambers.\n\nDemocrats needed to win a net of just three seats to take back the majority. The blue wave washed over many more GOP-held seats than that \u2014 from the East Coast to Texas\u2019 Rio Grande Valley \u2014 most in districts that Trump carried in 2024.\n\nA quartet of GOP incumbents in Pennsylvania were defeated. Democrat Bob Harvie beat GOP Rep. Brian Fitzpatrick, a leader of the bipartisan Problem Solvers Caucus; Democrat Bob Brooks knocked off GOP Rep. Ryan Mackenzie in the 7th Congressional District; Paige Cognetti bested GOP Rep. Rob Bresnahan in the 8th District; and Democrat Janelle Stelson ousted GOP Rep. Scott Perry, a former chairman of the far-right Freedom Caucus, in the 10th District.\n\nIn Virginia, Democratic former Rep. Elaine Luria won back her old seat, defeating Republican Rep. Jen Kiggans in the Virginia Beach area, while Democrat Shannon Taylor upset longtime GOP Rep. Rob Wittman outside Richmond.\n\nAnother big name in Republican politics, Rep. Tom Kean Jr. of New Jersey, lost his race for re-election to Democrat Rebecca Bennett. Rep. Victoria Spartz, R-Ind., the first Ukrainian-born member of Congress, who frequently clashed with Trump and GOP leaders, also was defeated. And in Colorado, Democratic state Rep. Manny Rutinel trounced GOP Rep. Gabe Evans."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-05-dailymirrorlk-b6f2c32b",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-b6f2c32b",
    "date_str": "2026-11-05",
    "description": "Democrats win control of the House of Representatives with a vow to combat Trump",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/international/Democrats-win-control-of-the-House-of-Representatives-with-a-vow-to-combat-Trump/107-354193",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1793857227.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-05-dailymirrorlk-b6f2c32b-0001",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "03d9192e0b104bc8c65c605f4ef63bec",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1956,
    "chunk_text": "Another big name in Republican politics, Rep. Tom Kean Jr. of New Jersey, lost his race for re-election to Democrat Rebecca Bennett. Rep. Victoria Spartz, R-Ind., the first Ukrainian-born member of Congress, who frequently clashed with Trump and GOP leaders, also was defeated. And in Colorado, Democratic state Rep. Manny Rutinel trounced GOP Rep. Gabe Evans.\n\nThe Democrats\u2019 victory was widely seen as a referendum on Trump\u2019s unpopular policies, including his tough immigration crackdown, the eight-month Iran war and tariffs on U.S. allies that drove up the prices of gas, groceries and other goods.\n\nWhen the party takes control of the chamber on Jan. 3, it will be the first time in Trump\u2019s second term that he won\u2019t have full control of Congress.\n\nSince he returned to the White House, Trump has tested the limits of his executive powers, dismantling federal agencies through the Department of Government Efficiency, unilaterally imposing sweeping tariffs and rescinding congressionally approved funding \u2014 all while the GOP-controlled House and Senate mostly looked the other way.\n\nThe House Democratic leader, Rep. Hakeem Jeffries of New York, who barnstormed across the country in the final weeks of the campaign, is expected to make history on Jan. 3 when he is sworn in as the first Black speaker of the House.\n\nHe walked into his election night watch party to raucous cheers as the rap song \u201cUnbelievable,\u201d by the Notorious B.I.G., played on the speakers. The midterm results show the \u201cAmerican people are crying out for transformational change,\u201d Jeffries told supporters.\n\n\u201cToday begins the great American comeback. The American people have spoken all across the land, in the North, in the South, in the East, in the West, in the Midwest, from sea to shining sea. The American people have spoken and made clear they\u2019ve had enough of the extremism, enough of the corruption,\u201d Jeffries said at the gathering in Washington."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-05-dailymirrorlk-b6f2c32b",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-b6f2c32b",
    "date_str": "2026-11-05",
    "description": "Democrats win control of the House of Representatives with a vow to combat Trump",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/international/Democrats-win-control-of-the-House-of-Representatives-with-a-vow-to-combat-Trump/107-354193",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1793857227.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-05-dailymirrorlk-b6f2c32b-0002",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "8053dc678e920a0430ddacbd91f15b6f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1814,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cToday begins the great American comeback. The American people have spoken all across the land, in the North, in the South, in the East, in the West, in the Midwest, from sea to shining sea. The American people have spoken and made clear they\u2019ve had enough of the extremism, enough of the corruption,\u201d Jeffries said at the gathering in Washington.\n\nWith their new majority, Democrats will take control of House committees, gaining subpoena power and the ability to conduct oversight investigations of Trump\u2019s administration, family and business ventures. That could take up considerable time and resources for Trump and his allies, forcing uncomfortable public hearings or prompting legal showdowns over subpoenas.\n\nAnd in a callback to Trump\u2019s first term, some Democrats have vowed to impeach him for a third time, though there is an internal debate about whether that\u2019s the right political path.\n\nJeffries told NBC News\u2019 \u201cMeet the Press\u201d that Democrats \u201chaven\u2019t ruled anything in and we haven\u2019t ruled anything out\u201d on impeachment.\n\nRep. Robert Garcia, D-Calif., now poised to become chairman of the powerful Oversight Committee in January, said his panel plans to focus on \u201cTrump family corruption,\u201d including Trump\u2019s cryptocurrency ventures, which have earned him more than $1 billion. The panel will also scrutinize \u201cabuses\u201d by ICE and the Department of Homeland Security, corporate corruption and the Jeffrey Epstein files.\n\nAside from investigative power, House Democrats will also command the ability to pass legislation with a simple majority. Jeffries has said Democrats would focus on four areas: reversing Trump\u2019s cuts to Medicaid, extending the Affordable Care Act credits, restoring congressional authority related to tariffs and stopping Trump\u2019s war with Iran."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-05-dailymirrorlk-b6f2c32b",
