    "chunk_size_bytes": 1153,
    "chunk_text": "Trump fired the first shot in the summer of 2025, when he urged GOP allies in Texas to redraw their congressional lines to help the party pick up as many as five seats. Republicans also redrew maps in places like Florida, North Carolina, Tennessee, Alabama, Louisiana and Missouri in a bid to win more seats.\n\nWhile the GOP successfully picked up a handful of majority-Black, Democratic-held seats in the South, the Supreme Court blocked Missouri Republicans\u2019 new congressional map, essentially preserving the Kansas City seat of longtime Democratic Rep. Emanuel Cleaver.\n\n\u201cWe made a promise to aggressively push back against the MAGA extremist effort to rip the election away from the American people by gerrymandering the possibility of Democrats winning the majority out of existence,\u201d Jeffries said before the election, adding that the redistricting wars will continue in the 120th Congress.\n\n\u201cThis fight is not over; we\u2019ve just gotten started,\u201d he added. \u201cIt will continue into the next Congress until we pass legislation signed into law by a future president that will prohibit mid-decade gerrymandering from ever happening again.\u201d"
