    "md5": "433752365675c21bc2235fa69f9d9bac",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1866,
    "chunk_text": "Food earnings lift Harischandra Mills\u2019 September-quarter profit\n\nHarischandra Mills PLC reported a 23 percent rise in group net profit for the September quarter, supported by higher food earnings and a return to profit in fuel and lubricants, although the rising costs squeezed the gross margins and the losses widened at its soap business.\n\nProfit after tax increased to Rs.59.8 million in the three months ended September 30, 2026, from Rs.48.4 million a year earlier. The earnings per share rose to Rs.31.14, from Rs.25.24.\n\nRevenue grew 25 percent to Rs.2.08 billion but the cost of sales increased faster, rising 27 percent to Rs.1.73 billion. Consequently, the gross profit rose a more modest 14 percent to Rs.342.2 million, with the gross margin narrowing to 16.5 percent, from 18.1 percent.\n\nThe food business remained the main earnings contributor. The quarterly revenue increased 14 percent to Rs.1.39 billion, while the segment operating profit rose 31 percent to Rs.66.5 million, from Rs.50.9 million.\n\nThe fuel and lubricant revenue more than doubled to Rs.500.2 million, from Rs.247.7 million, accounting for about 62 percent of the increase in the group quarterly revenue. The segment recorded an operating profit of Rs.2.1 million, reversing a loss of Rs.95,000 a year earlier.\n\nHowever, the soap business continued to weigh on the earnings. Revenue fell 8 percent to Rs.188.4 million, while its operating loss widened to Rs.9.7 million, from Rs.4.1 million.\n\nAt group level, the selling and distribution expenses increased 28 percent to Rs.144.3 million, outpacing the revenue growth. The administrative expenses declined 2 percent to Rs.139 million, providing some relief.\n\nThe operating profit, including other income, increased 21 percent to Rs.86.6 million. Other income contributed Rs.27.7 million, compared with Rs.25 million a year earlier."
  },
