    "chunk_text": "At group level, the selling and distribution expenses increased 28 percent to Rs.144.3 million, outpacing the revenue growth. The administrative expenses declined 2 percent to Rs.139 million, providing some relief.\n\nThe operating profit, including other income, increased 21 percent to Rs.86.6 million. Other income contributed Rs.27.7 million, compared with Rs.25 million a year earlier.\n\nProfit before tax rose 15 percent to Rs.93.4 million. A smaller 2 percent increase in the tax charge to Rs.33.6 million helped the net profit grow faster than the pre-tax earnings.\n\nFor the six months ended September 30, the group net profit increased 77 percent to Rs.151.6 million, while revenue rose 28 percent to Rs.4 billion. The earnings per share advanced to Rs.78.99, from Rs.44.65.\n\nThe half-year food segment operating profit rose to Rs.149.8 million, from Rs.86.8 million. Fuel and lubricants contributed Rs.4.3 million, against a loss of Rs.380,000, while the soap segment\u2019s loss widened to Rs.12.4 million, from Rs.3.7 million.\n\nThe net cash generated from the operating activities increased to Rs.206.9 million, from Rs.49 million. The spending on the property, plant and equipment totalled Rs.222.6 million, up from Rs.160.3 million.\n\nThe bank overdrafts declined to Rs.100.7 million at end-September, from Rs.262.9 million at end-March. The fixed deposits also fell to Rs.315.7 million, from Rs.634 million."
