    "chunk_text": "BOC\u2019s historic debenture issue oversubscribed 3.8 times on opening day\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s leading state-owned bank, Bank of Ceylon (BOC), successfully closed its historic Basel III-compliant Tier 2 debenture issue, being oversubscribed 3.8 times over its initial issue of Rs.10 billion on the opening day, November 3, 2026.\n\nThe bank issued 100 million Basel III-compliant Tier 2, listed, rated, unsecured, subordinated, redeemable debentures, with non-viability write-down features, at an issue price of Rs.100 each, to raise up to Rs.10 billion, with options to increase the amount up to Rs.20 billion and subsequently to Rs.30 billion in the event of oversubscription.\n\nThe bank received applications exceeding Rs.38 billion, making it the largest-ever listed debenture issue in Sri Lanka\u2019s capital market history.\n\nBOC Chairman Kavinda de Zoysa said, \u201cOversubscription of this landmark issuance on the opening day itself reflects the strong confidence placed by our investors in BOC\u2019s financial strength, resilience and governance.\u00a0 With a legacy spanning more than eight decades, BOC has operated at the centre of Sri Lanka\u2019s financial ecosystem, supporting national development while adapting to changing economic and social realities. BOC continues to lead and set new benchmarks for others to follow.\n\nThe funds raised through this issuance will be utilised to fuel productivity-driven sectors that will define the nation\u2019s future. We are deeply grateful to all our investors for their enthusiastic participation in this landmark issuance to support a stronger and more resilient nation.\u201d\n\nAs Sri Lanka\u2019s largest domestic systemically important bank, BOC\u2019s responsibilities extend well beyond traditional banking. Serving more than 16 million customers, from individuals to large corporates, the bank plays a pivotal role in advancing Sri Lanka\u2019s economic progress and social well-being."
