    "chunk_text": "As Sri Lanka\u2019s largest domestic systemically important bank, BOC\u2019s responsibilities extend well beyond traditional banking. Serving more than 16 million customers, from individuals to large corporates, the bank plays a pivotal role in advancing Sri Lanka\u2019s economic progress and social well-being.\n\nMobilising capital towards productive sectors will undoubtedly contribute towards achieving inclusive and sustainable economic growth. We remain dedicated to delivering an exceptional banking experience to all our stakeholders, ensuring growth and reliability for all who place their trust in us.\u201d\n\nThe Investment Banking Division of BOC served as the manager and registrar to this landmark Basel III-compliant debenture issue, while the bank\u2019s Legal Division acted as the lawyer to the issue.\n\nThe successful execution of this large-scale capital market transaction demonstrates BOC\u2019s extensive in-house expertise, institutional capabilities and commitment to developing Sri Lanka\u2019s debt capital market.\n\nThe Basel III-compliant debentures were assigned a rating of AA (Stable) by Lanka Rating Agency Limited.\n\nBOC is a corporate finance advisor licensed by the Securities and Exchange Commission of Sri Lanka (SEC). The bank\u2019s corporate finance advisory unit, coming under the Investment Banking Division, offers a comprehensive suite of advisory services that extend beyond traditional banking, including financial advisory for listed and unlisted debt issues such as debentures, perpetual bonds, GSS+ bonds and equity transactions.\n\nThe Rs.20 billion Basel III-compliant Tier II sustainability bond, structured and managed by the corporate finance advisory unit in 2025, received international recognition at the Environmental Finance\u2019s Sustainable Debt Awards 2026, winning the award for Innovation, Sustainability Bond Structure in Asia and the Pacific."
