    "chunk_size_bytes": 691,
    "chunk_text": "Earlier this year, Sri Lanka also ratified the International Labour Organisation\u2019s (ILO\u2019s) Violence and Harassment Convention, 2019 (No. 190), the first international treaty dedicated to eliminating violence and harassment, including gender-based harassment, in the world of work. In doing so, the Government committed itself to introducing the domestic legal provisions needed to give the Convention effect. I welcome that ratification wholeheartedly.\n\nWe need not look to distant shores for answers. Several of our Asian neighbours, with legal traditions and social pressures not unlike our own, have already travelled this road. Their experience offers both encouragement and caution."
