    "chunk_text": "The ruling also detailed an incident at work in April this year where Tamburella fractured bones in his right hand when he struck a metal hand rail.\n\nTamburella had been hoping the restaurant would sponsor a visa for him that allows skilled workers to be permanent residents.\n\nHe lost his unfair dismissal claim on the grounds that the application had been filed too late, according to the ruling.\n\nThe restaurant's managing director, Elliot Ingram, told the Daily Mail there was \"more to this story than a pizza topping\".\n\nOn the chef's LinkedIn profile, he describes himself as someone who, throughout his career, has focused on \"delivering exceptional food\" and \"improving business performance\".\n\nThree months ago he posted a \"letter for chefs\" with the theme \"respecting the ingredients\".\n\nThe LinkedIn profile states he now works at another Brisbane restaurant. A BBC check has found that pineapple is not on that restaurant's menu."
