    "chunk_size_bytes": 1999,
    "chunk_text": "Cancer radiation machine tender faces conflict of interest allegations\n\nColombo, Nov. 5 (Daily Mirror) - The procurement of cancer radiation therapy machines for the Apeksha Cancer Hospital and the Galle National Hospital has come under fresh scrutiny following allegations of conflicts of interest involving suppliers and government officials.\n\nConsultant Physician Dr. Chamal Sanjeewa has called for an independent investigation into the tender process, claiming that medical physicists involved in evaluating the bids had attended a promotional event organised by a company linked to one of the suppliers just nine days before the scheduled opening of tenders.\n\nThe procurement involves Linear Accelerator (Linac) machines funded through an Asian Development Bank (ADB) loan scheme.\n\nDr. Sanjeewa has also questioned the proposed purchase of a 17-year-old Linac model, warning that Sri Lanka could end up with outdated equipment for cancer treatment.\n\nAccording to information presented by Dr. Sanjeewa, the Government Medical Physicists' Association (GMPA) held its Annual General Meeting at the Taj Samudra Hotel in Colombo on June 14, 2026.\n\nAn international representative of the company manufacturing the radiation equipment in question had delivered a promotional presentation at the meeting. The event was sponsored by the company's local agent.\n\nThe presentation took place just nine days before the scheduled opening of tenders on June 23 for cancer treatment equipment for the Apeksha Cancer Hospital and the Galle National Hospital.\n\nDr. Sanjeewa claimed that medical physicists expected to serve on the Technical Evaluation Committees (TECs) for the same tenders had also attended the meeting.\n\nHe questioned the participation of officials responsible for evaluating the bids in a promotional event organised by a company linked to a potential supplier while the tender process was underway.\n\nHe said such contact could affect the independence and fairness of the procurement process."
  },
