    "chunk_size_bytes": 1477,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lankan High Commissioner presents credentials to Botswana President\n\nColombo, Nov. 5 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lanka\u2019s High Commissioner to Botswana, Air Chief Marshal Udeni Rajapaksa (Retd), has presented his Letters of Credence to Botswana President Advocate Duma Gideon Boko at a ceremony held at the President\u2019s Office in Gaborone on November 3.\n\nRajapaksa, who is based in Pretoria, South Africa, conveyed the greetings and best wishes of Sri Lankan President Anura Kumara Dissanayake to President Boko.\n\nHe reaffirmed Sri Lanka\u2019s commitment to strengthening bilateral relations and cooperation with Botswana.\n\nDuring the meeting, Rajapaksa highlighted opportunities to expand cooperation in trade, investment, education, tourism, capacity-building and people-to-people exchanges.\n\nHe also briefed the Botswana President on Sri Lanka\u2019s recent economic developments, recovery efforts and sustainable development initiatives.\n\nThe discussions also focused on cooperation between the two countries at international forums, including the United Nations, the Commonwealth and the Group of 77.\n\nPresident Boko welcomed the new High Commissioner and expressed Botswana\u2019s willingness to strengthen relations with Sri Lanka.\n\nBoth sides also discussed the importance of South-South cooperation in addressing common challenges and promoting peace, prosperity and sustainable development.\n\nRajapaksa served in the Sri Lanka Air Force for 37 years and was its 19th Commander."
