    "chunk_size_bytes": 1873,
    "chunk_text": "Court orders three-month suspension of Rakhitha Rajapaksa\u2019s bank accounts, vehicles\n\nColombo, Nov. 5 (Daily Mirror) - Colombo High Court Judge Ruwan Dissanayake today ordered the suspension of bank accounts and three vehicles belonging to lawyer Rakhitha Rajapaksa, which had been frozen by the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption, for a period of three months.\n\nThe order was issued by the Colombo High Court after considering a request by the Bribery Commission.\n\nLawyer Rakhitha Rajapaksa, the suspect in the case, was also present before the court when the matter was taken up.\n\nMaking submissions on behalf of the Bribery Commission, an Assistant Director General of the Commission informed court that an investigation had been initiated into an alleged incident in which a bribe of Rs. 120 million had been obtained from the wife of detained alleged underworld drug kingpin Harak Kata, alias Nadun Chinthaka Wickramaratne, in Dubai.\n\nThe alleged bribe was reportedly obtained in exchange for ensuring his safety and facilitating his transfer to a secure prison.\n\nShe further stated that investigations had revealed information regarding bank accounts and three vehicles belonging to Rakhitha Rajapaksa, and that further inquiries had been conducted in this regard.\n\nBased on the findings, sufficient grounds had been established to conduct an investigation against the suspect under the Proceeds of Crime Act No. 5 of 2025, she said.\n\nAccordingly, the Bribery Commission had taken steps on October 29 to freeze the relevant bank accounts and vehicles under the provisions of the Act, she informed court.\n\nThe Assistant Director General requested the court to issue an order suspending the relevant bank accounts and vehicles for a period of three months in terms of the provisions of the Anti-Corruption Act and the Proceeds of Crime Act."
