    "chunk_text": "The Assistant Director General requested the court to issue an order suspending the relevant bank accounts and vehicles for a period of three months in terms of the provisions of the Anti-Corruption Act and the Proceeds of Crime Act.\n\nHowever, no such evidence had been produced before court at this stage, he argued. He also pointed out that the bank accounts in question had been opened before the alleged offence took place.\n\nIn response, the Assistant Director General of the Bribery Commission informed court that Section 75 of the Proceeds of Crime Act empowered the court to issue an order suspending such assets.\n\nHaving considered the submissions made by both parties, the Judge observed that there was no legal impediment to issuing such an order under the provisions of the Proceeds of Crime Act.\n\nAccordingly, the Judge ordered the suspension of the relevant bank accounts and vehicles for a period of three months.\n\nThe Judge further directed that preservation orders be communicated to the banks where the relevant accounts are maintained and to the Commissioner General of Motor Traffic in respect of the vehicles and related assets."
