    "md5": "d562134f387a46306ec6c5ebdc69b0ec",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1917,
    "chunk_text": "Musk has little to show for his record spending on Republican campaigns in US midterms\n\nReuters\u00a0- Elon Musk spent nearly half a billion dollars on the US midterm elections, but the record expenditure yielded little for the world's \u200brichest man and leader of SpaceX (SPCX.O) and Tesla (TSLA.O).\n\nJust three of the 43 Republicans Musk backed for the House of Representatives won on Tuesday night, compared to 33 who lost. The \u200cremaining seven races had not been called by late Wednesday, though Democrats are running ahead in tallies so far.\n\nOf the seven Senate Republican candidates Musk backed, six lost and one race hangs in the balance. In that last race, Alaska, Democrat Mary Peltola is narrowly ahead with 77% of votes counted.\n\nIn Texas, where SpaceX and Tesla are headquartered and where Musk plans a chipmaking venture, Musk also came up empty after spending almost $230 million on the Senate contest, $5 million on the governor's race, and $500,000 \u200bon the lieutenant governor vote.\n\n\"A lot of Democrats see him as the Mr. Money Bags for their Republican opponents and that\u2019s certainly going to color how they\u2019re going to treat him personally,\" \u200bsaid David Hopkins, political science professor at Boston College. \"He\u2019s particularly at risk because he\u2019s been part of the Trump administration and his companies have direct government involvement.\"\n\nShares \u2060of SpaceX and Tesla fell 3.9% and 3.3% respectively on Wednesday on investor concerns that a Democratic-controlled Congress would tighten scrutiny of Musk's Starlink satellite service and his AI data center projects.\n\nMusk's outsized donations, which helped drive \u200bspending in this election cycle to a new record, have provoked the ire of Democrats who have said investigations into Musk and his businesses topped their agenda. With their newfound power, Democrats say they are adding campaign finance \u200breform to their wish list."
  },
