    "chunk_text": "Musk's outsized donations, which helped drive \u200bspending in this election cycle to a new record, have provoked the ire of Democrats who have said investigations into Musk and his businesses topped their agenda. With their newfound power, Democrats say they are adding campaign finance \u200breform to their wish list.\n\nMusk's political action committee, America PAC, \u200band his attorney Alex Spiro did not respond to requests for comment.\n\nSpending in recent elections has surged with the rise of super PACs, which can take unlimited donations from wealthy individuals and corporations \u200band spend on campaigns with few restrictions.\n\nPolitical advertising tracker AdImpact said the Texas Senate contest was the most expensive US non-presidential race ever, with roughly $573.2 million in total spending.\n\n\"We've just sent a message to every millionaire mega donor, to every \u200ctrillionaire mega \u2060donor, every corrupt defender of this broken political system. In this state, in this country, power belongs to the people,\" US Senator-elect James Talarico said in his acceptance speech late Tuesday in Austin, Texas.\n\nThe Democrat, whom Musk targeted with $153.5 million worth of attack ads, compared himself and Musk to the biblical David and Goliath, saying: \"Tonight we beat Goliath.\"\n\nDemocratic candidates significantly outraised Republicans with small-dollar donations, making Republicans more dependent on wealthy donors. Billionaire Michael Bloomberg donated $80 million to Democrats in the last weeks of the race.\n\nIncoming Texas Governor Gina Hinojosa, who beat Republican Governor Greg Abbott, indicated this year that she would challenge Musk's close relationship with the state if elected.\n\n\"Abbott gave \u200bcontrol of our Boca Chica Beach to the highest \u200bbidder. That beach is our inheritance,\" she \u2060said. SpaceX launches rockets from Boca Chica Beach in South Texas."
