    "chunk_text": "Incoming Texas Governor Gina Hinojosa, who beat Republican Governor Greg Abbott, indicated this year that she would challenge Musk's close relationship with the state if elected.\n\n\"Abbott gave \u200bcontrol of our Boca Chica Beach to the highest \u200bbidder. That beach is our inheritance,\" she \u2060said. SpaceX launches rockets from Boca Chica Beach in South Texas.\n\n\u201cThis lawsuit is a baseless stunt and nothing more than an act of desperation,\u201d Abbott's press secretary Andrew Mahaleris said on X.\n\nThe incoming chair of the House Committee on Oversight and Government Reform, US Representative Robert Garcia, a California Democrat, plans \u200bto introduce legislation closing the \"Musk loophole,\" \u2060referring to a provision in campaign finance law that allows individual executives to spend unlimited personal money on political campaigns, even though their companies are banned from doing so.\n\nDemocrats are expected to open a flurry of congressional investigations scrutinizing Musk's companies, their contracts, his work running the Department of Government Efficiency, involvement in Ukraine and contact with Russia.\n\nSome inquiries have already begun. Democrats on House and Senate investigative committees wrote to SpaceX, the Department of Defense and \u2060White House \u200blast month, looking into the company's restriction of its Starlink satellite system in Ukraine during a critical time in its war against \u200bRussia. Others have questioned Musk on AI chatbot Grok's dissemination of sexualized images of women and children, conflicts of interest while he ran DOGE, and SpaceX's federal contracts with NASA and the Defense Department.\n\nEarly on Wednesday, as the election results became clear, Musk posted on \u200bX: \"Guess my election-interfering space lasers didn\u2019t work this time.\""
