    "chunk_size_bytes": 2034,
    "chunk_text": "Comedian Russell Brand found guilty by UK court of rape and sexual assaults\n\nReuters - British comedian and actor Russell Brand was found guilty in a London court on Thursday of rape and sexual assaults, and told he faces a \u200blengthy jail sentence.\n\nBrand, once one of Britain's most high-profile broadcasters and the former husband \u200cof US singer Katy Perry, had denied the accusations, saying the incidents had either been consensual, reinvented or re-imagined.\n\nProsecutors had described the 51-year-old, who starred in the films \"Get Him to the Greek\" and \"Arthur\", as a ruthless sexual predator.\n\nHe was \u200bconvicted at London's Southwark Crown Court of one count of rape and three sexual assaults. \u200bHe was acquitted of two other rape charges and an attempted indecent assault.\n\nJudge \u2060Joel Bennathan said he would be sentenced on Monday and faced a lengthy prison term. Brand \u200bwas taken down to the cells ahead of a bail application at 1500 GMT.\n\nProsecutors said the charges, \u200bbetween 1999 and 2009 spanned the years in which Brand rose from performing stand-up comedy in small venues to becoming a television presenter and Hollywood film star.\n\nThe court heard tearful and forceful testimony from the six complainants, who are \u200ball entitled to lifelong anonymity. None of the women knew each other but all came forward \u200bto police in the wake of a TV documentary and press reports in 2023 in which anonymous allegations were \u200cmade by \u2060other women.\n\nThe most graphic evidence related to the rape for which he was convicted which took place in 2009, involving a victim who had met Brand after a gig where she had engaged in a sexual encounter in his dressing room.\n\nShe recounted how days later she had gone to his \u200bhome where during consensual sex, \u200bhe had anally \u2060raped her. Afterwards he had told her to clear up the blood and mess, she said.\n\nHe was convicted of sexual assaulting a woman at a \u200bLondon bar in 2004, when the victim said he had approached her at \u200ba party \u2060and grabbed her breasts."
