    "chunk_size_bytes": 1151,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka wins Luxury Food Destination award in UK\n\nColombo, Nov. 5 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lanka has won the \u2018Luxury Food Destination of the Year\u2019 award at the Travel & Taste Awards 2026 held in the United Kingdom.\n\nThe award was presented by Chief Organiser of the Travel & Taste Awards, Alex Crosley, at Sri Lanka\u2019s tourism promotion stand during the World Travel Market exhibition.\n\nDeputy Minister of Tourism Prof. Ruwan Ranasinghe accepted the award on behalf of the Sri Lankan people.\n\nThe Travel & Taste Awards recognise leading food-related travel experiences and destinations across 17 categories. Winners are selected by a panel of food and travel experts.\n\nThe judges highlighted Sri Lanka\u2019s growing number of boutique hotel groups, its vibrant culinary scene and the use of local produce in its food offerings.\n\nThe recognition is expected to strengthen Sri Lanka\u2019s position as a luxury food and travel destination and support efforts to attract more international tourists seeking quality dining and unique travel experiences.\n\nThe award also recognises the island\u2019s diverse cuisine, traditional flavours and rich food heritage."
