    "chunk_size_bytes": 942,
    "chunk_text": "His decision not to include Putin in next year's gathering in Manchester comes after European diplomats refused to stand for an official photo with Russia's Foreign Minister Sergei Lavrov at the G20 Foreign Ministers' Meeting in October.\n\nThe so-called \"family photo\" would usually include representatives from all nations in attendance, but this year it was cancelled.\n\nDiscussing Ukraine, UK Foreign Secretary Ed Miliband later told Lavrov at the summit: \"Let me say this directly to the Russian foreign minister: We all know who the aggressor in this war is.\"\n\nThe UK last hosted the G20 summit in 2009. Next year's two-day event will take place in the Manchester Central Convention Centre in Manchester city centre and host thousands of diplomats and delegates, as well as world leaders.\n\nThe government has said it will use its G20 presidency in 2027 to \"reinforce global economic stability\" and \"benefit people in every part of the UK\"."
