    "md5": "1ba9b8c54533fe117457c4c56ff2d55c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1421,
    "chunk_text": "The result was a blue tsunami that the Democratic leadership was scarcely prepared to handle. Voters will find out in the coming months whether the party respects the mandate and delivers on its promises.\n\nTrump and Netanyahu thought the Iranians would surrender and that regime change would occur within days, but the Iranians proved themselves a warrior nation determined to fight to the last. The war is now in its ninth month. Given Trump\u2019s unpredictability and Netanyahu\u2019s sinister designs, it is too early to say that the anti-war message of the election results will end the Iran war just as public opposition helped bring an end to the Vietnam War in 1975.\n\nDays before the midterms, renowned podcaster Tucker Carlson claimed in a lengthy post that Trump was being prodded by Netanyahu to drop a nuclear weapon on Iran\u2019s Pickaxe Mountain. The mountain is believed to house a secret nuclear facility built by the Islamic Republic to hide a stockpile of enriched uranium. The likely date for the attack was November 7.\n\nIn post-election statements, Trump claimed that the war was in the interest of the American people, even though they did not understand its long-term benefits. But the war served the billionaire class rather than ordinary Americans. In a display of indifference to the high grocery and fuel prices that people were paying, Trump bragged that the war had made American oil companies richer."
  },
