    "md5": "1f44cdd1a991b3c97d6e9ace6d1b3510",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1959,
    "chunk_text": "AIPAC remains as influential as ever. In a message posted on X, the group congratulated \u201cthe hundreds of pro-Israel Democrats and Republicans who won the election.\u201d It said that 234 candidates it supported had won. Among them were Democratic Party heavyweights Chuck Schumer and Hakeem Jeffries. The latter is expected to become Speaker of the House, the third-highest office in the line of succession after the President and Vice President.\n\nThe progressives, whom Trump derided as communists, have now established themselves as a force to be reckoned with in US politics, not only within the Democratic Party but also across sections of the Republican Party. Years ago, it was nearly impossible for an American politician to openly adopt a pro-Palestinian stance. Today, however, pro-Palestinian views can help win elections.\n\nDemocrat James Talarico, who condemned Netanyahu over the Gaza massacre, would once have been a non-starter in a Texas primary. Instead, he went on to win the Senate race. \u201cI\u2019ve never taken money from AIPAC, and I\u2019m not taking money from AIPAC in this campaign. Seeing what\u2019s happening in Gaza makes me sick to my stomach as a teacher, as a Christian, as a human being. I screamed at God for the starving children until I realised the starving children were God screaming at me,\u201d he said in a pre-election interview. Who would have imagined, even in their wildest dreams at the start of the election campaign, that Abdulrahman El Sayed, an American of Egyptian origin, would win the Michigan Senate race?\n\nThe obstacles he faced were formidable. Haley Stevens, the politician he defeated to secure the Democratic Party nomination in the primary, abandoned the party and backed El Sayed\u2019s Republican rival, Kim Rogers. Hardly a day passed without Trump and Republican leaders accusing him of being a terrorist sympathiser linked to the Muslim Brotherhood, an organisation banned in Egypt and several Arab countries."
