    "md5": "ac4e930f01fac96aa3dc69ab404563e4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1767,
    "chunk_text": "Trump\u2019s midterm rout: A lesson in the limits of a superpower\n\nThe U.S. elections and subsequent policy decisions will therefore have a bearing on Sri Lanka, particularly in trade, investment, energy security and foreign relations\n\nPeople across the world were glued to the media to see the outcome of the U.S. midterm elections. The United States, as the global economic powerhouse with unmatched military might, can make an impact across the world with just a stroke of the pen. The Israeli-U.S. war on Iran left countries such as Sri Lanka reeling, with little choice in the matter. It was a bitter experience. President Donald Trump was tested for his actions at the midterm elections. What happened to his party was not merely a defeat but a rout.\n\nDemocrats took control of both chambers of Congress, in what amounted to an astounding humiliation for a president whose political brand is built around the projection of power.\n\nTwo years ago, retaking the House looked like a genuine fight for Democrats, while the Senate appeared a long shot. However, the election results turned the political landscape upside down, with Democrats securing a majority in the Senate and comfortably taking the House. This was a major setback for a president who had sought to consolidate his political authority after returning to office.\n\nThe outcome is a reminder that even the most powerful political leaders are not immune to the verdict of the electorate. Trump, who often projects himself as a leader capable of bending institutions to his will, has been confronted with the reality of the American constitutional system. Congress has an important role in overseeing the administration, controlling public expenditure and scrutinising decisions relating to war and peace."
  },
