    "chunk_text": "The implications are not confined to the United States. In an increasingly interconnected world, decisions taken in Washington can reverberate across continents. The conflict involving Iran, Israel and the United States demonstrated how quickly a regional war could turn into a global economic crisis. Disruptions to energy supplies and shipping through the Strait of Hormuz sent shockwaves through international markets. Countries dependent on imported fuel, including Sri Lanka, were particularly vulnerable. They had to contend with rising import costs, pressure on foreign exchange reserves and the prospect of renewed inflation, despite having little influence over the decisions that led to the crisis.\n\nThe U.S. elections and subsequent policy decisions will therefore have a bearing on Sri Lanka, particularly in trade, investment, energy security and foreign relations.\n\nThere is also the geopolitical dimension. Washington\u2019s relations with China and India and its policies towards the Indian Ocean will remain important considerations for Colombo.\n\nIt is easier said than done. Sri Lanka has to learn from such experiences, strengthen its economic resilience and pursue a balanced and independent foreign policy. It cannot allow its national interests to become hostage to the political calculations of powerful countries."
