    "language": "en",
    "md5": "6d3fd9bc850acda03d5e400bb2bb7ed7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1903,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s High Commissioner-designate to Kenya Dhammika Fernando assumes duties\n\nHigh Commissioner-designate of Sri Lanka to the Republic of Kenya, Dhammika Fernando\n\nHigh Commissioner-designate of Sri Lanka to the Republic of Kenya, Dhammika Fernando, assumed duties at the Sri Lanka High Commission in Nairobi on 2 November 2026.\n\nAddressing the Mission\u2019s staff, High Commissioner-designate Fernando outlined his vision for advancing Sri Lanka\u2019s interests through purposeful diplomacy, practical economic engagement and responsive public service. He identified three principal priorities: representing Sri Lanka with dignity and delivering results; placing economic diplomacy at the forefront of the Mission\u2019s work; and building a professional, accountable and united team.\n\nHighlighting opportunities for closer cooperation between Sri Lanka and Kenya, he emphasised the importance of expanding trade, promoting tourism, facilitating investment in both directions and connecting businesses with potential partners. He expressed his commitment to making the Mission an active facilitator of opportunities that would generate tangible benefits for both countries.\n\nFernando also underscored the importance of safeguarding the welfare of Sri Lankans and providing efficient, courteous and accessible consular services. He noted the Mission\u2019s wider responsibilities across its countries of concurrent accreditation and Sri Lanka\u2019s engagement with the United Nations Environment Programme (UNEP) and the United Nations Human Settlements Programme (UN-Habitat).\n\nAcknowledging the staff\u2019s contribution to sustaining the Mission\u2019s work, he stressed that professionalism, integrity, accountability, teamwork and loyalty to Sri Lanka would guide its collective efforts. He pledged a consultative approach to leadership, grounded in mutual respect and a shared commitment to national service."
