    "chunk_size_bytes": 1866,
    "chunk_text": "President warns of \u2018shadow State\u2019 as narcotic seizures reach Rs. 224 b\n\nPresident Anura Kumara Dissanayake yesterday has warned that a powerful \u201cshadow State\u201d has emerged within Sri Lanka, with drug traffickers and organised criminal networks allegedly using their financial resources to influence politicians, law enforcement officers, public officials and State institutions.\n\nAddressing a religious summit at Temple Trees to mark the first anniversary of the Government\u2019s national anti-drug operation, the President said an underground criminal network had developed alongside the legitimate State machinery, posing a serious threat to the country\u2019s future.\n\nHe said drug traffickers had accumulated enormous wealth, enabling them to infiltrate politics, influence State institutions and establish networks capable of undermining law enforcement and the rule of law.\n\nThe President said the scale of drug seizures over the past year reflected the magnitude of the illegal narcotics trade, with authorities confiscating drugs valued at approximately Rs. 218 billion, rising to Rs. 224 billion when cannabis was included.\n\nThe seizures comprised 6,528 kg of ICE (crystal methamphetamine), 4,000 kg of heroin, 1,841 kg of hashish, 314 kg of cocaine and 2,598 kg of other narcotics. Authorities had also seized nearly 4.5 million drug tablets and capsules.\n\nHe further revealed that around 150 kg of heroin and ICE had been seized earlier in the day.\n\nThe President warned that the quantities intercepted by law enforcement agencies represented only part of the illegal trade, suggesting that substantially larger volumes could be entering the market.\n\nHe said the Government\u2019s efforts were not limited to confiscating narcotics and arresting suspects, but also focused on dismantling the financial and institutional networks sustaining organised crime."
  },
