    "md5": "fbb75fc96378e4313846fc887eee88c8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1585,
    "chunk_text": "A national Budget is the Government\u2019s annual financial and economic policy statement, outlining revenue, expenditure, borrowing and development priorities. It reflects the Government\u2019s economic direction and commitment to national development. Through taxation, public spending, subsidies and investment, the Budget directly affects individuals, businesses and the wider economy\u2014shaping living costs, public services, investment, employment and economic growth. Ultimately, a Budget\u2019s success should be measured not merely by revenue collection or fiscal surpluses, but by its ability to transform public resources into tangible economic and social benefits.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s present circumstances demand a careful balance between economic discipline and public welfare.\n\nDespite improved economic stability, households continue to face financial pressures from food, transport, electricity, healthcare, education and housing costs. The cumulative impact of the economic crisis and fiscal adjustments has weakened purchasing power. Budget 2027 should therefore prioritise household affordability, improved public services and targeted social protection while maintaining fiscal sustainability.\n\nBusinesses continue to face higher taxation, compliance costs, financing constraints and operational uncertainties. Private-sector investment is vital for employment, exports, innovation and productivity. Budget 2027 should therefore promote a predictable, business-friendly environment that encourages investment, expansion, technological advancement and sustainable economic growth."
  },
