    "md5": "a5074f49e331f62baa38e6aaf4ccfe2b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1967,
    "chunk_text": "Why should people have to adapt to technology?\n\nAfter years of illness and rehabilitation, Sri Lankan author Mohamed\n\nRihazudin Razik is using his experiences to rethink how technology should work for people\n\nWe use technology almost every day. We read messages, fill in forms, make payments, attend meetings and look for information online.\n\nFor many people, these are simple tasks. We hardly give them a second thought.\n\nA person with poor eyesight may struggle to read a website. Someone with unsteady hands may find it difficult to use a mouse or a touchscreen. An older person may become confused by an application that has too many instructions. A student may need more time to read and understand a passage.\n\nWe often expect people to find a way around these difficulties.\n\nI have come to believe that we should be asking a different question.\n\nWhy can't technology make things easier for the person using it? a question that came from experience.\n\nOver the years, I underwent seven surgeries, radiotherapy, chemotherapy and a long period of rehabilitation.\n\nThere were things I had once done without thinking that became difficult. My balance was affected. Writing became a challenge. Reading and concentrating sometimes required more effort than before.\n\nI had to learn to approach many ordinary activities differently.\n\nI also came to understand how frustrating it can be when something that appears simple to another person becomes difficult for you.\n\nSometimes I needed help. At other times, I wanted the opportunity to try for myself, even if it took longer.\n\nI did not always want someone to do things for me. I wanted to be able to do as much as possible on my own.\n\nThese experiences stayed with me as I continued learning and working with technology.\n\nToday, we have software that can carry out complicated tasks in seconds. We can communicate across countries, attend classes from home and access information that once required a visit to a library."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-06-dailyftlk-7a09b8d0",
    "num": "dailyftlk-7a09b8d0",
    "date_str": "2026-11-06",
    "description": "Why should people have to adapt to technology?",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/columns/Why-should-people-have-to-adapt-to-technology/4-799700",
