    "chunk_size_bytes": 1952,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s CH17 takes proprietary SaaS technology beyond borders with Nepal expansion\n\nCH17 Founder and CEO Jumar Preena (right) with CH17 Systems Ltd., Nepal Co-Founder Vivek Thakuri\n\nHomegrown technology company seeks international recognition for Sri Lankan-developed white-label loyalty, customer intelligence and engagement solutions\n\nSri Lankan loyalty and customer engagement technology company CH17 has taken a significant step towards international expansion with the establishment of Channel17 Systems Ltd., in Nepal, marking its first overseas market operation under its own brand.\n\nThe development represents more than geographical expansion. It opens a new avenue for international recognition of Sri Lankan-developed proprietary Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) technology, particularly in the specialised fields of loyalty management, customer intelligence, digital engagement and customer value-added services.\n\nEstablished in 2013, CH17 has spent more than a decade developing technology-driven solutions for organisations across Sri Lanka\u2019s insurance, finance and leasing, apparel and retail industries.\n\nIts experience has evolved into a proprietary technology ecosystem that enables businesses to introduce customised loyalty, rewards, membership management and customer engagement programmes under their own corporate identities.\n\nCH17\u2019s international ambitions are supported by practical experience in developing and managing white-label technology solutions for established organisations operating across diverse industries.\n\nA distinguishing feature of its business model is its pioneering focus on closed and targeted customer communities, identified through demographic, firmographic and institutional relationships.\n\nThis approach enables organisations to engage specific customer groups more effectively, moving beyond conventional mass-market promotions towards relevant, measurable and sustained customer relationships."
  },
