    "md5": "79d922527d01ef3778679375d81cb057",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1779,
    "chunk_text": "The model integrates three complementary disciplines: technology infrastructure, customer intelligence and customer engagement.\n\nHowever, the company\u2019s proprietary SaaS capabilities extend beyond conventional loyalty programmes and customer value-added services.\n\nThis versatility creates opportunities for CH17\u2019s technology to be deployed across multiple sectors and international markets, with configurations tailored to local business requirements.\n\nThe company\u2019s approach combines Human Intelligence supported by Artificial Intelligence, recognising that effective customer engagement requires both technological capability and practical understanding of customer behaviour.\n\nThe establishment of Channel17 Systems Ltd., in Nepal on 30 October 2026 marks the beginning of CH17\u2019s international market development strategy.\n\nThe Nepal operation has been established with local business partners to pursue opportunities across retail, financial services, insurance and other customer-oriented industries.\n\nUnder the proposed operating structure, the Nepal entity will focus on local business development, client relationships and market operations, while CH17\u2019s Colombo operation will provide proprietary technology, platform licensing, technical support and agreed specialist services.\n\nThis asset-light operating model is intended to create opportunities for recurring technology and service export revenue originating from Sri Lanka.\n\nImportantly, the expansion demonstrates how locally developed intellectual property can be introduced to overseas markets without the need to rebuild technology platforms for each country.\n\nIt also provides a potential foundation for evaluating further international market opportunities through suitably qualified local partners."
  },
  {
