    "chunk_size_bytes": 1515,
    "chunk_text": "JAT Holdings ups revenue by 36% to Rs. 7 b in 1H led by foreign operations\n\nVolt Charge commences pilot project for electric two- and three-wheeler charging\n\nJAT Holdings PLC has recorded Group revenue of Rs. 7.01 billion for the six months ended 30 September 2026, representing a 36% year-on-year increase, supported by growth across its local businesses and a higher contribution from international operations.\n\nLocal revenue increased by 14% to Rs. 4.56 billion, primarily supported by the emulsion category, while foreign operations revenue increased by 115% to Rs. 2.45 billion, reflecting improving business conditions in Bangladesh and JAT\u2019s expanding international presence. Gross profit margin across foreign markets also improved from 24% to 26% during the period, reflecting the growing contribution of international operations to both the scale and profitability of the Group.\n\nGross profit increased by 36% to Rs. 2.46 billion, maintaining a 35% gross profit margin despite higher raw material import costs and rising fuel prices. Operating profit increased by 15% to Rs. 653 million, while operating margin moderated from 11% to 9% amid higher administrative, selling and distribution expenses associated with consolidation of Mirotone operation, Volt software amortisation, transportation and expanded storage capacity. Favourable exchange rate movements helped reduce finance costs, with profit before tax increasing by 27% to Rs. 602 million and profit after tax rising by 27% to Rs. 504 million."
  },
