    "chunk_size_bytes": 1683,
    "chunk_text": "Gross profit increased by 36% to Rs. 2.46 billion, maintaining a 35% gross profit margin despite higher raw material import costs and rising fuel prices. Operating profit increased by 15% to Rs. 653 million, while operating margin moderated from 11% to 9% amid higher administrative, selling and distribution expenses associated with consolidation of Mirotone operation, Volt software amortisation, transportation and expanded storage capacity. Favourable exchange rate movements helped reduce finance costs, with profit before tax increasing by 27% to Rs. 602 million and profit after tax rising by 27% to Rs. 504 million.\n\nJAT\u2019s wood coatings business expanded its market share to 57.1%, recording 2% revenue growth and a 1.6% improvement in net gross profit margin, supported by efficiencies gained through the second phase of its Acrylic Binder Plant upgrade. Its loyalty customer base grew by 7% to exceed 191,000, contributing approximately 78% to 80% of sales.\n\nThe decorative paints segment recorded 107% revenue growth, supported by strong performance across key brands including White by JAT, Hydro Plus and Wallz, while gross profit margin across the segment improved by 1.4%. The segment also expanded its innovation portfolio with the introduction of JAT HeatBlock20 to the industrial market. Brushes and Rollers retained market leadership with a 31% market share and 11% revenue growth.\n\nThe furnishing business also recorded 16% growth, supported by a confirmed project pipeline of Rs. 561 million. Together, these results reflect continued growth beyond JAT\u2019s traditional wood coatings base, strengthening the Group\u2019s increasingly diversified revenue portfolio."
