    "chunk_text": "The alliance called on the Government to repeal the PTA without introducing another law with similar powers.\n\nIt also demanded the withdrawal of the proposed PSTA in its current form and called for public consultation and an independent human rights review before introducing any new anti-terrorism law.\n\nIt also demanded that every arrested person be brought before a judge without delay, informed of the charges and given access to a lawyer.\n\nThe alliance called for an urgent review of cases involving people held under the PTA for long periods, saying those who have no legal reason to remain in custody should be released.\n\nIt also urged the Government to conduct independent investigations into allegations of torture, enforced disappearances, unlawful detention and other human rights abuses.\n\nThe group said national security laws should be applied equally, without discrimination based on ethnicity, religion, language or political beliefs.\n\nRajeevkanth said the public should be given an opportunity to examine proposed laws before they are introduced.\n\n\u201cA law does not become democratic simply because it is introduced by a government that once opposed repression. Legislation must be judged by the powers it gives authorities and the safeguards it provides to the public,\u201d he said.\n\nHe said the alliance would continue to oppose the misuse of State power, regardless of which political party was in Government.\n\n\u201cWe are not demanding special privileges. We are demanding justice, accountability, fair legal procedures, judicial independence and equal protection under the law,\u201d he said."
