    "chunk_size_bytes": 1072,
    "chunk_text": "Fuel prices remain below cost-recovery levels despite November hikes \u2013 Verit\u00e9 Research\n\nColombo, November 6 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lanka\u2019s November fuel price increases have failed to bring pump prices in line with cost-recovery levels, with both diesel and Petrol 92 continuing to be sold below the prices required under the pricing formula, Verit\u00e9 Research said.\n\nAccording to Verit\u00e9 Research, the gap between the market price and the cost-recovery price for auto diesel has narrowed to Rs. 62 per litre following the November price revision.\n\nThis was due to an increase in the market price of diesel and a slight decline in its formula-based price.\n\nHowever, the shortfall for Petrol 92 has widened to Rs. 57 per litre, as the formula-based price increased at a faster rate than the pump price.\n\nVerit\u00e9 Research also pointed out that the diesel pricing formula continues to include the Rs. 70 per litre subsidy introduced in October.\n\nThe research organisation said the latest figures were available through the Fuel Price Tracker maintained by PublicFinance.lk."
  },
