    "chunk_text": "Raid Amazones is a women-only multi-sport adventure challenge founded in 2001 by French entrepreneur Alexandre Debanne of ZBO France. It brings together teams of women who compete in activities such as orienteering, mountain biking, canoeing, horse riding and running, while experiencing the culture and natural attractions of the host country.\n\nSri Lanka has previously hosted the event in 2004, 2009, 2018, 2019, 2022 and 2023, with each edition attracting more than 250 international participants.\n\nThe event is also expected to benefit the local tourism industry by attracting high-spending travellers who may extend their stays to explore the country's cultural and natural attractions.\n\nThe 2023 edition, organised with the support of Sri Lanka Tourism and SriLankan Airlines, generated an estimated USD 50 million in publicity value, according to the organisers. It also attracted more than 300 international press articles, reached an audience of around one million people and recorded over 65,000 engagements and 650,000 video views.\n\nSri Lanka Tourism expects the 2026 edition to generate further international media exposure and strengthen the country's position as a tourism destination.\n\nThe event is also expected to support the development of sports tourism, an emerging segment of the industry that could bring additional international visitors and tourism revenue to Sri Lanka."
