    "chunk_text": "Xiaomi introduces Redmi Note 17 series\n\nXiaomi, a global consumer electronics and smart manufacturing brand, unveiled the Redmi Note 17 series in Sri Lanka, alongside an expanded Xiaomi ecosystem spanning entertainment, smart home technology, personal care, health and fitness, kitchen appliances and lifestyle products.\n\nThe Redmi Note 17 series comprises four models: Redmi Note 17 Pro Max 5G, Redmi Note 17 Pro 5G, Redmi Note 17 5G and Redmi Note 17. The lineup brings together long-lasting battery performance, immersive displays, enhanced durability and AI-powered capabilities, offering the consumers a range of options to suit their needs.\n\nLeading the series, Redmi Note 17 Pro Max 5G features a 10,000mAh battery with 100W HyperCharge, designed to deliver up to three days of use. Its 6.83-inch 1.5K CrystalRes AMOLED display supports a refresh rate of up to 120Hz, while a 50MP main camera with optical image stabilisation (OIS), Snapdragon 6 Gen 5 processor and Xiaomi HyperAI with Google Gemini support an enhanced everyday smartphone experience.\n\nRedmi Note 17 Pro 5G combines an 8,340mAh battery with 67W HyperCharge, while both Redmi Note 17 models feature 7,700mAh batteries and 45W charging. Across the range, features include high-refresh-rate AMOLED displays, capable camera systems and AI-assisted tools. The Pro models also offer IP66, IP68, IP69 and IP69K dust and water resistance, alongside certified drop resistance of up to three metres.\n\nXiaomi Sri Lanka Country Head Kain Wang said, \u201cWith Redmi Note 17 Series, we are delivering a combination of performance, durability, battery endurance and intelligent features that meet the evolving expectations of consumers.\u201d\n\nBeyond smartphones, Xiaomi introduced a broader portfolio of ecosystem products across multiple categories. The entertainment range includes televisions and sound speakers, while smart home offerings extend to security cameras, smart locks, LED bulbs, robot vacuum cleaners, air purifiers and tower fans."
