    "chunk_text": "Cross River Bank global financial infrastructure platform partners with Hatch\n\nCross River Bank EVP and Chief AI Officer Pravesh Rijal in Colombo\n\nCross River, a global financial infrastructure platform founded by fintech pioneer Gilles Gade, has brought its global expansion efforts to Sri Lanka, with EVP and Chief AI Officer Pravesh Rijal visiting Colombo recently.\n\nRijal\u2019s visit, facilitated by Hatch, one of Sri Lanka\u2019s leading start-up and innovation hubs and its founder Jeevan Gnanam, included meetings with senior executives from several of the country\u2019s major banks, the Fintech Forum, Central Bank of Sri Lanka and Presidential Secretariat.\n\nDiscussions focused on enabling faster cross-border payments, expanding access to modern financial infrastructure for Sri Lankan businesses and exploring how artificial intelligence is reshaping the movement of money and the future of financial services.\n\nThe visit marks a significant step in exploring opportunities to connect Sri Lanka\u2019s financial ecosystem with global payment networks and next-generation financial technology.\n\nCross River\u2019s strategy centres on building regulated US dollar infrastructure that banks, fintech companies and businesses worldwide can access to support international transactions and financial innovation.\n\nBy connecting payment networks across currencies and markets, the platform aims to reduce friction in cross-border transactions while working alongside local financial institutions rather than replacing them.\n\nCross River already powers some of the world\u2019s leading technology and fintech companies, including Stripe, X Money, Coinbase, Affirm and Upgrade. The company pioneered embedded finance through a technology platform built on its own real-time banking core. Today, Cross River operates at the intersection of banking, fintech, artificial intelligence and agentic commerce, as it continues to expand its global reach."
  },
