    "chunk_size_bytes": 1663,
    "chunk_text": "hSenidBiz sustains growth in 2Q FY2027\n\nhSenid Business Solutions PLC (hSenidBiz) announced its financial results for the second quarter of FY2027.\n\nThe quarter reflected continued progress in the quality of the company\u2019s recurring revenue base and the strength of the underlying operating performance, even as sequential revenue was modestly softer, due to the timing of large project invoicing.\n\nTotal revenue for the quarter reached Rs.598.6 million, up 16 percent year-on-year (YoY). Recurring revenue accounted for 76 percent of total revenue and exit annualised recurring revenue stood at US $ 5.7 million, also up 16 percent YoY and broadly in line with the prior quarter.\n\nSequential revenue was marginally lower, reflecting softer contributions from OnPrem and payroll outsourcing solutions, partly offset by the higher tracking-device sales. The company views the sequential movement as consistent with the normal variability of a multi-product business that is steadily increasing the weight of its higher-quality recurring SaaS revenue.\n\nThe underlying operating performance continued to strengthen. Gross profit rose 25 percent YoY to Rs.300.3 million at a 50 percent margin. The EBITDA, excluding the foreign exchange losses, increased 141 percent YoY to Rs.72.0 million, equivalent to a 12 percent margin.\n\nThe appreciation of the Sri Lankan rupee resulted in a foreign exchange loss, contributing to a net loss of Rs.9.3 million for the quarter. This net loss was 64 percent narrower than the corresponding quarter of the prior year. Operating cash flow returned to positive territory at Rs.70.6 million and the free cash flow was also positive."
  },
