    "md5": "33f9394bfbc0a4e032db205272727f71",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1830,
    "chunk_text": "Spot On returns with 5 of  Sri Lanka\u2019s standout brand stories\n\nWe often look to global markets for inspiration, while there is so much being created here that our own industry can learn from.\n\nThat is the thinking behind Spot On, a platform by The Faculty of Brands (TFOB) that shines a spotlight on noteworthy brand work from Sri Lanka.\n\nIt brings the people behind the work together to share the thinking, purpose, challenges and lessons behind it. An opportunity for the industry to learn from one another, build confidence in what we can create here, sharpen our craft and take our work to a global stage.\n\nFollowing a successful inaugural edition that brought together more than 400 participants, Spot On returns on November 12, 2026, at Bay 7, Trace Expert City, Colombo, for its second edition.\n\nThis year, five new Sri Lankan brands will take the stage, offering a closer look at the thinking, decisions and work behind some of the country\u2019s most noteworthy brand stories.\n\nThe line-up features Barista Coffee Lanka (Pvt.) Ltd Chief Executive Officer Dilupa Pathirana, who will share how Barista has helped shape Sri Lanka\u2019s coffee landscape through years of sustained effort, with particularly exponential growth over the last two years. The story behind that growth is one of sharp execution, knowing exactly what the brand stands for and having the conviction to commit to it.\n\nRepresenting Maliban, Maliban Group of Companies Group Head of Corporate Communications Positha Perera and Shuffl Studio co-founder Sagar Hiranand will explore what it takes to keep a heritage brand relevant to a generation that did not grow up with it. Their story looks at how a brand with decades of history can make its legacy meaningful to new audiences, balancing the weight of heritage with the courage to do things differently."
  },
