    "md5": "0e347544aec188507de58983aadda751",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1701,
    "chunk_text": "Representing Maliban, Maliban Group of Companies Group Head of Corporate Communications Positha Perera and Shuffl Studio co-founder Sagar Hiranand will explore what it takes to keep a heritage brand relevant to a generation that did not grow up with it. Their story looks at how a brand with decades of history can make its legacy meaningful to new audiences, balancing the weight of heritage with the courage to do things differently.\n\nFrom Unilever Sri Lanka, Director Marketing, Personal Care, Beauty and Wellbeing and Media Shamara Perera will discuss how Sunsilk tapped into the cultural influence of cinema to connect with younger audiences. Drawing on the popularity of Korean dramas, Bollywood and Hollywood, the Hair Moves campaign recognised the role of hair in the worlds and stories young audiences already love, using cinema as a vehicle to reach them.\n\nCompleting the line-up, Lion Brewery (Ceylon) PLC Chief Sales and Marketing Officer Madhushanka Ranatunga will share the thinking behind building a brand in a category where traditional advertising opportunities are restricted. With a brand legacy spanning 139 years, Lion\u2019s story explores how marketers can work within constraints, find different ways to reach audiences and continue building strong brands when conventional tools are not available.\n\nEach presentation will take the audience behind the finished work, exploring the thinking, challenges, strategic choices and execution that shaped the brand\u2019s journey. Together, the five stories offer a range of perspectives on what it takes to build, grow and sustain brands in the Sri Lankan market.\n\nThe event begins at 6:00 p.m. Tickets are available through PickMe Explore."
