    "md5": "4a20a75d794295af94b454e1becd2a65",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1901,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lankan-origin UAE off-roading figure dies in Dubai\n\nGulf News - Sri Lankan-origin Mitchell Perera, a well-known figure in the UAE's off-roading and camping community and a veteran marshal at Gulf News' annual Fun Drive, died in Dubai on Wednesday, his family confirmed to Gulf News on Thursday.\n\nPopularly known as Mitch, he was 59. He died after battling complications following open-heart surgery on August 14, the family said.\n\nMitch is survived by his wife and son, who live in Germany, and his elderly parents in Sri Lanka, who are aged 85 and over 90, respectively. He was an only child.\n\nSpeaking to Gulf News, his relative Dalrene Devadason said Mitch was diagnosed with a leak in a heart valve after being rushed to hospital when his blood sugar levels rose to 400. He remained in the ICU at a hospital in Dubai following the surgery, during which he suffered breathing difficulties, kidney dysfunction and lung complications.\n\nAlthough he showed gradual improvement and was undergoing rehabilitation, his condition deteriorated in the days before his death after he developed internal bleeding.\n\n\"He fought really hard. There were two or three occasions after the surgery when the doctors told us his condition was critical and that he might not survive, but he pulled through each time. He gave all of us so much hope. But unfortunately, the past few days had been tough and he couldn't make it. Despite doctors' efforts, he passed away around noon yesterday,\" said Dalrene.\n\nMitch had a huge circle of friends, and many of them were like brothers and sisters to him. \"People have been calling us, and everyone is shocked by his passing,\" Dalrene said.\n\n\"Mitch was deeply passionate about off-roading and camping. He had been involved in it for years, travelled to the US because of his interest in vehicles, and was one of the pioneers of the off-roading community here,\" she recalled."
  },
