    "md5": "6ed5994ac00498ff4f1acac3d788c83d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1556,
    "chunk_text": "\"Mitch was deeply passionate about off-roading and camping. He had been involved in it for years, travelled to the US because of his interest in vehicles, and was one of the pioneers of the off-roading community here,\" she recalled.\n\nThe Sri Lankan Consulate in Dubai is extending its support for the repatriation procedures.\n\nGulf News has paid tribute to Mitch and offered its condolences to his family and friends.\n\n\u201cMitch was one of the heroes of the Gulf News Fun Drive. He began as a marshal and went on to serve as communications controller and project leader on multiple occasions. His contribution was integral to the success of every Fun Drive he was involved in. All of us at Gulf News remember him with gratitude and extend our heartfelt condolences to his family and friends in the off-roading community on his untimely passing,\u201d said Ashfaq Ahmed, Managing Editor, Gulf News.\n\nMitch first took part in the Fun Drive in its inaugural year in 1986 as a navigator when his dad Chris Perera was a marshal.\n\nFollowing in the footsteps of his father, Mitch became a marshal after he got his licence and became a certified desert driver in 1987. He took part in the annual desert drive for decades and helped make it one of the UAE's best-known recreational motoring events.\n\nGulf News has run several reports about Mitch's contributions to the Fun Drive. He was reportedly excellent as a marshal, pulling, pushing, instructing and guiding participants through the drive. He was also known for offering great tips and advice for offroad drivers."
  },
