    "md5": "eeb45e6d3284280cf3b7f1f826cadf25",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1788,
    "chunk_text": "Dialog Completes Restoration at Divisional Hospital, Kothmale\n\nUnveiling of the plaque. From left to right: Asith De Silva, Senior Manager Social Innovation, Dialog Axiata PLC; Dr. Niranji Wijesuriya, Regional Director of Health Services (RDHS), Nuwara Eliya District; Asanga Priyadarshana, Group Chief Corporate Officer, Dialog Axiata PLC; Lasantha Theverapperuma, Group Chief Marketing Officer, Dialog Axiata PLC; Dr. Nalinda Jayatissa, Minister of Health and Mass Media, Sri Lanka; Anushka Thilakarathne, Member of Parliament, Nuwara Eliya District; Jagath Adhikari, Secretary, Central Provincial Ministry of Health; Dr. Himesh Weeratunga, Divisional Medical officer, Kotmale Hospital; Ajith Muramudali, Chairman, Kotmale Pradeshiya Sabha\n\nGifts Fully Equipped Emergency Treatment Unit to Strengthen Emergency Care\n\nDialog Axiata PLC, Sri Lanka\u2019s #1 connectivity provider, marked the completion of its restoration initiative at Divisional Hospital, Kothmale, gifting the hospital a fully equipped Emergency Treatment Unit (ETU). Featuring state-of-the-art medical equipment, the new facility will strengthen emergency treatment services and improve access to timely medical care for patients in Kothmale and surrounding communities.\n\nThe initiative forms part of Dialog\u2019s broader LKR 420 million post-Ditwah recovery programme to restore and strengthen critical healthcare and education infrastructure across Sri Lanka. Following the completion of restoration work at District General Hospital, Chilaw, in October, Kothmale marks the second hospital to benefit under the programme, with further healthcare restoration initiatives planned in the coming months. The programme also includes the development of IT infrastructure in 20 schools to strengthen access to digital education."
  },
