    "chunk_text": "The initiative forms part of Dialog\u2019s broader LKR 420 million post-Ditwah recovery programme to restore and strengthen critical healthcare and education infrastructure across Sri Lanka. Following the completion of restoration work at District General Hospital, Chilaw, in October, Kothmale marks the second hospital to benefit under the programme, with further healthcare restoration initiatives planned in the coming months. The programme also includes the development of IT infrastructure in 20 schools to strengthen access to digital education.\n\nInvitees visiting the upgraded Emergency Treatment Unit at the Divisional Hospital, Kothmale\n\nHon. Dr. Nalinda Jayatissa, Minister of Health and Mass Media, said, \u201cA strong public healthcare system must ensure that quality medical services are accessible to people across the country, regardless of where they live. Strengthening hospitals at the community level is essential to achieving this, particularly when it comes to emergency care, where timely treatment can make a critical difference. The Government remains committed to improving healthcare infrastructure and services nationwide, and partnerships with organisations such as Dialog play an important role in supporting these efforts. We appreciate Dialog\u2019s continued contribution, from the recent restoration at Chilaw to this new facility in Kothmale, and its commitment to supporting the healthcare needs of our people.\u201d"
