    "chunk_text": "Hon. Dr. Nalinda Jayatissa, Minister of Health and Mass Media, said, \u201cA strong public healthcare system must ensure that quality medical services are accessible to people across the country, regardless of where they live. Strengthening hospitals at the community level is essential to achieving this, particularly when it comes to emergency care, where timely treatment can make a critical difference. The Government remains committed to improving healthcare infrastructure and services nationwide, and partnerships with organisations such as Dialog play an important role in supporting these efforts. We appreciate Dialog\u2019s continued contribution, from the recent restoration at Chilaw to this new facility in Kothmale, and its commitment to supporting the healthcare needs of our people.\u201d\n\nThe completion of the Kothmale facility follows Dialog\u2019s restoration initiative at District General Hospital, Chilaw, where a fully equipped Operating Theatre and upgraded Endoscopy Unit were handed over in October 2026. Together, these initiatives reflect Dialog\u2019s continued efforts to strengthen essential healthcare services, from emergency treatment to surgical and diagnostic care.\n\nBuilding on its longstanding contribution to Sri Lanka\u2019s healthcare sector, Dialog continues to work alongside the Government and healthcare institutions to strengthen essential public services, support communities and contribute towards the country\u2019s long-term development."
