    "md5": "c793c9d3e0b05e9d6a407280e30e8d6c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1511,
    "chunk_text": "Indices close in green\n\nIndices closed in green as a result of price gains in counters such as Commercial Bank, Dialog Axiata and Hayleys with the turnover crossing Rs. 5.4bn.\n\nHigh net worth and institutional investor participation was noted in Lanka Milk Foods, Cargills Bank and Royal Ceramics.\n\nMixed interest was observed in People\u2019s Leasing & Finance, Hatton National Bank and Digital Mobility Solutions Lanka whilst retail interest was noted in Softlogic Finance, SMB Leasing and Softlogic Finance.\n\nForeign participation in the market activity remained at subdued levels with foreigners closing as net sellers. The Banking sector was the top contributor to the market turnover (due to Hatton National Bank and Cargills Bank) whilst the sector index gained 3.73%.\n\nThe share price of Hatton National Bank moved up by Rs. 5.00 (1.30%) to close at Rs. 390.00. The share price of Cargills Bank appreciated by Rs. 0.10 (1.45%) to close at Rs. 7.00.\n\nMaterials sector was the second highest contributor to the market turnover (due to Tokyo Cement Company nonvoting) whilst the sector index increased by 3.81%. The share price of Tokyo Cement Company nonvoting recorded a gain of Rs. 5.60 (9.62%) to close at Rs. 63.80.\n\nLanka Milk Foods and People\u2019s Leasing & Finance were also included amongst the top turnover contributors. The share price of Lanka Milk Foods increased by Rs. 4.60 (%) to close at Rs. 88.30. The share price of People\u2019s Leasing & Finance gained Rs. 0.60 (5.50%) to close at Rs. 18.10."
