    "chunk_text": "Fitch lifts ratings of People\u2019s Leasing, MBSL and CBC Finance on parent bank upgrades\n\nPeople\u2019s Leasing & Finance PLC and Merchant Bank of Sri Lanka & Finance PLC (MBSL) have been lifted two notches to \u2018AA-(lka)\u2019, while CBC Finance PLC moved a notch higher to \u2018A+(lka)\u2019, as last week\u2019s upgrades of their parent banks strengthened the parents\u2019 ability to support them, Fitch Ratings said.\n\nThe action follows Fitch\u2019s 30 October upgrades of People\u2019s Bank and Bank of Ceylon to \u2018AA+(lka)\u2019 and Commercial Bank of Ceylon PLC to \u2018AA(lka)\u2019, which came after the agency recalibrated its national rating scale following Sri Lanka\u2019s sovereign rating upgrade to \u2018B-\u2019 from \u2018CCC+\u2019 in September. All three finance companies carry Stable Outlooks.\n\nThe upgrades \u201creflect our view of the parents\u2019 improved ability to support their subsidiaries,\u201d Fitch noted, adding that high ownership stakes, shared branding in some cases and management oversight raise the reputational risk to the parents should a subsidiary fail. People\u2019s Bank owns 75 percent of People\u2019s Leasing and Bank of Ceylon 84.4 percent of MBSL, while Commercial Bank wholly owns CBC Finance.\n\nHowever, Fitch drew distinctions in each parent\u2019s willingness to step in. It said People\u2019s Leasing\u2019s \u201clongstanding and largely successful role\u201d as the People\u2019s Bank group\u2019s leasing arm strengthened its parent\u2019s propensity to provide support, though this was balanced against the company\u2019s significant balance sheet size relative to that of People\u2019s Bank.\n\nMeanwhile, MBSL plays a more limited role within the Bank of Ceylon group, and its record of high growth and variable profitability has put pressure on its regulatory capitalisation and leverage, the agency observed, adding that this may weigh on the parent\u2019s willingness to support it. Even so, Fitch expects Bank of Ceylon, which has provided shareholder support when needed in the past, to keep meeting MBSL\u2019s growth and regulatory capital needs over the near to medium term."
