    "chunk_size_bytes": 1985,
    "chunk_text": "JAT Holdings lifts first half profit by 26.7% as overseas revenue more than doubles\n\nJAT Holdings PLC grew Group revenue 36.0 percent to Rs. 7,007.1 million in the six months to 30 September 2026, as foreign revenue more than doubled.\n\nLocal revenue rose 13.5 percent to Rs. 4,557.2 million, led by emulsions, while foreign revenue climbed 115.5 percent to Rs. 2,450.0 million on improving conditions in Bangladesh and wider international reach. Foreign gross margin widened from 24 percent to 26 percent.\n\nGross profit increased 36.4 percent to Rs. 2,457.0 million, with the gross margin steady at 35.1 percent despite higher raw material and fuel costs. Operating profit grew 14.8 percent to Rs. 653.1 million, though costs from the Mirotone consolidation, Volt software amortisation, transport and storage narrowed operating margin to 9.3 percent from 11.0 percent. Finance costs fell 29.7 percent to Rs. 115.7 million, helped by a Rs. 51.4 million exchange gain, lifting profit before tax 27.0 percent to Rs. 601.7 million and profit after tax 26.7 percent to Rs. 504.0 million.\n\nCEO Nishal Ferdinando said the results reflected \u201cthe increasing breadth of the Group\u2019s growth\u201d, and that holding the gross margin amid higher input costs \u201creinforces the value of the investments we have made in manufacturing efficiency and backward vertical integration.\u201d\n\nWood coatings raised market share to 57.1 percent, with revenue up 2 percent and gross margin up 1.6 percent, aided by the second phase of the Acrylic Binder Plant upgrade. Loyalty customers rose 7 percent to over 191,000, contributing 78 percent to 80 percent of sales.\n\nDecorative paints revenue rose 107 percent, driven by White by JAT, Hydro Plus and Wallz, and JAT HeatBlock20 was launched for the industrial market.\n\nBrushes and Rollers retained market leadership with a 31 percent share and 11.6 percent growth, while furnishing grew 16.6 percent to Rs. 252.9 million with a confirmed Rs. 561 million pipeline."
