    "chunk_size_bytes": 1432,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka named \u2018Luxury Food Destination of the Year\u2019 at UK Travel & Taste Awards\n\nSri Lanka has been named \u2018Luxury Food Destination of the Year\u2019 at the Travel & Taste Awards 2026 in the United Kingdom, with judges citing the wave of new boutique hotel groups redefining luxury on the island among the reasons, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Foreign Employment and Tourism said.\n\nThe award was presented by Travel & Taste Awards Chief Organiser Alex Crosley at Sri Lanka Tourism\u2019s promotion stand during the World Travel Market exhibition in London.\n\nThe awards, which celebrate food-centric travel experiences and destinations across 17 categories, were judged by a panel of food and travel experts that included spirits specialist Millie Milliken-Holdsham, food travel content creator Verna Gao, and hospitality connoisseurs Gina Jackson and Millie Kenny-Ryder.\n\nBesides the new boutique hotel groups, the judges placed particular emphasis on the island\u2019s vibrant and dynamic culinary scene and how\u00a0 Sri Lanka showcases its indigenous natural produce, according to the ministry.\n\nThe ministry noted that the recognition, which acknowledges the island\u2019s culinary diversity and high-quality dining experiences, strengthens Sri Lanka\u2019s position as an emerging luxury food and travel destination and \u201cadds further momentum to the country\u2019s efforts to attract quality-conscious and experience-driven tourists\u201d."
