    "md5": "17132764c23612a1dacea39087592bc5",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1893,
    "chunk_text": "Janaki Siriwardena further remanded in Krrish case\n\nFormer director of Krrish Group Janaki Siriwardena, who is in remand custody over the alleged Krrish financial transaction, was further remanded till November 20 by Colombo Chief Magistrate Asanga S. Bodaragama.\n\nMaking further submissions on behalf of the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption, Assistant Director of Legal Tanuja Bandara informed court that statements had been recorded from several individuals in connection with the incident, including the Colombo Divisional Secretary and a former Land Commissioner.\n\nShe further said that additional statements were yet to be recorded.\n\nShe also informed the court that a letter bearing the signature of the fourth suspect had been sent to the Government Analyst for handwriting examination. However, the document submitted was only a photocopy, and the Government Analyst had informed the Commission that the original document was required to conduct the examination.\n\nThe original document is currently filed in connection with another case pending before Courtroom No. 7 of the Colombo High Court.\n\nAs the Commission is not a party to that case, it is unable to obtain the original document directly, she said.\n\nShe requested court to issue an order directing that the original document be released to the Commission, stating that it could be forwarded to the Government Analyst within one day and returned to court thereafter.\n\nHaving considered the submissions, the Chief Magistrate advised the CIABOC to submit a written report clearly setting out the grounds for its request.\n\nMeanwhile, the counsel appearing for the third suspect, former Krrish Group director Janaki Siriwardena, informed court that a bail application would be made on her behalf.\n\nThe Chief Magistrate directed the counsel to file a motion on November 13 to make the bail application."
