    "md5": "9f6222bdae627849bc89a8bbc0a8c467",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1490,
    "chunk_text": "Kenyan cult leader sentenced to 200 years in prison\n\nMOMBASA, Kenya, Nov 6 (Reuters) - A Kenyan court sentenced cult leader Paul Mackenzie on Friday to 200 years in prison for the \u200cmurders of 190 children starved to death on his orders and buried in a forest, among 500 suspected victims of one of the deadliest cult-related mass killings of modern times.\n\nThe sentence comprised 100 years for murder by starvation and 100 years for direct homicide, Justice Diana Kavedza said, reading out the judgement.\n\nProsecutors said Mackenzie, who led an apocalyptic Christian church in a forest near eastern Kenya's Indian Ocean coast, had told his followers to starve themselves to death, along with their children, to \u200breach heaven before the end of the world.\n\nHis accomplices threatened and beat victims to ensure they followed his orders. The emaciated bodies were found scattered in shallow graves and dumped in latrines. \u200bSome had been buried alive.\n\nMackenzie, wearing a grey polo shirt and black trousers, did not react as the judge read out his sentence in a tent \u2060set up outside the court where the hearing was held.\n\nHe had denied murder charges, saying he did not force the victims to starve. The court rejected his defence.\n\nTwenty-eight accomplices received sentences ranging from 10 to \u200b160 years. All were found guilty at a trial last month.\n\nDefence lawyer Lawrence Obonyo, who represents Mackenzie and almost all of the others convicted, said he would appeal the ruling."
