    "chunk_text": "Equally important, Budget 2027 must demonstrate how economic recovery will translate into higher real incomes, productive investment,\u00a0 employment and improved public services. Public expenditure must be judged by delivery, not merely allocations, while accountability must apply equally to present officeholders and their predecessors.\n\nDr. Colvin R. de Silva\u2019s observation about J.R. Jayewardene remains relevant because political leadership is ultimately tested by its ability to recognise the forces surrounding it.\n\nThe greatest danger for the NPP is not necessarily losing power at the next election. It is losing the democratic purpose and moral credibility that brought it to power in the first place.\n\nSri Lanka does not need another Government that believes national security requires excessive State authority or that economic recovery justifies indefinite public sacrifice. It needs leadership confident enough to tolerate criticism, capable enough to transform the economy and principled enough to limit its own powers.\n\nThe ultimate measure of AKD\u2019s leadership will not be how effectively he preserves the authority of the State, but how successfully he builds a country in which the State itself is answerable to its citizens.\n\nThat is the real promise of political renewal\u2014and the test the NPP must not fail."
