    "md5": "44be2e87ae16d3f51f99b4f9ef345f1d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1823,
    "chunk_text": "Jinasena expands engineering capabilities into fire and safety sector\n\nJinasena Ltd., has launched its Fire and Safety Projects Division, marking a strategic expansion into the fire protection and safety sector.\n\nThe move extends the company\u2019s established engineering expertise into Sri Lanka\u2019s commercial, industrial and institutional infrastructure, with a comprehensive range of fire detection, protection and suppression solutions.\n\nJinasena Ltd., Managing Director, Shani Jinasena said:\u00a0 \u201cResponsible building and infrastructure development has always included fire safety as an important aspect. In order to provide customers with a more comprehensive approach to fire protection, we are combining our engineering expertise and reliable service capabilities with existing fire pump solutions with this new division. Our goal is to offer reliable, end-to-end solutions that meet organisations\u2019 fire safety needs, from system design and installation to testing and ongoing maintenance.\u201d\n\nThe Fire and Safety Projects Division offers addressable, conventional and wireless fire alarm systems, aspirating smoke detection, portable fire extinguishers, hydrants and hose reels, listed and non-listed fire pump sets, fire-rated doors, and sprinkler and valve systems. Specialised suppression solutions include water mist, clean agent, carbon dioxide (CO2), foam and kitchen wet-chemical systems.\n\nEach project follows a three-step approach: risk assessment, solution design, and verification through installation, commissioning and testing before handover. Systems with UL and LPCB approvals are designed and installed in line with recognised international standards, such as NFPA, BS EN, and SLS/ISO. From initial surveys and design to installation, commissioning, and maintenance, lifecycle support is provided."
  },
