    "chunk_size_bytes": 1267,
    "chunk_text": "John Keells Stock Brokers Head of Research Navin Ratnayake then turned to the relationship between equities and underlying real estate assets, examining the significance of land and property holdings within publicly listed companies and the importance of understanding underlying asset values when evaluating investment opportunities. His segment highlighted how investors can gain exposure to real estate both through direct property ownership and through the equity market.\n\nCommenting on the event, Nadeem Shums said: \u201cReal estate has always played a significant role in how Sri Lankans create and preserve wealth. However, the conversation around property investment needs to evolve beyond simply purchasing an apartment or acquiring land. Investors today are increasingly looking at capital appreciation, rental income, location fundamentals and the long-term value of the assets they hold. At John Keells Properties, we believe that well-planned developments in strategic locations can play an important role in long-term wealth creation. Through events such as The Investment Playbook, we want to encourage investors to look at property within the context of their broader investment portfolios and make decisions based on a deeper understanding of value.\u201d"
