    "chunk_text": "Commenting on the event, Nadeem Shums said: \u201cReal estate has always played a significant role in how Sri Lankans create and preserve wealth. However, the conversation around property investment needs to evolve beyond simply purchasing an apartment or acquiring land. Investors today are increasingly looking at capital appreciation, rental income, location fundamentals and the long-term value of the assets they hold. At John Keells Properties, we believe that well-planned developments in strategic locations can play an important role in long-term wealth creation. Through events such as The Investment Playbook, we want to encourage investors to look at property within the context of their broader investment portfolios and make decisions based on a deeper understanding of value.\u201d\n\nThe collaboration reflects a shared effort to encourage informed investment decisions by bringing together expertise from different segments of the investment landscape. For John Keells Properties, the initiative forms part of a broader commitment to engaging with investors beyond individual property transactions, creating space for meaningful conversations around investment strategy, market developments and long-term value. For John Keells Stock Brokers, it reinforces the importance of investment education, market research and informed decision-making in an increasingly dynamic financial landscape.\n\nAs economic conditions and financial markets continue to evolve, The Investment Playbook reinforced a central message: long-term wealth is not built by choosing between asset classes, but by understanding how each contributes to a broader investment strategy.\n\nThe evening concluded with an informal networking session, giving attendees the opportunity to engage with the speakers and continue the investment conversation."
  },
