    "chunk_text": "The Master\u2019s program will be jointly developed and delivered under the national\u00a0 coordination of the University of Jaffna, with the participation of the Universities of\u00a0 Moratuwa, Peradeniya and Ruhuna. The European consortium comprises HVL, Norway;\u00a0 the University of Groningen, the Netherlands; OTH Regensburg \u2013 Technical University of\u00a0 Applied Sciences, Germany; and Virumaa College of Tallinn University of Technology,\u00a0 Estonia.\n\nThrough this international partnership, the consortium will jointly develop the\u00a0 curriculum, enhance academic staff competencies, strengthen laboratory facilities and\u00a0 establish shared teaching resources and quality assurance mechanisms. Academic\u00a0 training programs and industrial visits in Europe will provide Sri Lankan academics\u00a0 with opportunities to exchange knowledge and experience with leading university and\u00a0 industry specialists and adapt international best practices to the country\u2019s specific\u00a0 needs.\n\nThe proposed curriculum will address the entire hydrogen value chain, covering hydrogen\u00a0 production, storage, transportation, fuel cells and integration with renewable energy\u00a0 systems. It will also incorporate essential interdisciplinary areas, including hydrogen\u00a0 safety, environmental assessment, techno-economic analysis, policy and regulation,\u00a0 modelling and digital technologies. The European partner institutions will contribute\u00a0 complementary expertise in hydrogen technologies, advanced materials and\u00a0 sustainable energy systems."
