    "chunk_text": "The proposed curriculum will address the entire hydrogen value chain, covering hydrogen\u00a0 production, storage, transportation, fuel cells and integration with renewable energy\u00a0 systems. It will also incorporate essential interdisciplinary areas, including hydrogen\u00a0 safety, environmental assessment, techno-economic analysis, policy and regulation,\u00a0 modelling and digital technologies. The European partner institutions will contribute\u00a0 complementary expertise in hydrogen technologies, advanced materials and\u00a0 sustainable energy systems.\n\nAn important component of the project will be the establishment of a National Hydrogen\u00a0 Forum, bringing together universities, industry representatives, government authorities\u00a0 and civil society organisations. Through stakeholder consultations, seminars,\u00a0 knowledge-sharing activities and public outreach programs, the Forum will facilitate\u00a0 dialogue, promote awareness, inform curriculum development and foster sustainable\u00a0 collaboration among national stakeholders beyond the project\u2019s funding period.\n\nFor young people in Sri Lanka, the initiative will create valuable opportunities to access\u00a0 internationally informed postgraduate education within the country, acquire practical\u00a0 knowledge and engage in research addressing emerging needs in the energy sector. The\u00a0 joint delivery of the program across four Sri Lankan universities will enable students\u00a0 to benefit from the combined academic expertise, research capabilities and laboratory\u00a0 facilities of the participating institutions."
