    "language": "en",
    "md5": "9fad01c0f0f6809d58e3deab529a5e81",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1945,
    "chunk_text": "Sixth Bay of Bengal Maritime Dialogue in Colombo\n\nFrom left: Pathfinder Director Ahmed Jawad, Chairman Bernard Goonetilleke, German Ambassador Dr. Felix Neumann, Pathfinder Founder Milinda Moragoda, BOBP-IGO Director Dr. Pandian Krishnan Pandey,\u00a0 CHD Senior Adviser for South Asia Venu Rajamony, and President\u2019s Adviser to the President on Maritime, Ports and Logistics Dr. Parakrama Dissanayake\n\nCo-hosted by the Pathfinder Foundation and the Centre for Humanitarian Dialogue\n\nParticipant of the two-day sixth Bay of Bengal Maritime Dialogue attracted local and international participants, with the inaugural session featuring Colombo-based diplomatic missions, including ambassadors and high commissioners.\n\nThe sixth Bay of Bengal Maritime Dialogue, co-hosted by the Pathfinder Foundation and the Centre for Humanitarian Dialogue (CHD) of Switzerland, was held at the Cinnamon Grand Colombo.\n\nThe inaugural session of the two-day Dialogue was attended by Pathfinder Foundation Founder Milinda Moragoda. The session featured a plenary address by Bay of Bengal Initiative for Multi-Sectoral Technical and Economic Cooperation (BIMSTEC) Secretary-General Ambassador Indra Mani Pandey, and a keynote address delivered via a recorded message by Indonesia Vice Minister for Foreign Affairs Arief Havas Oegroseno.\n\nA special address was delivered by German Ambassador Dr. Felix Neumann, who highlighted the strategic significance of the Indian Ocean, describing it as a maritime region that connects the global economy and serves as the heartbeat of international commerce.\n\nThe Bay of Bengal region, one of the world\u2019s most densely populated and economically dynamic areas, continues to play a pivotal role in global trade and regional development. Approximately a quarter of global maritime commerce passes through its waters, while its considerable natural and human resources offer significant opportunities for sustainable economic growth."
  },
