    "language": "en",
    "md5": "e24fc5b6c98dd3ec59d25ad5410894ee",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1900,
    "chunk_text": "President pledges to crush narco \u2019shadow State\u2019 and safeguard democracy and fundamental rights\n\nYes, we need an Act to prevent organised crime. The next question is whether the provisions in the Bill are too extensive or insufficient. We can discuss that. That is why we intend to inform the Supreme Court that we agree to three amendments. We have repeatedly indicated to the Supreme Court that we are prepared to amend these provisions. What we need is strong legislation to combat organised crime\n\nReveals Rs. 220 b trade that has \"bought\" Customs, Motor Traffic and immigration officers, Police, politicians and even reached revered religious institutions\n\nSays only those \"who receive privileges and protection from organised criminals\" will be ignored; critics who speak for democracy and rights will be heard\n\nNotes aim is not to suppress people or strip their rights, but to give Police, the AG's Department and and Courts the means to finish cases\n\nStates three amendments offered to the Supreme Court: detention cut from 72 to 48 hours, tattoo-based gang clause dropped, Excise Ordinance overlap removed\n\nAffirms every law to be judged by one question \u2014 what they would mean when this Govt. is no longer in power\n\nFull text of speech delivered by President Anura Kumara Dissanayake at the religious summit held at Temple Trees on Thursday (5) to mark the first anniversary of the \u2018Quit\u2019 operation:\n\n\u201cVenerable members of the Maha Sangha and all other religious clergy have gathered here today with the aim of defeating a grave national menace. First of all, I wish to express our sincere gratitude to all of you for accepting our invitation and joining us on this occasion.\n\nWhen I look at the thousands of members of the Maha Sangha and religious clergy gathered here, I am filled with the firm conviction that, however great the challenge before us may be, it can be overcome."
  },
