    "language": "en",
    "md5": "855f6f27a0e5f9798b0c2447c2b181ec",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1745,
    "chunk_text": "When I look at the thousands of members of the Maha Sangha and religious clergy gathered here, I am filled with the firm conviction that, however great the challenge before us may be, it can be overcome.\n\nWe met several times during the year and took various decisions. Members of the Maha Sangha and religious clergy representing the National Council attended those meetings. Their support has consistently encouraged us. We can defeat this menace only through such a coordinated program.\n\nWe made a promise to the people of this country that we would eradicate this menace from Sri Lanka entirely. We have gradually opened the doors to the extent of the destruction caused by it. The problem was far deeper than it appeared from the outside. We have therefore opened the doors of a cave filled with immense destruction. We know that there are people who have been unsettled by the opening of those doors. We now face two possible paths. One is to yield to those opposing this effort and abandon the journey. The other is to overcome whatever obstacles arise and bring to a successful conclusion the decision we have taken to defeat this menace. As a Government, we have chosen the second path. This menace must be defeated successfully.\n\nThis is the greatest menace afflicting our nation today. I know that different social groups have problems unique to them. However, irrespective of social divisions or cultural and linguistic differences, the national menace confronting all of us is the drug menace. We must save our nation from this scourge. We must therefore continue on this path.\n\nA large quantity of drugs was seized during operations last year. The total quantity of drugs seized by us during this year amounts to 438,330 kilograms."
  },
