    "chunk_text": "They can remain within their shadow State, while we continue carrying out the work entrusted to us within the State. That is how many people have conducted themselves. However, as a Government, we have taken a decision: we will defeat this shadow State and dismantle it. Our children cannot have a secure future unless we dismantle the shadow State linked to drugs. How much hope do parents place in raising their children? Parents spend most of their lives on their children \u2013 to give them a good life, a good future and a safe society. How hard they work. I do not think there is a mother or father anywhere in the world who works harder for their children.\n\nThis year, we arrested individuals known by various aliases who had terrorised towns and villages. We brought 67 people who were overseas back to Sri Lanka. Going forward, wherever in the world they may be hiding, if they are involved in organised crime connected to the drug trade in our country, we say to them: \u2018You are not safe, wherever you may be.\u2019 We have also issued Red Notices for 112 people and frozen assets worth 4,500 million.\n\nWe have frozen assets worth 4,500 million that were acquired through drug trafficking. During this year, 97 T-56 automatic firearms have been seized. That is a quantity that may even exceed what some police stations have available. Some of these firearms have come out of our armed forces; this has been revealed through audit reports. On certain occasions, we received reports that a police officer had sold a firearm and fled. Firearms had found their way out. We have seized 143 pistols, 47 AK-47 rifles and 105 revolvers. These are the quantities of firearms held by the criminal State. We believe there are more."
  },
