    "chunk_size_bytes": 1636,
    "chunk_text": "We have frozen assets worth 4,500 million that were acquired through drug trafficking. During this year, 97 T-56 automatic firearms have been seized. That is a quantity that may even exceed what some police stations have available. Some of these firearms have come out of our armed forces; this has been revealed through audit reports. On certain occasions, we received reports that a police officer had sold a firearm and fled. Firearms had found their way out. We have seized 143 pistols, 47 AK-47 rifles and 105 revolvers. These are the quantities of firearms held by the criminal State. We believe there are more.\n\nIn particular, the Inspector-General of Police and the Police Department, together with the Commander of the Navy, the Commander of the Air Force, the Commander of the Army and the wider military apparatus, are making a tremendous effort in this operation, in these arrests and in defeating this menace.\u201d\n\nThese institutions are engaged in a major operation to save the State and protect our children. Yet, instead of recognising these operations, if an officer makes some mistake, it becomes a newspaper headline and the main item on a television channel\u2019s news program.\n\nWho has made the effort to seize drugs worth nearly Rs. 220 billion and to confiscate such large quantities of firearms? It is the Police and the three armed forces. Our Government will therefore give due recognition to the work they have done in this operation. We have also taken steps to provide bonuses and incentives to many officers who took part in operations in the recent past, and we will consider further measures in this regard."
