    "md5": "4216a5712096cf536e52c01018371ddd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1866,
    "chunk_text": "We act knowing that the people have entrusted power to us, and that they can take it back at any time \u2013 they can do so through an election. We know that. Therefore, in exercising power, we have no agenda involving me, my children or my relatives.\n\nHowever, the law alone is not enough. Ultimately, once an organised criminal or drug trafficker is arrested, that person must be brought before the law and punished. As a Government, we do not follow a policy of imposing punishment outside the law. That has happened in the past. We will under no circumstances punish anyone outside the law. A law is required, and the case must be heard and punishment imposed in accordance with that law.\n\nHowever, trials take too long. That cannot continue. Those institutions must therefore be strengthened. The institutions conducting investigations must be strengthened; the Attorney General\u2019s Department, which files cases, must be strengthened; the Government Analyst\u2019s Department, which provides the scientific evidence required for those cases, must be strengthened; and the judicial sector, which ultimately hears those cases, must also be strengthened. We are intervening in all these areas.\n\nWe have made plans to improve investigative institutions and the police, and to provide them with specialised training. Investigations must be conducted, and cases must be filed on the basis of those investigations. For that, the Attorney General\u2019s Department must be strengthened. In particular, we need Government Analyst\u2019s reports. Our Government Analyst is here, and we need those reports. We had a backlog of 36,000 reports.\n\nNormally, only around 3,000 reports were completed a month. We deployed additional staff and provided new allowances. Our Navy also assisted with some infrastructure requirements. What did we do by providing assistance with infrastructure?"
  },
