    "md5": "e9485f3c7a1da9981046dfe1f35734ae",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1708,
    "chunk_text": "The State cannot do this alone. Everyone\u2019s contribution and organised involvement are necessary. We will give this priority: we will enact the necessary laws, strengthen institutions, ensure that courts are equipped to hear cases, make the police and armed forces effective, and establish our rehabilitation authority and institutions. That is the Government\u2019s responsibility. However, the greatest role in defeating this menace belongs to the general public.\n\nLet us set aside all our other divisions as well. Above those divisions, we must recognise only two sides: those who support the drugs trade, armed criminal gangs and the criminal State built around them, and those who oppose them. That is all. There should be no other division in the country today.\n\nToday, this monster called drugs has spread throughout the country, leaving no place untouched. This menace has grown over several decades because it was supported, ignored or simply allowed to continue. We are now tasked with defeating a menace that has already grown to enormous proportions. We know what needs to be done to address it, but this is no longer at the beginning. It has now become a massive national crisis. This is not something that can be brought to an end in a year or two. However, if we continue this effort without giving up for several years, we can free our nation from this menace. We can create a secure future for our younger generation and a safe society, free from conflict. We can build a country in which our children can live with pride. I believe that our Venerable monks have a great responsibility in this endeavour. I invite and appeal to you to become partners and active participants in this effort.\u201d"
  },
