    "md5": "821e67a0e28fb3ed43e0020d01299527",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 947,
    "chunk_text": "Are borrowed funds being directed towards purposes that justify the future liabilities?\n\nIs the public receiving transparent information on the actual results achieved?\n\nThese are not unreasonable demands from taxpayers. They are essential requirements of an accountable Government.\n\nTaxation must not destroy the capacity to create wealth. Borrowing must not become a permanent substitute for financial discipline. Budgets must not be built on hypothetical expectations while actual obligations are passed on to future generations.\n\nA Government should collect what is reasonably necessary, spend what it can responsibly afford, borrow for defensible purposes and account openly for every major financial decision.\n\nThe true measure of a successful fiscal policy is not how much money a Government manages to collect or borrow, but how effectively it converts public resources into national prosperity, economic opportunity and social well-being."
