    "chunk_text": "Bimal Ratnayake appointed ICAPP Media Forum Co-Chair\n\nMinister of Transport, Highways and Urban Development and Leader of the House Bimal Ratnayake has been appointed Co-Chair of the Media Forum of the International Conference of Asian Political Parties (ICAPP).\n\nHe will serve a two-year term alongside Dr. Seo Ji-young, who was also elected Co-Chair of the forum.\n\nThe appointments were made during the 13th ICAPP Session, held in Seoul, South Korea, from November 4 to 7.\n\nThe session brought together representatives of 83 political parties from 36 countries.\n\nMinister Ratnayake has also been appointed a member of the ICAPP Steering Committee."
