    "chunk_size_bytes": 843,
    "chunk_text": "Colombo Mayor holds urgent talks to address city flooding\n\nColombo Mayor Vraie Cally Balthazaar is holding a special discussion with representatives of key government institutions to identify immediate solutions to the flooding experienced in the city following Friday evening\u2019s heavy rainfall.\n\nThe discussion is focused on improving the city\u2019s drainage systems and addressing issues related to Colombo\u2019s canal network and road infrastructure.\n\nThe Mayor earlier said Colombo\u2019s drainage system was designed to accommodate approximately 30mm of rainfall, whereas the city received 129mm within a few hours on Friday, resulting in widespread flooding and disruption.\n\nThe meeting is expected to focus on identifying urgent measures to improve the city\u2019s capacity to cope with heavy rainfall and prevent similar flooding in the future."
