    "md5": "2c5aecbbdb68df26c64a6f0d1db1a70e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1037,
    "chunk_text": "Chinese Dragon Caf\u00e9 opens flagship outlet in Negombo\n\nChinese Dragon Caf\u00e9 (CDC) has expanded its presence with the opening of its newest outlet in Negombo, marking another important step in the brand\u2019s growth across the country.\n\nLocated at Chilaw Road, Negombo, just 400 metres from the Maris Stella College towards Kochchikade, the new restaurant becomes Chinese Dragon Caf\u00e9\u2019s 13th outlet in Sri Lanka and 14th outlet worldwide, bringing the brand to one of the country\u2019s most popular coastal cities.\n\nFounded in 1942 by a Chinese couple in Bambalapitiya, Chinese Dragon Caf\u00e9 has grown from a small neighbourhood restaurant into one of Sri Lanka\u2019s most recognized Chinese restaurant brands.\n\nCommenting on the opening, Lahiruwan Lakmal, Chief Operating Officer of Chinese Dragon Caf\u00e9 said, \u201cNegombo is a unique and growing city with a strong connection to seafood, tourism and a diverse customer community. We see great potential in this market and believe our Chinese cuisine will be well received by customers here.\u201d"
