    "md5": "410f5049b5c9971fcdf6247ceeb79429",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1493,
    "chunk_text": "Rainforest Ecolodge - A new chapter at the edge of Sinharaja\n\nManaged by Aitken Spence Hotels, The Rainforest Ecolodge is entering a new chapter, placing the Sinharaja Forest Reserve, its biodiversity, and the communities living alongside it at the heart of the guest experience. This renewed direction strengthens the property\u2019s role as the hospitality gateway to one of Sri Lanka\u2019s most significant natural landscapes, bringing together responsible hospitality, conservation, and the spirit of discovery.\n\nSet within the Enselwatte Tea Estate and adjoining the Sinharaja Forest Reserve, the ecolodge occupies one of Sri Lanka\u2019s most extraordinary natural settings and holds a LEED Platinum certification from the US Green Building Council, reflecting the principles of sustainability embedded in its design and construction. A UNESCO World Heritage Site and a Man and the Biosphere Reserve, the Sinharaja is Sri Lanka\u2019s last viable area of primary tropical rainforest, supporting an exceptional concentration of endemic plants, birds, mammals, reptiles, amphibians, invertebrates, and aquatic life.\n\nThe relaunch positions The Rainforest Ecolodge as the hospitality gateway to this living ecosystem: a place for travellers who want to do more than simply stay near nature. It is designed for those who want to enter the forest with curiosity, understand what they encounter, immerse themselves in the rainforest, and leave with a stronger connection to the natural world and self.\u201d"
  },
