    "chunk_text": "MBA Kelaniya Alumni Association sets sights on making national impact\n\nThe University of Kelaniya MBA Alumni Association has embarked on an exciting new chapter, placing collective leadership, innovation and national contribution at the heart of its future.\n\nThis renewed direction was unveiled at its Annual General Meeting and Fellowship Night, held on 31 October at the Lotus Tower, Colombo.\n\nThe event was graced by Chief Guest Dr. S. C. Thushara, Dean of the Faculty of Commerce and Management Studies, together with Heads of Departments, Professors and other distinguished academic representatives of the University of Kelaniya.\n\nA new 21-member Executive Committee was appointed for the 2026\u20132028 term, ushering in a fresh phase of leadership and organizational development. The Association also introduced its refreshed brand identity, symbolizing the strength of connection, diversity, resilience and shared heritage that unite Kelaniya MBA graduates.\n\nMarking another significant step in its digital transformation, the Association launched its official website (www.mbakelaniya.lk), featuring a dedicated Members\u2019 Portal and online voting facilities to strengthen member engagement, accessibility and transparent governance.\n\nAddressing the gathering, the Association\u2019s President Saranga Panapitiya said, \u201cOur ambition is to build more than an alumni association. We want to create a powerful leadership network with over 2,000 members, that transforms shared knowledge and collective action into meaningful national impact. Through entrepreneurship, education, sustainability and community-focused initiatives, we aspire to contribute to a stronger future for our country and create a legacy that extends beyond generations\u201d."
  },
