    "chunk_size_bytes": 1866,
    "chunk_text": "Culinary Art Food Expo 2026 to kick-off on November 27\n\nGroup photograph of sponsors and members of Chefs\u2019 Guild of Sri Lanka\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s food and hospitality industries will take centre stage at the 23rd edition of the Culinary Art Food Expo (CAFE 2026), bringing together industry professionals, businesses and emerging culinary talent at one of the country\u2019s leading events dedicated to the sector.\n\nScheduled to be held from 27 to 29 November at the Bandaranaike Memorial International Conference Hall (BMICH), Colombo, the exhibition is expected to attract more than 15,000 visitors, with over 200 exhibition stalls showcasing products, services and technologies across the food and hospitality value chain. The awards ceremony will take place on 30 November.\n\nOrganised by the Chefs\u2019 Guild of Lanka (CGL), a member of the World Association of Chefs\u2019 Societies (Worldchefs), in collaboration with CDC Events & Travels (Pvt) Ltd, CAFE 2026 will draw chefs, hoteliers, food manufacturers, distributors, hospitality professionals and industry leaders.\n\nA major feature of this year\u2019s event will be its international culinary competition, with more than 3,000 participants, nearly 4,000 food entries and over 40 local and international judges expected. Categories will include live cooking, pastry and bakery, chocolate showpieces, cake decorating, fruit and vegetable carving, and mixology, providing a platform for culinary professionals and hospitality students to demonstrate their skills.\n\nThe programme will also introduce two concurrent events: the World Young Chefs Club Sri Lanka Junior Chefs Culinary Championship 2026 and the World Chefs Global Butchery Competition 2026 - Sri Lanka. These initiatives are expected to create further opportunities for young and emerging culinary professionals to develop their capabilities and gain exposure."
  },
