    "md5": "c20d2bbba4d5a294b136052ac7ee511a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2027,
    "chunk_text": "ESG communication must move beyond annual reports to build brand equity\n\nSri Lankan businesses urged to turn credible sustainability initiatives into meaningful stakeholder narratives\n\nSri Lankan businesses must look beyond annual sustainability reports to communicate the broader value of their environmental, social and governance (ESG) initiatives, according to discussions at FireCircle Strategic Consultancy (Pvt.) Ltd\u2019s third ESG Storytelling Workshop, \u2018From Compliance to Brand Equity\u2019, held recently at Cinnamon Grand Colombo.\n\nThe interactive workshop brought together professionals from different organisations to explore how strategic ESG communication can strengthen stakeholder trust, corporate reputation and brand equity.\n\n\u201cMany Sri Lankan organisations are doing meaningful work across the ESG spectrum, from environmental stewardship and employee welfare to community development, ethical business practices, transparency and good governance. Yet, much of this remains confined to annual reports. While reporting is essential, it should not be the only place these stories are told,\u201d said FireCircle founder and workshop facilitator Gayani Punchihewa.\n\nEmphasising the importance of humanising the ESG data, she noted that storytelling should complement credible evidence rather than replace it.\n\n\u201cBehind every ESG data point is a human story. A water conservation initiative may protect resources for a community, while an employee welfare programme may improve a family\u2019s quality of life. Data establishes credibility but storytelling helps people understand why that impact matters.\u201d\n\nThe workshop explored evidence-based storytelling, stakeholder relevance and consistent communication, while addressing the risks of exaggeration and greenwashing. \u201cIf organisations don\u2019t tell their stories clearly and credibly, others may define those narratives for them. Strategic ESG communication allows businesses to take ownership of their stories and build long-term value,\u201d Punchihewa added."
  },
