    "md5": "834d8b2e9cae7e54e78e33ca638fa489",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1937,
    "chunk_text": "Seylan Bank opens 3 more \u2018Pahasara\u2019 libraries\n\nSeylan Bank recently opened its 297th, 298th, and 299th \u2018Pahasara\u2019 libraries at MT/Ismaliya Vidyalaya in Matale, Ireby Tamil Maha Vidyalaya in Norwood, Hatton and G/Weera Wijaya Wimalarathne MV in Dambulla, bringing the bank within a single library of completing its target of 300 Pahasara libraries across Sri Lanka.\n\nThe three libraries further reaffirm the bank\u2019s commitment and consistent dedication across over a decade to strengthening educational opportunities for students islandwide, as part of long-standing social sustainability efforts that place education, knowledge, financial literacy and access to learning resources at the centre of empowering future generations.\n\nAs part of the initiative, Seylan Bank provided each of the three schools with two laptops, a multimedia projector, projector screen and books, enhancing the schools\u2019 library infrastructure while giving students access to additional educational and digital learning resources.\n\nSeylan Bank AGM Marketing and Sales Asiri Abhayaratne said, \u201cAt Seylan Bank, we believe that access to knowledge and the right learning resources have a definite lasting impact on a child\u2019s future. The opening of our 297th, 298th, and 299th Pahasara libraries represent some of the most meaningful steps in our journey, with just one library away from opening our 300th chapter. Our hope for these spaces is that they will encourage students to explore, learn and develop the confidence and skills they need to shape their futures and build the future of our nation.\u201d\n\nThe libraries\u2019 openings were attended by representatives of Seylan Bank, alongside education officials, school representatives and members of the wider community with each opening complemented by a Pahasara Week, featuring a series of student-focused engagement activities aimed at supporting the broader development of students and parents."
  },
