    "md5": "7121c63603f464718f6eae1f4f48eb92",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1312,
    "chunk_text": "Wickramarachchi Hearing Care-WISH Foundation donate 50 hearing aids\n\nWickramarachchi Hearing Care, in collaboration with the Wonderful Sound Project and Signia, presented 50 hearing aids to beneficiaries of the WISH Foundation at a special World Children\u2019s and Adults\u2019 Day celebration held recently.\n\nThe initiative brought together organisations committed to improving access to hearing care and creating greater opportunities for individuals with hearing loss to communicate, connect and participate more fully in everyday life.\n\nThe occasion formed part of the celebrations marking 50 years of Wickramarachchi Opticians & Hearing Care, recognising five decades of service in vision and hearing care in Sri Lanka. As a long-standing partner of the company, Signia donated the 50 hearing aids for the initiative while professional and technical support for the beneficiaries was provided by Wickramarachchi Opticians & Hearing Care.\n\nThis initiative also reflects the work of the Wonderful Sound Project (WSP), a global, employee-powered programme of Denmark-based hearing healthcare leader WS Audiology that supports community-based hearing health initiatives around the world. Through WSP, the employees and partners of WSA collaborate to help close the hearing care access gap in underserved communities."
  },
