    "md5": "7b4a8a8a108620d47b8da50fed633df1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1008,
    "chunk_text": "This initiative also reflects the work of the Wonderful Sound Project (WSP), a global, employee-powered programme of Denmark-based hearing healthcare leader WS Audiology that supports community-based hearing health initiatives around the world. Through WSP, the employees and partners of WSA collaborate to help close the hearing care access gap in underserved communities.\n\nDr. Mihira Wickramarachchi stated, \u201cAs Wickramarachchi Opticians & Hearing Care marks its 50th anniversary, the organisation continues its long-standing commitment to hearing and vision care while working with local and international partners to create lasting improvements in the lives of individuals and communities across Sri Lanka. This collaboration between the WISH Foundation, Wickramarachchi Hearing Care, Wonderful Sound Project, Signia and WSA demonstrates the value of partnerships in addressing hearing-care needs and supporting individuals who may otherwise face barriers in accessing appropriate hearing solutions.\u201d"
