    "description": "IRDCRP-KIST support passion fruit cultivation",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business/IRDCRP-KIST-support-passion-fruit-cultivation/215-354387",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1794035286.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-07-dailymirrorlk-6677f485-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "5341c7d2a9341e0cebcb889dbb58fad2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1567,
    "chunk_text": "IRDCRP-KIST support passion fruit cultivation\n\nThe Integrated Rurban Development and Climate Resilience Project (IRDCRP) of the Agriculture, Livestock, Land and Irrigation Ministry, funded by the World Bank, has partnered with KIST, a renowned brand of Cargills Food and Beverage Ltd, to support the smallholder farmers in the Kalutara district through an integrated value chain partnership.\n\nThe initiative aims to strengthen local passionfruit cultivation by providing farmers with reliable market access, technical expertise and financial support. The initiative will target 300 selected smallholder farmers from the region in cultivating a total of around 200 acres, creating opportunities to diversify their farming activities and develop passion fruit as a commercially viable crop. Passion fruit cultivation was introduced to the Kalutara district in the early 1960s and was once an important source of income for local farmers. However, marketing difficulties led many to move away from the crop and focus on tea cultivation.\u00a0 Through this partnership, efforts are being made to encourage farmers to return to passion fruit cultivation by providing the support and market access needed to make it a viable income-generating activity.\n\nUnder the partnership, the Agriculture Department will provide technical training on land preparation, planting, crop management, fertiliser application and pest and disease control. The Agriculture Insurance Board will provide agricultural insurance to help farmers manage production risks and support access to financing."
  },
