    "description": "Asia Foundation-Sri Lanka Police launch national cybersecurity awareness campaign",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business/Asia-Foundation-Sri-Lanka-Police-launch-national-cybersecurity-awareness-campaign/215-354388",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1794035617.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-07-dailymirrorlk-4cdafb59-0001",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "6bccc706fe9f38ddb9c5078f1b65a1e2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1339,
    "chunk_text": "Central to the campaign are straightforward precautions that support safer digital practices. These include using strong, unique passwords, enabling two-factor authentication wherever possible, verifying suspicious links, attachments and messages before responding and never sharing one-time passwords with anyone. Together, these messages encourage vigilance in daily digital interactions.\n\nIn Sri Lanka, implementation partners include Sri Lanka Institute of Information Technology (SLIIT), Uva Wellassa University, Lanka Education And Research Network (LEARN), Regional Development Bank (RDB) and Sarvodaya.\n\nMore than 11,000 individuals representing over 7,000 MSMEs have received training to identify, prevent and manage cybersecurity risks.\n\nUniversity Cybersecurity Clinics at SLIIT and Uva Wellassa University have also reached more than 200 MSMEs with practical support to strengthen digital safety.\n\nComplementing public outreach, ACF\u2019s partnership withthe Sri Lanka Police National Police Academy has trained 150 station and divisional level officers as trainers, 50 women officers in inclusive community engagement and first-response protocols and 30 officers in technical skills, including evidence preservation and referrals. A customised cybersecurity toolkit will be integrated into the Police learning management system."
