    "md5": "edc1404c1257ab88d9d54e5b4e3834e6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1989,
    "chunk_text": "Most of the immediate victims of that pogrom are probably dead or are at death\u2019s door today. The original leaders of the organisations which took up arms to defend the victim Tamil community are also dead.\u00a0 Around a fourth of the then Tamil population fled the country and are now citizens of those country\u2019s which offered them succour.\n\nThe question that arises is, why it took two years after the NPP government was elected into power, to \u2018suddenly\u2019 call for an investigation into the causes behind the \u2018so-called 1983 riots\u2019 and its impact.\n\nAre the MPs really concerned at the plight of the long-suffering of the Tamil people? The devastating effect it had on the economy of the country, or a fear that it has created permanent ethnic divisions among our countrymen? Or could it be a ploy to take the minds of our people away from their daily struggle to keep body and soul together.\n\nToday the average wage varies between Rs. 35,000/- to Rs. 50,000l/- per month. Yet the cost of having two nutritious meals per day for a family of four (father, mother and two children) costs at least around 100,000/- per month, without taking into consideration other costs like clothes, travel or medical expenses.\n\nNot surprisingly over 20% of our schoolchildren suffer from malnutrition, while according to the WHO, over 25% of the population lives below the poverty line. Despite this, the government keeps increasing prices of essentials. Today,\u00a0 the price of wheat flour has been increased by a whopping Rs. 13/- per kg and the PUCSL is speaking of further increasing the cost of electricity.\n\nWith most of the Rajapaksa family now facing charges of bribery and corruption,\u00a0 it seems a new distraction is needed to take the attention of the people away from the intolerable burdens government continues heaping on them. Whose twisted mind came up with the idea of digging up the horrors of 1983 to save the government its blushes for having failed to control the cost of living?"
  },
