    "chunk_text": "Deduru Oya residents alerted as 4,100 cusecs released\n\nDeduru Oya reservoir releases 4,100 cusecs of water; downstream residents urged to remain vigilant\n\nSix sluice gates of the Deduru Oya Reservoir are currently being opened by one foot each, releasing approximately 4,100 cubic feet of water per second into the Deduru Oya, the Irrigation Department said.\n\nThe measure has been taken to control the volume of water entering the reservoir.\n\nThe Director of Irrigation (Water Management) urged people living downstream of the reservoir, particularly residents along the Deduru Oya, to remain vigilant and closely monitor changes in river water levels.\n\nResidents have also been advised to follow announcements and safety instructions issued by the Irrigation Department and Disaster Management authorities.\n\nThe department warned that water inflows into the reservoir and rainfall could change, potentially affecting the volume of water released downstream."
