    "md5": "373c8bbf45d527aed24620bb846e6cbc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1969,
    "chunk_text": "Six killed in Krakow \u2019far-right\u2019 shooting, as three more bodies found in attacker\u2019s home\n\nBBC - A gunman believed to have been inspired by far-right ideology has killed six people and injured more than a dozen others in an attack in the busy centre of Poland's second largest city.\n\nPolice said the attacker drove on to Main Market Square in Krakow, a popular tourist attraction, on Saturday afternoon and fired randomly at people.\n\nFour women and two men were killed. Three were Polish, one was British and two have not been identified.\n\nAmong the 16 injured are five foreign nationals from Austria, Germany, Portugal, Russia and Britain.\n\nAnother three bodies were found when counter-terrorism police searched the suspect's home around 125 miles (200km) away, Polish Prime Minister Donald Tusk said.\n\nA massive armed police presence was deployed across Krakow on Saturday evening, as security measures were ramped up in the capital Warsaw and elsewhere.\n\nA period of mourning has been declared in Krakow until 11 November.\n\nTwo police officers are also among those injured, one critically.\n\nThe suspect, who was equipped with military-style weapons and attire, is a 25-year-old Polish man - described by a minister as \"ultra-nationalist\".\n\nHe has been arrested and remains in hospital after having surgery.\n\nTusk said there were \"strong indications\" the two women and one man found dead at the suspect's home in Ostrowiec \u015awi\u0119tokrzyski were his immediate family members.\n\nHe said: \"Until now in Poland we haven't had such drastic cases of terrorism... that's what we have to call this cruel attack on people's lives here in Krakow.\"\n\nUK Prime Minister Andy Burnham said: \"I'm shocked and saddened by the appalling shooting in Krak\u00f3w today.\"\n\n\"My thoughts are with the families of those who have lost their lives, everyone injured and all those affected by this senseless violence. The United Kingdom stands in solidarity with the people of Poland,\" he added."
