    "md5": "1992d65079e56b6071ec5637568d5951",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2002,
    "chunk_text": "David C. Sanders: Master educator, visionary leader, and true friend of Sri Lanka\n\nThe news of the passing of David Charles Sanders in the UK on 14 October was received in Sri Lanka with profound sorrow and deep gratitude. A British educator by birth, he served Colombo International School (CIS) for nearly three decades from 1994, leaving an indelible mark on generations of students, staff, and families across both the Colombo and Kandy branches. His exceptional dedication was recognised in 2005 when he was honoured with the national title Sri Lanka Rathna.\n\nSucceeding founding principal Elizabeth Moir, Sanders brought sharp administrative vision and a masterclass in pedagogy. Under his guidance, CIS cemented its standing as a premier benchmark for international education. He personally mentored young minds towards Oxford, Cambridge, and leading UK medical schools, and his intellectually rich Monday morning assemblies set a gold standard for school leadership.\n\nYet it is the human moments that we, his students and colleagues, hold most dear. To us, he was the epitome of a wise, kind, and gentle leader.\n\nOdile Melder, former Head of Drama at CIS, recalled that Sanders never made staff feel managed, but rather supported: \u201cHe respected my choices and judgement, giving me a completely free hand during my nine and a half years as Head of Drama. He was more of a father figure, cushioning me from difficulties, always generous with his appreciation, and unfailingly humble.\u201d\n\nFormer student Dilruha de Silva remembered his approachable nature and trademark humour: \u201cAn extraordinary man who took a genuine, personal interest in the school and the wellbeing of every student. He knew each of us by name and enforced his slightly strict rules with a unique blend of firmness, kindness and fairness. I still laugh remembering him walking around with his foot ruler during intervals and school socials, greeting everyone while ensuring couples maintained a strict 12-inch distance!\u201d"
  },
