    "language": "en",
    "md5": "3425509840024b60e27e110c38127cd4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1922,
    "chunk_text": "There is also a regulatory difference of interpretation. In a September 2026 clarification, PUCSL maintained that separate measurement of electricity imports and exports could be implemented without necessarily discontinuing the existing commercial arrangements under Net Metering and Net Accounting.\n\nBefore making fundamental changes to Net Metering and Net Accounting arrangements, it would be prudent for the authorities to undertake and publish a comprehensive, transparent cost-benefit assessment of rooftop solar generation. Such an assessment should establish its true economic value to the national electricity system and provide a sound basis for fair and sustainable tariff policies, while protecting existing contractual commitments and investor confidence\n\nBattery Energy Storage Systems (BESS) and pumped storage hydropower plants can play a vital role in addressing the challenges associated with increasing solar generation. Surplus solar electricity produced during the daytime can be stored and released during evening peak-demand hours, reducing dependence on expensive thermal generation. Batteries can also respond rapidly to sudden changes in generation, helping maintain system frequency, improve grid stability and minimise the curtailment of renewable energy.\n\nThe National System Operator (NSO) has outlined plans to introduce approximately 1,240 MW of battery storage capacity, with an energy storage capability of 4,660 MWh, during 2027\u20132029. However, the location of these storage facilities is equally important. While large batteries connected to grid substations can support overall power system stability, they may not resolve local voltage fluctuations and transformer overloading caused by high rooftop solar penetration. Therefore, a coordinated approach involving grid-scale storage, strategically located distribution-level batteries and consumer-owned storage systems is essential."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
