    "chunk_text": "AKD can use the forthcoming Budget to renew the relationship between the State and the taxpayer through fair taxation, efficient spending, integrity and accountability. Tax relief should not be a political concession to silence the Opposition, but part of a broader effort to make Government more responsive and responsible. Citizens, too, must recognise that taxation sustains essential services, supports recovery and protects future generations from excessive debt. The goal is not a State without taxes, but one that justifies what it collects. Both sides must honour their obligations if this relationship is to endure.\n\nMauro\u2019s lesson is simple: the State must earn the trust of those whose money it collects. The forthcoming Budget gives AKD an opportunity to turn that principle into practice. He should seize it before frustration becomes a deeper crisis of confidence, placing responsible stewardship at the heart of fiscal policy.\n\nThe State may have the power to collect our hard-earned money. But it has a moral obligation to earn the right to spend it.\n\n(The writer, a former Deputy Governor of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka, can be reached at [email\u00a0protected])"
