    "chunk_size_bytes": 1980,
    "chunk_text": "FTZ Toastmasters Club presents Moulding the Mindset to Mastery on 12 November\n\nFacilitator Toastmasters World Champion of Public Speaking 2026 Dirceu da Silva\n\nIn today\u2019s rapidly evolving business environment, professional success requires more than technical knowledge and managerial experience. Organisations need leaders who can think strategically, communicate with confidence, inspire teams and navigate change. Developing this mindset is becoming an essential investment for businesses seeking sustainable growth.\n\nRecognising this need, FTZ Toastmasters Club presents \u201cMoulding the Mindset to Mastery\u201d, an exclusive leadership development event featuring Toastmasters World Champion of Public Speaking 2026 Dirceu da Silva.\n\nScheduled for Thursday, 12 November 2026, at the Colombo International Airport Hotel, Katunayake, the program is designed specifically for mid-level managers and C-suite executives working in Free Trade Zone companies.\n\nThe event will feature two dedicated sessions. The Leadership Masterclass, from 3 p.m. to 5 p.m., will focus on developing leadership capabilities among mid-level managers. The evening program, from 6 p.m., to 10 p.m.will bring together senior corporate leaders for the CXO Forum, creating an opportunity to explore leadership perspectives at the highest levels of organisational responsibility.\n\nHaving a world champion of public speaking lead this experience offers participants an opportunity to gain insights into the power of communication, influence and personal mastery. In an increasingly competitive corporate landscape, the ability to communicate a vision, engage people and lead with clarity can make a significant difference to organisational performance.\n\nBeyond the learning sessions, the event will also provide an opportunity for professional networking. High tea will be served, offering participants a relaxed setting to connect, exchange ideas and build relationships with fellow business professionals."
