    "chunk_size_bytes": 1632,
    "chunk_text": "Venkadeshwara Agro unveils Board to drive next phase of growth\n\nNorthern Province\u2019s largest edible oil manufacturer brings together banking, finance, FMCG, export and sustainability expertise, with stronger Board of Directors\n\nVenkadeshwara Agro Industry Ltd., the largest edible oil manufacturer in Sri Lanka\u2019s Northern Province, has constituted a seven-member Board of Directors that pairs founder leadership with deep expertise in banking, finance, FMCG, exports and sustainability.\n\nFive of the seven directors are independent, a structure that signals the Company\u2019s intent to hold itself to the governance standards expected of Sri Lanka\u2019s leading corporates as it scales.\n\nThe appointment\u00a0 of Michael Ranasinghe and L. Chiranthi Cooray to Venkadeshwara\u2019s Board has strengthened the company\u2019s existing robust leadership which includes Dr. Bradley Emerson (Non-Executive Chairman), Kanakasingam Suganthon (Founder/MD), Rizvi Mowlana, R. Suresh, and Manjula Priyadarshana.\n\nL. Chiranthi Cooray, is appointed as an Independent Board Director and specialist in ESG, Enterprise Transformation and Risk Expert. She is the Founder, of Accedo Intel.\n\nWith more than 20 years of leadership experience across banking, financial services, capital markets, the public sector, and academia. Chiranthi brings a strong combination of board governance, enterprise risk, ESG, human capital, organisational transformation, and institutional resilience expertise. Her work focuses on helping boards and senior leadership teams strengthen accountability, culture, leadership capability, internal controls, and sustainable performance."
  },
