    "chunk_size_bytes": 2001,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cVenkadeshwara is driven towards a stronger governance, financial discipline culture with market insight that allows the business to standout. With five independent directors and experience that spans banking, finance, FMCG and exports, we intend to hold ourselves to the standards that investors, lenders and customers expect of the country\u2019s best-run companies,\u201d said Non-Executive Chairman Dr. Bradley Emerson.\n\nThe Company manufactures premium (RBD) palm olein, coconut oil and rice bran oil, and has expanded into margarine and bakery fats in 2025. Nothing is wasted: by-products are converted into palm, coconut and rice fatty acids, rice bran wax, palm stearin and, serving food manufacturers, bakeries and industrial users. A pioneer of advanced filtration technology in edible oil refining in the Jaffna District, Venkadeshwara is ISO 9001:2015, HACCP, GMP and Halal certified, with an in-house laboratory and quality control at every stage of production.\n\nDr. Bradley Emerson, Non-Executive Chairman is a seasoned senior banker and management professional with more than four decades of experience in strategic leadership across private and public sector boards, including a banking career spanning Commercial Bank, Nations Trust Bank and Pan Asia Bank, and service as CIMA Regional Director for the Middle East, South Asia and North Africa.\n\nKanakasingam Suganthon, Founder and Managing Director is the entrepreneur who built Venkadeshwara from its Jaffna roots into one of the North\u2019s leading manufacturers, and who continues to set its strategic direction.\n\nRizvi Mowlana, Marketing Director, brings more than four decades in FMCG marketing, with deep knowledge of consumer markets, brands and commercial strategy.\n\nR. Suresh, Independent Non-Executive Director, is a Chartered Accountant, Chartered Management Accountant with over 20 years of experience in the field of taxation , and Principal at Gajma and Co., bringing strength in accounting, taxation and financial oversight."
