    "md5": "ec11c88ab88b163f69235e5bc7342924",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1983,
    "chunk_text": "Significant Court victory for Friends of Manipay Hospital in Ride For Ceylon dispute\n\nSri Lankan Commercial High Court rejects interim injunction application by former volunteer rider and awards costs to FOMH\n\nCourt recognises FOMH\u2019s longstanding charitable use of the Ride For Ceylon brand and considers earlier UK Intellectual Property Office decision in favour of charity\n\nFriends of Manipay Hospital (FOMH), a UK-registered charity supporting Green Memorial Hospital in Manipay, Sri Lanka, issuing a statement welcomed the order delivered by the Commercial High Court of Colombo on 7 October in Case No. CHC/014/2026/IP.\n\nIt said the Court rejected the applications for interim injunctions brought by a former volunteer rider against FOMH and other defendants, with an award of costs of Rs. 75,000.\n\n\u201cThe decision represents a significant development in FOMH\u2019s efforts to protect the Ride For Ceylon charitable fundraising initiative and its associated intellectual property interests,\u201d FOMH said.\n\nIn its judgement, the Court acknowledged that the Ride For Ceylon name and mark had been used for a considerable period in fundraising activities undertaken by FOMH in both the UK and Sri Lanka.\n\nThe Court considered the history of the charitable cycling initiative, the involvement of volunteers, the competing claims to the trademark, and the evidence presented by the parties.\n\nThe judgement also recorded that the plaintiff was a volunteer member of FOMH and had participated in charitable fundraising activities undertaken for the benefit of Green Memorial Hospital.\n\nThe Court concluded that the plaintiff had not established sufficient grounds to prevent the defendants from continuing to use the Ride For Ceylon name and mark by way of the interim injunctions sought until the final determination of the case.\n\nThe Sri Lankan Court\u2019s order also considered the earlier UK Intellectual Property Office (UK IPO) proceedings concerning the Ride For Ceylon trademark."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-09-dailyftlk-20c47fd5",
    "num": "dailyftlk-20c47fd5",
    "date_str": "2026-11-09",
    "description": "Significant Court victory for Friends of Manipay Hospital in Ride For Ceylon dispute",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/news/Significant-Court-victory-for-Friends-of-Manipay-Hospital-in-Ride-For-Ceylon-dispute/56-799816",
    "lang": "en",
