    "chunk_size_bytes": 1715,
    "chunk_text": "Journalism Awards for Excellence 2025: Lifetime Achievement Award winners\n\nAsoka Goonetilleke commenced his journalistic career in Lake House in 1976 and after serving on the Central News Desk and in the foreign news desk, he left in 1982. During this period, he also served on the Observer, feature write on the Yovun, Janatha and Editorial news reporter in Janatha newspaper. He joined Upali Newspapers in 1982 as the Sports Editor of the Divaina and rose to the position of Associate Editor when he left in 2013.\n\nHe has contributed articles to the FIFA and AFC football magazines, the Dawn (Bangladesh) and Calcutta Times (India). He has translated to Sinhala language from English language several books. Among them - An Adventurous Voyage to the Sea (Mahamuhuda Meda -Maranaya Abhiyasa), and The Black Dragon (Kalu Makara). He has also translated books from Sinhala language to English language - What Makes the Buddha Great, Impermanence in Plain English \u2013 both books were written by The Most Rev. Henepola Gunaratane.\n\nHe has been a lecturer and served in the National Olympic Committee of Sri Lanka, School of Sports Sciences (Sports Ministry) National Course Director - Sri Lanka and the International Olympic Committee. He has also worked at the Department of Govt. Information.\n\nGoonetilleke has also received several awards. Among them Sports Journalist of the year 2000 (Editors Guild of Sri Lanka), Olympic Award for Excellence in Sports Journalism 2024 (International Olympic Committee), Presidential Award 2015 for the most outstanding sports publication, Kreeda Sahithya Vedi (2020-Sabuddhi Sports Literary Awards) and Multi Literal Sports Literate Award (2022- Sabuddhi Sports Literary Awards)."
  },
