    "chunk_text": "The event also featured two panel discussions with panellists representing the media, ECSL, advocacy groups, and civil society. The first panel discussion, titled \u2018The Election Information Ecosystem,\u2019 discussed disinformation, accountability, and challenges to electoral integrity.\n\nThe second panel discussion, titled \u2018Resilience in Practice,\u2019 drew experiences from fact-checking, advocacy, and media literacy work. The discussion navigated challenges when it comes to verifying information, type of responses received from social media companies during the fact-checking processes, how local journalists have been capacitated to counter disinformation, and lack of interest towards funding fact-checking initiatives.\n\nClosing the event, DRI Project Manager Aingkaran Kugathasan thanked participants and partners for their contribution to the project.\n\nThe event was held as part of the \u2018Strengthening Resilience Against Disinformation in Sri Lanka\u2019 project, co-funded by the European Union, and brought together representatives from international partner organisations, stakeholder institutions, the media, and civil society groups.\n\nDRI and Factum produced eight research reports under the project. The reports are available at https://democracy-reporting.org/en/office/sri-lanka.\n\n66 accounts impersonated political parties and candidates on TikTok. 45.5% of accounts had been active during the 2024 Presidential Election and 21.2% of them remained active till the 2025 Local Council Election. In terms of action, following reports of these accounts made to TikTok and the ECSL, 51 of these accounts were removed"
