    "md5": "19839f75fe1dfa6a91b6793680c1c79d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1643,
    "chunk_text": "SENOK celebrates 47 years of enterprise, innovation and nation building\n\nSENOK is marking its 47th anniversary this year, celebrating nearly five decades of Sri Lankan enterprise and growth across industries that have played an important role in the country\u2019s development.\n\nFrom a travel company established in 1979, SENOK has grown into one of Sri Lanka\u2019s largest diversified privately owned business groups, today encompassing more than 40 companies with interests spanning construction and heavy machinery, automobiles and commercial vehicles, renewable energy, manufacturing and aviation, with operations extending beyond Sri Lanka into international markets.\n\nSENOK was founded in 1979 by Noel Selvanayagam with the establishment of Senok Travels Ltd. From its beginnings in the travel industry, the business soon expanded into construction machinery and began the diversification that would shape the Group over the decades that followed. As SENOK grew, Managing Director Gerard Fernando became a key force in its development, playing a central role in building and leading many of the Group\u2019s principal businesses, operations and major projects.\n\nConstruction and heavy machinery became one of the foundations of the Group\u2019s growth. Machinery supplied and supported by SENOK has been deployed across roads, irrigation schemes, hydropower projects, precast construction projects, harbours, airports and other major infrastructure throughout Sri Lanka. Today, SENOK represents internationally recognised brands including Kobelco, JCB, HAMM and Airman, supported by extensive sales, service, spare parts and technical capabilities."
  },
