    "md5": "b73a79badf78baceac6b4c64d0277855",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1768,
    "chunk_text": "Blue Yonder\u2019s cognitive solutions to power future of Sri Lankan retail\n\nHayleys PLC Chairman and Chief Executive Mohan Pandithage (second from right) and Blue Yonder Chief Revenue Officer Corey Tollefson with the strategic partnership agreement signed between two organisations. Hayleys Retail CEO Bruno Jousselin and Blue Yonder APAC President Antonio Boccalandro are also present\u00a0\u2013 Pic by Upul Abayasekara\n\nHayleys Retail Holdings Ltd., will launch and scale supermarket business on the Blue Yonder Platform\n\nHayleys Retail Holdings Ltd., last week announced that it has selected Blue Yonder to build its grocery retail operations from the ground up with AI and connected supply chain technology.\n\nHayleys Retail plans to open a number of stores in the near future to bring reliable service and greater convenience to consumers across Sri Lanka. The company is Blue Yonder\u2019s first retail customer in Sri Lanka.\n\nHayleys is Sri Lanka\u2019s number one ranked public listed company and a multinational conglomerate, accounting for approximately 5% of Sri Lanka\u2019s export income, with operations spanning 17 business sectors across five continents. Entering the large-scale supermarket sector and drawing on the Group\u2019s strengths in manufacturing, logistics and services, the company looked beyond the applications it would need on day one to how it wanted the business to operate at scale. Hayleys Retail selected Blue Yonder for three reasons: a unified data foundation that connects merchandising, replenishment and space decisions; AI agents that monitor operations, detect anomalies and recommend actions before problems cascade; and a cloud-native platform that can grow with the business from its first stores to a national network without re-platforming."
