    "chunk_text": "Hayleys is Sri Lanka\u2019s number one ranked public listed company and a multinational conglomerate, accounting for approximately 5% of Sri Lanka\u2019s export income, with operations spanning 17 business sectors across five continents. Entering the large-scale supermarket sector and drawing on the Group\u2019s strengths in manufacturing, logistics and services, the company looked beyond the applications it would need on day one to how it wanted the business to operate at scale. Hayleys Retail selected Blue Yonder for three reasons: a unified data foundation that connects merchandising, replenishment and space decisions; AI agents that monitor operations, detect anomalies and recommend actions before problems cascade; and a cloud-native platform that can grow with the business from its first stores to a national network without re-platforming.\n\nHayleys PLC Chairman and Chief Executive Mohan Pandithage said: \u201cService excellence has been at the heart of every Hayleys business for 148 years, and our entry into supermarket retail is about bringing that same commitment to quality and reliability closer to everyday Sri Lankan consumers. Digital transformation has been a key driver of how we create greater value across the Group, empowering our teams and enabling us to serve our customers better. Building a new retail business allows us to embed that approach from day one. With Blue Yonder, our teams will have AI-driven insight to deliver a seamless, consistent shopping experience across every store. This collaboration represents an important step in building a future-ready retail business.\u201d With Blue Yonder, Hayleys Retail will be able to:\n\nMake connected decisions across merchandising, inventory and the shelf from a single, AI-ready data foundation.\n\nAccurately forecast demand and rebalance inventory based on actual sales, local seasonality, changing market conditions and real-time constraints."
