    "chunk_text": "NASA is officially hiring people to live on the moon\n\nThe Guardian - Nasa has launched a callout for a new generation of astronauts as it searches for explorers who could live and work on the moon.\n\nOpening applications for the latest expansion of its Artemis program, the US agency said successful candidates would help \u201cshape humanity\u2019s future in space\u201d as it builds a base on the moon and plans the first crewed missions to Mars.\n\nThe news was announced on Saturday during a Kennedy Space Center air show promoting lunar exploration, as well as advances in aviation and technology.\n\n\u201cThis is an extraordinary time to join Nasa\u2019s astronaut corps,\u201d said Nasa administrator Jared Isaacman. \u201cThe people we select could walk on the Moon, live and work at the Moon Base, and help pioneer the systems and operations that will ultimately carry crews to Mars.\u201d\n\nNasa expects to make its final selection in late 2027 to begin training the next class of astronaut candidates. The agency last opened applications for new astronauts in 2024, ultimately accepting 10 new astronauts out of more than 8,000 applicants in September 2025.\n\n\u201cFor those who apply, becoming a Nasa astronaut is more than a career opportunity,\u201d said Scott Tingle, chief astronaut and chair of the Astronaut Selection Board at Nasa\u2019s Johnson Space Center in Houston. \u201cIt is a chance to join a legacy of explorers who have pushed the boundaries of discovery and play a role in the missions that will shape humanity\u2019s future in space.\u201d\n\nSince the 1960s, Nasa has selected 370 people to train as astronaut candidates for increasingly challenging missions. The agency currently has 32 astronauts active in the astronaut corps.\n\nIsaacman and other agency leaders recently laid out Nasa\u2019s ambitions to return Americans to the moon in 2028. Both SpaceX and Blue Origin intend to support a crewed lunar landing."
