    "md5": "22da25b612b00e1587813d71fb188434",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1617,
    "chunk_text": "He further emphasised that Port City Colombo is a project of national importance, operating under the direct purview of the Office of Sri Lanka\u2019s President,Anura Kumara Dissanayake, who also serves as the Minister of Finance, underscoring the Government\u2019s interest in the project.\n\nA panel discussion brought together Madhu Raghunath, CEO, TVS Vehicle Mobility Solutions and Co-Chairman of the CII SR Taskforce on International Business Development; Robin S, Senior Director and Head \u2013 Centre of Excellence, Strategic Consulting and Value & Risk Advisory, India & Sri Lanka, JLL;\u00a0 Amarasekera; and Thulci Aluwihare, Deputy Managing Director, CHEC Port City Colombo, to discuss sectoral opportunities, regulatory facilitation and prospects for business partnerships.\n\nRobin S., Senior Director, Head of Centre of Excellence, Strategic Consulting and Value and Risk Advisory, India and Sri Lanka, JLL, said: \u201cFor Indian businesses exploring opportunities beyond the domestic market, geographic proximity, ease of doing business and access to new growth markets are important considerations. A clear regulatory framework and transparent incentive framework give Port City Colombo the ingredients for serious interest from India, and the conversations thus far show that interest is building.\u201d\n\nThe Investor Forum in Chennai marks an important step in Port City Colombo\u2019s efforts to deepen engagement with the Indian business and investment community. Going forward, continued dialogue will be pursued to further potential cross-border partnerships and unlocking new avenues for investment and collaboration."
