    "chunk_size_bytes": 2007,
    "chunk_text": "Siyapatha Finance-Toyota enhance value-added services in vehicle leasing\n\nStrategic partnership aims to deliver flexible financing solutions, enhanced customer convenience and comprehensive vehicle ownership support\n\nSiyapatha Finance PLC has entered into a strategic partnership with Toyota Lanka (Private) Limited through the signing of a memorandum of understanding (MoU), marking a significant milestone in the companies\u2019 shared commitment to enhancing value-added services and elevating the vehicle leasing experience in Sri Lanka.\n\nThe partnership brings together Siyapatha Finance PLC\u2019s financial expertise and Toyota Lanka\u2019s automotive leadership to deliver accessible, convenient and flexible vehicle financing solutions, complemented by services designed to address the evolving needs and expectations of the leasing customers.\n\nThrough this collaboration, both organisations aim to create greater value for the customers by streamlining the leasing journey and strengthening support throughout the vehicle ownership lifecycle.\n\nThe MoU was formally signed by Siyapatha Finance Chief Operating Officer Rajeev De Silva and Chief Marketing Officer Hisham Ziard and Toyota Lanka Chairman Masaaki Kawabata and Managing Director and Chief Executive Officer Manohara Atukorala.\n\nThe signing ceremony was attended by the senior management teams of both organisations, reflecting their shared commitment to establishing a strong and enduring business relationship.\n\nUnder this strategic alliance, the customers can look forward to a more streamlined and convenient leasing experience, supported by flexible financing solutions, long-term leasing options, enhanced service delivery, comprehensive protection through trusted insurance partners and access to a range of reliable vehicles from a globally recognised automotive brand.\n\nThe collaboration aims to strengthen customer confidence by bringing financing and automotive services together through a more integrated and customer-focused approach."
  },
