    "md5": "e7a28124c0dc7e91dabba6ed424b1ab3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1860,
    "chunk_text": "Atlas Axillia-Nalanda College launch Tinkering Lab\n\nHigh Commissioner of India to Sri Lanka Santosh Jha and Hemas Holdings Group Chief Executive Officer Ashish Chandra unveil newly established Tinkering Lab at Nalanda Innovation Centre\n\nTo nurture Sri Lanka\u2019s next generation of innovators and entrepreneurs\n\nAtlas Axillia, the learning-focused subsidiary of Hemas Holdings PLC, recently partnered with Nalanda College to inaugurate the Tinkering Lab at the Nalanda Innovation Centre, marking a transformative step toward preparing Sri Lanka\u2019s youth for a technology-driven future.\n\nThe initiative is led by Atlas Axillia in partnership with Nalanda College, supported by technical expertise from India\u2019s Atal Innovation Mission - NITI Aayog and facilitated by the High Commission of India.\n\nHoused within the Nalanda College Centenary Building, the facility brings hands-on STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics) and arts learning directly into a school environment.\n\nBy integrating scientific concepts with creative exploration and entrepreneurship, the lab bridges textbook theory and practical application, offering the students a resource-rich space to experiment and develop real-world solutions through robotics, artificial intelligence (AI) and design thinking.\n\nHemas Holdings Group CEO Ashish Chandra said, \u201cTrue empowerment begins with giving our children the tools and confidence to shape their own futures.\u201d\n\nThe Nalanda Innovation Centre is designed to guide students through every stage of the innovation journey, from developing an initial idea to creating a prototype and presenting a finished concept. Its facilities include a DIY Innovation Lab, an advanced fabrication lab equipped for 3D printing and digital manufacturing and dedicated spaces for augmented and virtual reality, arts and agricultural technology."
