    "md5": "2ac38204f74d5525cbfbfb8bcf13d2c7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1036,
    "chunk_text": "Video of Israeli tourist pushing Sri Lankan guide into sea sparks outrage\n\nA video showing an Israeli tourist pushing a Sri Lankan tour guide off a boat and into the sea has gone viral on social media.\n\nThe footage, shared by Russian media outlet RT, shows a group of Israeli tourists travelling on a boat in Sri Lanka when one of them suddenly pushes the male tour guide into the water while he is drinking.\n\nThe incident has sparked anger online, with many questioning the behaviour of the tourists and their treatment of the local guide.\n\nIsraeli journalist and social activist Daniel Amram, who brought the video to public attention, later shared the tourists\u2019 explanation of the incident.\n\nAccording to Amram, the tourists claimed it was a joke and said the tour guide knew about the prank and was involved in it.\n\nThey also insisted that there was no intention to disrespect or humiliate the guide and that he was not injured.\n\n\u201cIt was a joke, the worker is fine, it wasn\u2019t meant to be mean,\u201d the tourists reportedly said."
