    "language": "en",
    "md5": "b61150ab3ed851ee83f9732877a998e2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1581,
    "chunk_text": "Hayleys Solar inaugurates Kosgama 5MW ground-mounted solar development\n\nCeremonial unveiling of Kosgama I (2MW) and Kosgama II (3MW) ground-mounted solar projects, marking another milestone in Hayleys Solar\u2019s planned 300MW ground-mounted solar portfolio\n\nHayleys Solar inaugurated two ground-mounted solar power projects in Kosgama.\n\nComprising Kosgama I (2MW) and Kosgama II (3MW), the projects represent the second phase of Hayleys Solar\u2019s planned 300MW ground-mounted solar portfolio.\n\nEquipped with 10,790 high-efficiency 640W solar panels, the installations are expected to generate approximately 9.9 million kWh of clean electricity annually, avoiding an estimated 6,930 tonnes of CO emissions each year.\n\nConventional machinery access was restricted across sections of the site, necessitating labour-intensive activities, including manual drilling and foundation preparation.\n\nThrough careful planning and site-specific engineering solutions, Hayleys Solar successfully executed the development while preserving the land\u2019s natural contours and the existing water drainage patterns.\n\nThe development forms part of the Hayleys group\u2019s broader commitment to purpose-led growth, guided by its Lifecode ESG framework.\n\nAs Sri Lanka works towards its target of 70 percent renewable electricity by 2030, Hayleys Solar is contributing utility-scale capacity to the national grid, building on its Veyangoda project under the planned 300MW ground-mounted portfolio.\n\nThe Hayleys group\u2019s own operations already source around 70 percent of their energy from renewable sources."
  },
