    "chunk_text": "As Sri Lanka works towards its target of 70 percent renewable electricity by 2030, Hayleys Solar is contributing utility-scale capacity to the national grid, building on its Veyangoda project under the planned 300MW ground-mounted portfolio.\n\nThe Hayleys group\u2019s own operations already source around 70 percent of their energy from renewable sources.\n\nBy promoting beekeeping and supporting pollinator conservation, the initiative demonstrates our commitment to delivering renewable energy projects that generate lasting environmental and social value.\u201d\n\nHayleys Fentons Deputy Managing Director Energy Roshane Perera added, \u201cUnlike conventional ground-mounted installations, the Kosgama projects demanded a highly customised engineering approach. From manual foundation works to adapting installation methods to the site\u2019s natural topography, our teams overcame considerable technical challenges without altering the existing natural drainage patterns.\u201d"
