    "chunk_size_bytes": 1772,
    "chunk_text": "Cargills 2Q profit up 8.4% as group lines up new leadership\n\nCargills (Ceylon) PLC\u2019s profit rose by 8.4 percent to Rs.3.0 billion in the September quarter on revenue of Rs.76.3 billion, as the Group appointed senior executives from within to lead its Retail, Dairy and F&B sectors and Group Finance from January 2027, according to the company.\n\nGroup revenue increased by 16.2 percent year-on-year, supported by strong growth across its Retail, FMCG and Restaurants businesses, while EBITDA grew by 13.9 percent to Rs.7.6 billion despite pressure on operating costs from higher energy and input prices. Earnings per share improved to Rs.11.80 from Rs.10.83 a year earlier. Over the six months to 30 September, revenue grew by 15.2 percent to Rs.152.4 billion and profit by 10.4 percent to Rs.5.6 billion.\n\nThe FMCG sector was the Group\u2019s largest contributor to operating profit in the quarter, accounting for nearly half the total while bringing in about 23 percent of revenue. Sector revenue grew by 20.4 percent, driven primarily by volume expansion across the general trade, modern trade and food service channels. Operating profit rose by 27.4 percent to Rs.2.6 billion, aided by a favourable product mix and ongoing cost optimisation. For the six months, FMCG also overtook Retail in operating profit, reversing the position of a year earlier.\n\nThe Retail sector\u2019s revenue increased by 14.7 percent, supported by same-store sales growth of 13.2 percent on the back of higher customer footfall, while operating profit rose by 8.5 percent to Rs.2.2 billion. Cargills Food City added four stores during the quarter, taking its nationwide footprint to 564 stores. Selected large-format stores will also be repositioned to offer a wider assortment and more services."
  },
