    "chunk_text": "The Retail sector\u2019s revenue increased by 14.7 percent, supported by same-store sales growth of 13.2 percent on the back of higher customer footfall, while operating profit rose by 8.5 percent to Rs.2.2 billion. Cargills Food City added four stores during the quarter, taking its nationwide footprint to 564 stores. Selected large-format stores will also be repositioned to offer a wider assortment and more services.\n\nCargills attributed the performance to resilient consumer demand and its focus on growing volumes, strengthening operational capabilities and delivering value to consumers amid a challenging cost environment.\n\nThe company described the appointments as part of its long-term succession planning as it positions itself for its next phase of growth. It noted that the executives taking on the new roles have built substantial careers within the Group and bring extensive operating experience, institutional knowledge and a deep understanding of its businesses, values and purpose.\n\nLooking ahead, Cargills remains optimistic about Sri Lanka\u2019s medium-term economic prospects while staying mindful of global volatility. The Group has committed to investing in modernising its retail and food service networks, developing agricultural and dairy sourcing, expanding manufacturing capacity and strengthening its distribution, cold chain and logistics infrastructure, alongside digital transformation and talent development. Capital expenditure on property, plant and equipment rose by 83 percent to Rs.4.7 billion in the first half, from Rs.2.6 billion a year earlier."
