    "chunk_size_bytes": 1911,
    "chunk_text": "First Wendy\u2019s outlet to open by month-end\n\nJohn Keells Holdings (JKH) will open Sri Lanka\u2019s first Wendy\u2019s outlet by the end of this month, slightly ahead of the December timeline it flagged in July, with a second restaurant following in January and a longer-term target of 8 to 10 new outlets a year, the conglomerate\u2019s top management said.\n\nSpeaking at the group\u2019s investor webinar last week, JKH Deputy Chairperson and Group Finance Director Gihan Cooray noted that the first outlet was due to open within a couple of weeks, with a pipeline of further restaurants to follow.\n\n\u201cWe\u2019ll definitely look to open two outlets before the end of this financial year or maybe a third, and we\u2019re largely on track to do that,\u201d Cooray remarked.\n\nJKH\u2019s interim financial statements for the September quarter, filed with the Colombo Stock Exchange, place the second opening in January 2027 and state that operational and marketing preparations for the launch are progressing well. Cooray also confirmed that the franchise carries a minimum outlet requirement, although he did not disclose the number.\n\n\u201cYes, there is a minimum number of outlets that we have to open, but that\u2019s over a five-year period where there are certain commitments and we are quite confident that that can be achieved,\u201d he added.\n\nJKH expects the rollout to gather pace after the launch phase. At its first-quarter webinar in July, management said the business could open \u201cabout eight to 10 stores annually. Maybe more,\u201d banking on growth in the quick service restaurant (QSR) segment as disposable incomes and consumption pick up.\n\nThe restaurants will be operated by John Keells Restaurants (Private) Limited, a wholly owned subsidiary incorporated in 2025. JKH has described the equity investment in the business as not material, with future expansion to be funded through a mix of debt and internally generated funds."
