    "chunk_size_bytes": 707,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cSo the path is no longer detection, it is interception in real time,\u201d he noted.\n\nHe identified deepfake onboarding and card testing by bots as the most common forms of attack at present, adding that global card fraud is projected to reach US$ 40 billion by 2027.\n\nHellwig claimed that banks using AI-based defences have improved real-time detection by 20 percent and cut false positives by 95 percent. He added that AI-assisted investigations can reduce both the time taken and the US$ 6.3 million average cost of a breach. He cautioned, though, that AI agents used for defence also need to be properly governed.\n\n\u201cThere is no other means than to defend AI attacks with AI,\u201d Hellwig concluded. (NF)"
