    "chunk_text": "\u201cIf not for the CWIT capacity inducted this year, the Port of Colombo would have witnessed a negative growth,\u201d Sri Lanka Ports Authority (SLPA) Chairman Dr. Parakrama Dissanayake remarked at the launch of CWIT\u2019s second phase in late September.\n\n\u201cIt is something that we would strongly encourage the government to do because we believe the demand will be there and the sooner we can get capacity on stream, the Port of Colombo and Sri Lanka won\u2019t lose out,\u201d Balendra urged.\n\nJKH\u2019s annual report notes that West Container Terminal 2 and the first container terminal at the Colombo North Port are planned to be operational by 2030 and 2034, respectively. Speaking at an investment summit in October, President Anura Kumara Dissanayake indicated that the breakwater required for West Container Terminal 2 was now estimated at about US$ 1.4 billion, with the Asian Development Bank\u2019s feasibility study due by April 2027."
