    "chunk_size_bytes": 701,
    "chunk_text": "Rupee weakens slightly against US Dollar\n\nColombo, Nov.9 (Daily Mirror) - The Sri Lankan Rupee has depreciated slightly against the US Dollar today (09), compared to last Friday, according to the Central Bank of Sri Lanka.\n\nThe Central Bank's daily exchange rates show that the US Dollar's buying rate has increased from Rs. 328.05 to Rs. 328.09, while the selling rate has risen from Rs. 337.00 to Rs. 337.05.\n\nAt Commercial Bank, the buying rate increased from Rs. 326.38 to Rs. 326.58, while its selling rate has risen from Rs. 336.30 to Rs. 336.50.\n\nAt People\u2019s Bank, the buying rate has increased from Rs. 328.35 to Rs. 328.48, while the selling rate has moved up from Rs. 336.49 to Rs. 336.59."
