    "chunk_size_bytes": 1914,
    "chunk_text": "Dr. Janey Lowes, British veterinarian and founder of WECare Worldwide completed an extraordinary 621km run across the island titled \u2018Dog Jog\u2019. The goal is to raise \u00a31.6 million to build a fully furbished animal hospital with modern facilities. Dr. Lowes from Barnard Castle, County Durham gave up her life in UK to care for injured street animals in Sri Lanka. In 2014, she founded WeCare Worldwide, a UK charity with the support from Westway Veterinary Group to provide veterinary care for the estimated three million street dogs in Sri Lanka as well as many street cats. During her jog, Dr. Lowes rescued several injured street dogs including Sarnie and Petal which made her realise the importance of this initiative.\u00a0 In a candid interview with the Daily Mirror, Dr. Lowes shared her experience jogging across a country like Sri Lanka, her encounter with Sarnie, the goal of her fundraising campaign, activities carried out by the WECare Animal Hospital and why people shouldn\u2019t frown at stray animals. Excerpts :\n\nQ How challenging or fun has it been to jog around a tropical country like Sri Lanka ?\n\nI found Sarnie by chance on day five of my Dog Jog (October 13) as I had to change my route at the last minute due to reports of elephant attacks in the area. She didn\u2019t move as my support tuk drove past her, which was a huge red flag, and that\u2019s when I realised she was paralysed and couldn\u2019t use her back legs. She was super skinny and I knew if we left her there, she would end up starving to death by the side of the road. So we asked around if anyone knew her (they didn\u2019t) and took her with us. We were really far from the hospital at this stage. So we snuck Sarnie into our hotels for a few nights before managing to get her down to the WECare hospital for treatment. The X-rays showed that she had an old spinal fracture and an old femoral fracture as well as issues with her bladder."
