    "chunk_size_bytes": 1776,
    "chunk_text": "I still can\u2019t quite believe that I managed to complete this run. While I\u2019m so proud of myself and incredibly thankful for all the amazing people who supported me, we still have a long way to go to reach our \u00a31.5 million (LKR 671,270,850) fundraising goal. We\u2019ve raised \u00a3260,000 (LKR 116,353,614) so far, which is incredible. But we need a lot more. So please continue to share, donate and support to give these street animals the hospital they not only need, but deserve.\n\nOn day 15 (October 24) in the Hill Country, we had a bit of a fright only an hour into the day\u2019s run when an electricity pylon almost fell on me!! A bus drove past and hit the power line, pulling the pylon over right in front of me; it was pretty scary how close we were to disaster! Thankfully, everybody was ok, but we were a bit shaken.\n\nTwo days before the end of my run (October 30) we came across Petal, a seriously ill puppy who\u2019d been hit by a car two weeks prior, so we transferred her down to the WECare hospital. Petal is now recovering after emergency surgery to repair a life-threatening diaphragmatic hernia (the impact of the accident had pushed her abdominal organs into her chest cavity!). The team stayed all night on Friday to look after her as she crashed after surgery- she\u2019s now doing so much better, but isn\u2019t out of the woods yet. We\u2019re doing everything we can to get her back on her feet!\n\nOur current hospital is in Gandara in the south of Sri Lanka and is the only fully-equipped vet hospital on the island that\u2019s dedicated to street dogs (and cats!). We have 27 permanent kennels for inpatients (plus many pop-up kennels), X-ray, ultrasound machines, an in-house laboratory, isolation facilities (for potentially infectious animals), and a surgical suite."
