    "md5": "e26c1cade8149b13d304860b81ca54d1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1144,
    "chunk_text": "What the 2026 US Midterm Elections mean for Sri Lanka\u2019s Economic Recovery\n\nThe American people have voted. Washington\u2019s political balance has changed. But thousands of miles away, Sri Lanka faces a far more pressing question. Could the outcome of an American election determine the future of our exports, industrial employment, foreign-exchange earnings and economic recovery?\n\nThe answer is that American political decisions can significantly influence all four.\n\nThe November 3, 2026, midterm elections delivered Democratic control of both chambers of Congress, confronting President Donald Trump with a substantially altered political landscape.\n\nFor Sri Lanka, still recovering from its worst economic crisis, this is not merely an American political development. It is an economic warning.\n\nWhen nearly one-quarter of a country\u2019s merchandise exports depend on a single foreign market, political uncertainty in that market becomes a national economic vulnerability.\n\nSri Lanka must therefore look beyond the electoral headlines and confront the economic realities.\n\nGLOBAL MARKETS SHAKEN \u2014 A WARNING AND AN OPPORTUNITY FOR SRI LANKA"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-09-dailymirrorlk-ca1a10f3",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-ca1a10f3",
    "date_str": "2026-11-09",
    "description": "What the 2026 US Midterm Elections mean for Sri Lanka\u2019s Economic Recovery",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/breaking-news/What-the-2026-US-Midterm-Elections-mean-for-Sri-Lankas-Economic-Recovery/108-354497",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1794213675.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-09-dailymirrorlk-ca1a10f3-0001",
