    "md5": "9bb8ccf694744c13924628382329d193",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1672,
    "chunk_text": "Colombo - A city that should not drown\n\nColombo, Nov.9 (Daily Mirror) - Colombo\u2019s roads turned into rivers on Friday evening, residential neighbourhoods were submerged, sewage systems overflowed and thousands of commuters were left stranded after 129mm of rain fell within just two hours. What should have been a routine evening in the commercial capital turned into a nightmare for residents, exposing once again the glaring weaknesses in the city\u2019s drainage infrastructure and the failure of those entrusted with maintaining it.\n\nWhile heavy rainfall is certainly beyond the control of municipal authorities, the failure to prepare for increasingly unpredictable weather is not. Flooding is no longer an occasional inconvenience that cities can afford to address only after disaster strikes. It is a growing urban challenge, particularly in countries such as Sri Lanka, which are increasingly vulnerable to climate change.\n\nWhat is particularly disappointing is the response from Colombo Mayor Vraie Cally Balthazaar, who explained that the city\u2019s drainage system was designed to accommodate approximately 30mm of rainfall, whereas Colombo received 129mm within a few hours. While the explanation may be technically correct, is this really an acceptable excuse from someone entrusted with governing the country\u2019s commercial capital?\n\nIf Colombo\u2019s drainage infrastructure can only withstand 30mm to 50mm of rainfall, then surely the question should be why successive municipal administrations have failed to improve this capacity. More importantly, what has the present administration done during its months in office to address these longstanding shortcomings?"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-09-dailymirrorlk-dc647e31",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-dc647e31",
    "date_str": "2026-11-09",
    "description": "Colombo - A city that should not drown",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/breaking-news/Colombo-A-city-that-should-not-drown/108-354502",
