    "md5": "7916c13c9d1345f0bdab8f51c5ab9783",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1181,
    "chunk_text": "Technology must play a greater role too. Real-time rainfall monitoring, flood-risk mapping and early warning systems could help authorities identify vulnerable neighbourhoods and respond before roads become impassable.\n\nThe establishment of a special task force following Friday\u2019s floods is welcome, but committees and meetings cannot substitute for actual work on the ground.\n\nColombo is the country\u2019s commercial heart. It attracts investors, tourists, businesses and thousands of daily commuters. A capital city that cannot manage heavy rainfall risks damaging not only its residents\u2019 confidence but also its reputation as a place to do business.\n\nThe Mayor must understand that leadership is not about explaining why a city floods after the damage is done. It is about anticipating problems, investing in solutions and ensuring that public institutions perform the responsibilities entrusted to them.\n\nClimate change may be beyond our control, but poor planning, neglected infrastructure and administrative complacency are not. Colombo cannot afford another rainy evening that leaves its residents swimming through their own streets. The city deserves better than excuses."
