    "chunk_text": "\u201cGovernement representatives describe the leasing programme as national policy. Then explain how that policy honours your own declaration. Secure housing land with legal deeds and livelihood land for our youth before signing commercial agreements,\u201d he said.\n\nHe stressed that the TPA welcomed private investment and economic development, but insisted that these must proceed after the community\u2019s promised land rights were secured.\n\nCiting the World Bank\u2019s October assessment, he noted that only about 8% of the Rs. 500 billion national reconstruction allocation had been spent by mid-2026.\n\n\u201cBudget allocations and media spectacles cannot shelter a family from a landslide. People need land, completed homes and livelihoods,\u201d he said.\n\nArullsamy recalled that the TPA, under Leader Mano Ganesan MP, supported the previous Budget\u2019s Second Reading in good faith. He said Ganesan had written to President Dissanayake the previous week and tabled his ten-point letter in Parliament, seeking gazetted wage protections, land rights, equitable development and the repeal of the PTA without similarly restrictive replacements.\n\n\u201cThe Government can find a Cabinet route for investors and draft new powers under proposals such as the PSTA, yet a plantation worker\u2019s land deed apparently requires a miracle. Is this the promised transformation, new powers to suppress minority voices, old excuses for landlessness? Hold the leasing decision. Honour Hatton Declaration first. Give our people housing and livelihood land, then bring forward investment proposals. We will support development that delivers on those promises, why we are demanding land rights, because we have proved that we can during our tenure\u201d he said."
