    "chunk_text": "Bring employers inside the tent. Employer reputation is worth 20% of the QS Asia score. Chambers of commerce, export associations and large employers should formalise partnerships with universities on curricula, internships and joint research.\n\nLet the best rise faster. Moratuwa\u2019s progress shows what focus can achieve. Give a handful of universities more autonomy over hiring, admissions and partnerships, in return for clear performance targets.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s universities have long performed below what our income, literacy and history would predict. The 2027 rankings show that the gap is not closing; it is widening. Countries that were poorer than us a decade ago, and some that still are, now have universities that the world takes seriously. Ours are slipping further down the table each year, not because our academics are less able, but because the system around them has stood still while the rest of Asia has moved.\n\nFor a country that hopes to sell services, attract investment and keep its talented young people at home that is not an academic concern. It is an economic one. The great fall can still be reversed \u2013 but only if we stop treating the rankings as somebody else\u2019s problem.\n\n(The author is a policy researcher cum academic. Ai tools including Claude.ai, Perplexity AI and Grok.com have been used in the compilation of the article. The author has validated the facts and takes full responsibility. The ideas expressed are personal. The author can be reached at [email\u00a0protected].)"
