    "chunk_size_bytes": 1846,
    "chunk_text": "Initial work is being carried out at Kirimandala Mawatha in Narahenpita, Haig Road in Bambalapitiya, Collingwood Place and Parakum Road in Wellawatte, the Cooray Urban Housing Scheme, Stafford Road in Kirulapone and the adjoining canal.\n\nOther locations identified for intervention include Heen Ela near Baseline Road, Aramaya Road in Dematagoda, the New Bazaar area in Central Colombo, De Mel Watta and Paradise Road.\n\nAuthorities said the program would go beyond clearing immediate blockages to address longstanding drainage deficiencies through repairs, regular maintenance and improved coordination among State institutions.\n\nDeputy Minister of Public Security and Parliamentary Affairs Sunil Watagala, Colombo District MP, also attended the field operations, alongside CMC Deputy Mayor Hemantha Weerakoon, local government representatives, officials and residents.\n\nThe November 6 flooding affected several areas, including Pettah, Dematagoda, Orugodawatte, Kollupitiya, Bambalapitiya and Kompanna Veediya.\n\nAuthorities have identified poor drainage maintenance, unauthorised construction and land reclamation, unplanned urban development, the dumping of waste into canals and drainage networks, and inadequate institutional coordination as contributing factors.\n\nThe Government intends to establish a coordinated mechanism for the maintenance, rehabilitation and monitoring of drainage infrastructure, replacing the fragmented approach under which individual institutions have operated separately. The initiative is intended to provide immediate relief while establishing a longer-term framework to reduce Colombo\u2019s exposure to flash floods.\n\nOpposition MP S.M. Marikkar, meanwhile, called for Mayor Balthazar\u2019s resignation or removal, accusing the CMC of failing to clean drains and culverts despite advance warnings of heavy rainfall."
