    "chunk_size_bytes": 1872,
    "chunk_text": "WCIC IGNITE 2026 empowers 100 young women toead Sri Lanka\u2019s next wave of entrepreneurship\n\nThe Women\u2019s Chamber of Industry and Commerce (WCIC) successfully concluded IGNITE 2026, its flagship youth entrepreneurship initiative, bringing together 100 female university undergraduates from 17 universities across Sri Lanka for a transformative day of learning, inspiration and practical business exposure at The Kingsbury, Colombo on the 31\u00a0 October 2026.\n\nNow in its second year, IGNITE has rapidly established itself as a premier platform for nurturing the next generation of women entrepreneurs. The program was designed to equip young women with the confidence, skills and entrepreneurial mind set required to transform innovative ideas into successful ventures.\n\nParticipants engaged in a dynamic program featuring interactive workshops, business idea development sessions, entrepreneur-led discussions and networking opportunities. The event provided valuable exposure to entrepreneurship, financial literacy, leadership and innovation through real-world experiences shared by successful business leaders and founders.\n\nSpeech-Language Pathologist and Founder/CEO of Ceylon Speechie Nadini Perera, conducted an engaging and interactive workshop titled \u201cBuild a Business That Fits Your Life and Can Reach the World\u201d.\n\nA highlight of the event was the inspiring stories shared by young Sri Lankan entrepreneurs, Spice Carriage (Lactoboost) Founder Lasni Silva, Blue Fish Ceylon Ltd., Founder/Director Bhagya Sandakelum, and Sleepyheads SL Founder Shehara Ferdinandis, who candidly discussed their journeys, challenges and successes, demonstrating that ambition, resilience and innovation can turn ideas into thriving enterprises.\n\nWCIC Board Member Zahara Ansary conducted an interactive session, guiding students in developing and refining their business ideas."
  },
