    "chunk_size_bytes": 1801,
    "chunk_text": "India\u2013Sri Lanka economic ties spotlights inaugural Colombo Port City Investor Forum in India\n\nOver 200 participants convened to advance investment dialogue across key sectors\n\nBuilding on the longstanding economic relationship between India and Sri Lanka, the Colombo Port City Investor Forum, held at the Hyatt Regency, Chennai, on 4 November, explored new avenues for investment, enterprise and cross-border business partnerships.\n\nHosted by the Deputy High Commission of Sri Lanka in Chennai, in collaboration with Port City Colombo (PCC), the forum brought together over 200 participants, including business leaders from the real estate, financial services, logistics, IT and technology sectors, representatives of leading Indian industry chambers, investors and policymakers, to explore how closer commercial engagement can create opportunities for businesses in both countries. The invitation-only forum marked Port City Colombo\u2019s first investor forum in India, underscoring its commitment to deepening engagement with the Indian business and investment community and translating longstanding bilateral economic ties into tangible business opportunities.\n\nThe program opened with an address by Deputy High Commissioner of Sri Lanka for Southern India Dr. Ganesanathan Geathiswaran. \u201cIndia and Sri Lanka are bound by geography, history and commerce, and that relationship is stronger than ever. There is considerable scope to deepen these ties through greater business engagement and investment. Chennai, with its strong industrial base and entrepreneurial ecosystem, is an important market for this conversation. We hope the forum will help build lasting partnerships between businesses in our two countries and translate shared opportunities into meaningful economic outcomes,\u201d he said."
  },
