    "chunk_text": "A useful Budget should also distinguish clearly between measures that provide immediate relief and reforms whose benefits will emerge over several years. People can accept difficult choices more readily when the government explains the purpose, likely timing and costs of its decisions. This requires honest communication and consistent follow-through, not merely ambitious language on Budget day.\n\nThese goals demand a more productive and export-oriented economy, responsible fiscal management, investor confidence and public administration that combines integrity with the ability to act.\n\nThe 2027 Budget should mark a shift from promises to implementation, from allocations to outcomes, and from short-term relief to lasting prosperity.\n\nThis is not simply a matter of political criticism. It is a constructive test of economic leadership. Ultimately, the success of a national Budget should be measured not by the promises made in Parliament, but by the improvements people experience in their everyday lives."
